6 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja Press Release July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Press Release June 30, 2026 NDIC Highlights Expanded Deposit Protection and Accelerated Reimbursement Systems Press Release June 22, 2026 NDIC and Federal High Court Strengthen Partnership for Efficient Justice and Financial System Protection Press Release May 29, 2026 NDIC and NCGC Partner to Strengthen Banking System Resilience Through Unified Risk Management Press Release May 25, 2026 NDIC Reiterates Commitment to Enhance Financial System Stability Press Release May 21, 2026 Youth Leadership: NDIC, NILE University host immersion challenge for business school students Press Release May 11, 2026 NDIC, CDIC Taiwan Benchmark Deposit Insurance Experience Press Release April 7, 2026 NDIC Provides Educational Platform for Students on Financial System Stability Press Release April 2, 2026 NDIC Hosts Deposit Protection Fund Uganda on Strategic Study Visit Program Press Release April 2, 2026 NDIC Celebrates Women's Empowerment at International Women's Day 2026 Observance Press Release February 27, 2026 House Commends NDIC On Efficient Budget Implementation", "content_hash": "b19e273a13bced57eca6a489bf65ca5b67248e5b7199a31740671319082aa8bb", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:25.250768+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1362", "title": "Everything You Need to Know About Colon Cancer (Colorectal Cancer)", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/colon-cancer", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/colon-cancer", "text": "Key takeaways Colon cancer occurs when cells in your large intestine grow out of control. Treatment can vary by the stage and type of colon cancer, but may include changes in bowel movements. You might not experience colon cancer symptoms at all, especially in the early stages. However, regular screening could help with early detection. The exact causes of colon cancer are still unknown, but genetics and lifestyle factors may increase your risk of developing it. Colon cancer is a type of cancer that starts in your colon (large intestine). It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s often referred to as colorectal cancer. However, colorectal cancer is a group of cancers that includes both colon cancer and rectal cancer, which begins in the rectum. According to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), colorectal cancer is the fourth most common type of cancer in the United States. The American Cancer Society (ACS) estimates that about 1 in 24 males and 1 in 26 females will develop colorectal cancer during their lifetime.Approximately 7 in 10 cases of colorectal cancers begin in the colon. Learn more about colon cancer stages, causes, and risk factors \u00e2\u0080\u0094 plus resources to help you find support. Are there different types of colon cancer?There are several types of colon cancer. They vary based on the different types of cancerous cells and where they\u00e2\u0080\u0099re located in the digestive tract.The most common type of colon cancer starts from adenocarcinomas, according to the ACS. Adenocarcinomas in colon cancer form within the cells that make mucus in either the colon or rectum.Less commonly, colon cancers are caused by other types of tumors, such as:lymphomascarcinoidssarcomasgastrointestinal stromal tumorsStages of colon cancerDoctors use staging as a general guideline to help them determine how far along the cancer is. This could help them develop the best treatment plan and better predict your long-term outlook. Stage 0 colon cancer is the earliest stage, and stage 4 is the most advanced stage. Here\u00e2\u0080\u0099s how the stages are defined:Stage 0: Also known as carcinoma in situ, this stage involves abnormal cells that are only in the inner lining of the colon.Stage 1: The cancer has penetrated the lining, or mucosa, of the colon and may have grown into the muscle layer. It hasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t spread to nearby lymph nodes or other parts of the body.Stage 2: The cancer has spread to the walls of the colon or through the walls to nearby tissues but hasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t affected the lymph nodes.Stage 3: The cancer has moved to the lymph nodes but not to other parts of the body.Stage 4: The cancer has spread to other distant organs, such as the liver or lungs.Learn more about the stages of colon cancer. What are the symptoms of colon cancer?You might not experience colon cancer symptoms at all, especially in the early stages. If you do experience symptoms of colon cancer, they may include: constipationdiarrheablood in the stoolchanges in stool colorchanges in stool shape, such as narrowed stoolbleeding from the rectumunintentional weight lossabdominal painexcessive fatiguethe feeling that your bowel won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t completely empty (tenesmus)It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that many of these symptoms may also be caused by other less serious conditions.As such, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a good idea to see a doctor if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve had any of these symptoms for 3 weeks or more. You and the doctor can discuss your symptoms and decide if colon cancer screening is appropriate.Learn more about the symptoms of colon cancer.How is colon cancer diagnosed?An early diagnosis of colon cancer gives you the best chance of curing it. Since colon cancer often has no symptoms during the early stages, it is usually caught during routine screenings like colonoscopy.The U.S. Preventive Service Task Force (USPSTF) and the ACS recommend starting colon cancer screening at age 45.A doctor will start by getting information about your medical and family history. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll also perform a physical exam. They may press on your abdomen or perform a rectal exam to determine whether lumps or polyps are present.A variety of other tests are recommended at different yearly intervals for the screening of colon cancer, including:Fecal tests: Guaiac-based fecal occult blood test (gFOBT) and fecal immunochemical test (FIT) are recommended every year.Sigmoidoscopy: every 5 yearsVirtual colonoscopy: every 5 yearsColonoscopy: every 10 yearsThe Shield Blood Test by Guardant Health was approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in July 2024 for the screening of colorectal cancer.A healthcare professional may recommend more frequent screening if you have a higher risk of developing colon cancer. Learn more about the tests used for colon cancer detection and diagnosis. Products to trySome at-home tests may also be used to help detect blood in the stool, an important symptom of colon cancer. These may include:LetsGetChecked Colon Cancer Screening TestEverlywell FIT Colon Cancer Screening TestSecond Generation FIT (Fecal Immunochemical Test)Shop for them online and learn more about the pros and cons of at-home tests.What are the treatment options for colon cancer?Treatment for colon cancer will depend on several factors, such as the stage and type of cancer and whether it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s spread to other parts of your body.In stages 0, 1, and 2 of colon cancer, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s often possible for a surgeon to remove cancerous polyps through surgery. The smaller and more contained the polyp is, the better the outlook.If your cancer has metastasized, you may require other types of treatment, such as:colostomychemotherapyablation therapytargeted therapyimmunotherapyLearn more about the treatment options for colon cancer. What causes colon cancer?The exact causes of colon cancer are still unknown, but researchers have identified several factors that may increase your risk of developing colon cancer. GeneticsColon cancer may be caused by genetic mutations that can either be inherited or acquired. These mutations don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t guarantee you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll develop colon cancer, but they do increase your chances.Some genetic conditions associated with colon cancer include:familial adenomatous polyposis (FAP)Gardner\u00e2\u0080\u0099s syndromeLynch syndromecystic fibrosisSome mutations may cause abnormal cells to accumulate in the colon lining, forming polyps. These are small, benign growths. However, untreated polyps can become cancerous. Removing these growths through surgery can be a preventive measure.Learn more about the association between genetics and colon cancer. Risk factors you can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t changeSome factors that increase your risk of developing colon cancer can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t be changed. For instance, your age, ethnicity, and family health history can all impact your risk of colon cancer. Risk factors you can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t control include:being over age 50a prior history of colon polypsa prior history of bowel diseasesa family history of colorectal cancerhaving certain genetic syndromes, such as FAPhaving certain health conditions, such as inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)having certain medical procedures, such as abdominal radiation and gallbladder removalbeing of Ashkenazi Jewish descentIn the United States, the highest rates of colon cancer are among American Indians, Alaska Natives, and Black people. One reason for these higher rates may be due to inequities in healthcare. Learn more about the causes and risk factors of colon cancer. Can colon cancer be prevented?Certain risk factors for colon cancer, such as family history and age, aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t preventable.However, certain lifestyle factors that may contribute to colon cancer are preventable, and changing them might help lower your overall risk of developing this disease.You can reduce your risk by:avoiding processed foods, such as hot dogs and deli meatseating more plant-based foodsdecreasing dietary fat and red meatexercising dailymaintaining a moderate weight, especially if you have obesity or overweightquitting smoking, if you smokereducing alcohol consumption, if you drinkdecreasing stressmanaging diabetesGetting a colonoscopy or other cancer screenings when you turn 45 years old could help detect colon cancer. This is important, as early diagnosis and treatment could help prevent further complications.What is the life expectancy for colon cancer?It can be alarming and stressful to receive a diagnosis like colon cancer. Colon cancer is treatable, especially when detected early.The life expectancy for colon cancer is provided as a 5-year life expectancy. This compares how likely a person with colon cancer is to be alive 5 years after receiving their diagnosis compared to people without colon cancer. Below are the 5-year relative survival rates for colorectal cancer provided by the ACS:Colon cancer stage at diagnosisRelative survival rateStage 0 and stage 191%Stage 2 and stage 373%Stage 413%Overall 63%It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that survival rates are continuing to increase as new cancer treatments are being developed. That said, the ACS notes that colorectal cancer cases have risen by 2.4% per year among people under 50 between 2012 and 2021.How can I get support for colon cancer?No matter what happens on your treatment journey, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need support along the way. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to talk with your medical team and loved ones and to feel comfortable reaching out for help. Here are some resources to start building a support system:The Colorectal Cancer Alliance Helpline (877-422-2030) is a free service that can connect you to resources and peer support.The Colorectal Cancer support group live chatmeets every weekday between 12 pm and 1 pm EST. Blue Hope Nation is a supportive Facebook group for colon cancer patients and family members.CancerCare offers a Colorectal Cancer Patient Support Group led by an oncology social worker. Fight Colorectal Cancer offers a resource library for people with colon cancer including videos, podcasts, and more to support you through treatment and beyond.Frequently asked questionsCan colon cancer be cured?If colon cancer is diagnosed in the early stages, surgery may be able to completely remove the cancerous polyp. Does colon cancer spread fast?The progression of colon cancer varies for each person. However, the ACS notes that colon cancer usually takes years to develop and spread. Early detection and treatment are key to preventing further spreading and complications. How bad is stage 1 colon cancer?Many people don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t experience symptoms of colon cancer during stage 1. However, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible to experience changes in your bowel habits, rectal bleeding, fatigue, and unexplained weight loss. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to see a doctor if you experience these symptoms. TakeawayColon cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the colon. In the early stages, you may not experience any symptoms of colon cancer, which makes it hard to diagnose. However, regular screening could help catch colon cancer early, leading to prompt treatment to reduce complications.Read this article in Spanish.", "content_hash": "9cfe125f492afbe292cc9c9a8e0280ce33b1f2ef4e65b95ae96e17b1de2b62d2", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:27.697425+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1363", "title": "All About Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA)", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/botox", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/botox", "text": "Botox (onabotulinumtoxinA) is a prescription drug that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used to treat a variety of medical conditions. Botox comes as a powder that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s mixed with liquid to form a solution, which is injected.Botox is used for medical purposes in adults and some children. Some of its uses include:helping prevent migraine episodes due to chronic migrainetreating neck muscle spasmstreating excessive sweating in the armpitstreating crossed or misaligned eyestreating overactive bladdertreating loss of bladder control that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s caused by a nerve disorderTo learn more, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWhat is Botox used for?\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Botox basicsThe active ingredient in Botox is called onabotulinumtoxinA, which is a biologic medication. A biologic is made from parts of living organisms. Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s active ingredient is not available in a biosimilar form. (Biosimilars are like generic drugs. But unlike generics, which are made for nonbiologic drugs, biosimilars are made for biologic drugs.)Note: This article discusses Botox, which is used for medical purposes. It does not cover Botox Cosmetic, the version of Botox that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used for cosmetic reasons.What is Botox used for?If you have certain conditions, your doctor may recommend Botox. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used for:helping prevent migraine episodes in adults with chronic migrainetreating excessive eye blinking that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s related to involuntary muscle spasms in adults and children ages 12 years and oldertreating involuntary muscle spasms in the neck in adultstreating severe excessive armpit sweating in adultstreating muscle spasticity in the arms or legs in adults and children ages 2 years and oldertreating crossed or misaligned eyes in adults and children ages 12 years and oldertreating overactive bladder with loss of bladder control and frequent or urgent urination in certain adultstreating loss of bladder control that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s related to a disorder of the nervous system in certain adults and certain children ages 5 years and olderFor bladder-related conditions, doctors can prescribe Botox for people who can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t take anticholinergic drugs or whose condition didn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t respond to anticholinergic drugs.With all the conditions Botox treats, nerves send signals that cause symptoms such as muscle contractions, sweating, or pain. Botox works by preventing nerves from sending signals that trigger these symptoms.It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that Botox is not used to treat:episodic migraine (in which migraine episodes occur on 14 or fewer days per month)excessive sweating in areas other than the armpitThe manufacturer of Botox warns that using this drug for conditions that the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has not approved could lead to serious side effects. For more information, see the next section.Also, you should not use Botox interchangeably with other botulinum toxin products.What are Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Like most drugs, Botox may cause mild or serious side effects. The following lists describe some of the more common side effects. These lists don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t include all possible side effects. Side effects from Botox can be different for each of the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s uses.Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about the potential side effects of Botox. They can also suggest ways to help reduce side effects.Mild side effectsHere\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a list of some of the mild side effects that Botox can cause. To learn about other mild side effects, talk with your doctor or pharmacist, or read Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information.Side effects of Botox can vary depending on where the drug is injected. Mild side effects can include:bleeding where the drug was injectedbronchitiscoughdrooping eyelidexcessive sweating in places other than your underarmsflu-like symptoms, such as fever, body aches, and nauseaheadachepain in your back, neck, arms, or legs after injectionpainful urinationsore throatupper respiratory tract infection, such as the common coldurinary tract infection (UTI)For more information about some of these side effects, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Mild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days to a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Serious side effectsSerious side effects from Botox can occur, but they aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common. They can vary depending on the condition being treated.If you have serious side effects from Botox, call your doctor right away. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Serious side effects can include:boxed warning: spread of toxin effectsallergic reactionulcers (open sores) on your corneasudden eye bleedingdifficulty swallowing or breathingurinary retention (a condition in which your bladder doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t completely empty)involuntary overreaction of your nervous system, which may cause a sudden increase in your blood pressureIn studies, an overreaction of the nervous system was more likely in people receiving Botox for loss of bladder control that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s related to a disorder of the nervous system.For more information about some of the listed side effects, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Note: The manufacturer of Botox warns that using this drug for conditions that haven\u00e2\u0080\u0099t been approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) could lead to serious side effects. Examples include excessive weakness, difficulty swallowing, and aspiration pneumonia (an infection caused by accidentally inhaling substances such as food). To learn about the FDA-approved uses of Botox, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWhat is Botox used for?\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Side effect focusLearn more about some of the side effects Botox may cause.Pain after injectionYou may have some pain after receiving Botox injections. In fact, this was a common side effect in studies of the drug. The pain typically occurs around Botox injection sites, which could include areas on your back, neck, arms, or legs.What might helpTo help relieve pain after Botox injections, try the following:Avoid rubbing or massaging the skin around or on the injection site.Apply a cold compress to the injection site.Take over-the-counter pain relievers such as acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Advil) if your doctor says it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s fine to do so.If you have pain that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s severe or bothersome after getting Botox injections, talk with your doctor.Spread of toxin effectsBotox has a boxed warning about the risk of the spread of toxin effects. A boxed warning is the most serious warning from the Food and Drug Administration (FDA).When it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s injected into your body, Botox may spread outside of the area where you receive the injection. This can lead to symptoms that are similar to botulism poisoning. These symptoms may include:hoarsenessdifficulty breathingdifficulty speakingdifficulty swallowingvision problems, such as blurry vision or double visionThese symptoms might happen within hours of getting a Botox injection. Or, they might not happen until weeks after you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve had a Botox injection. Your risk of having difficulty breathing or swallowing is higher if you already have either breathing or swallowing problems.What might helpIf you have any of the symptoms listed previously after getting a Botox injection, tell your doctor right away. Call 911 or your local emergency number if your symptoms feel life threatening.Urinary tract infectionYou might get a urinary tract infection (UTI) after getting Botox. In studies, this side effect was more common in people who received Botox to treat overactive bladder than in people receiving the drug for other conditions.A few possible symptoms of UTI include:painful urinationbloody urinepelvic painWhat might helpIf you have any UTI symptoms after getting a Botox injection, tell your doctor. Prescription drugs such as antibiotics, antivirals, or antifungals are usually needed to treat UTIs. But to help lessen UTI symptoms, you can also try home remedies such as drinking water and cranberry juice.Allergic reactionSome people may have an allergic reaction to Botox. Symptoms of a mild allergic reaction can include:rashitchinessflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)A more severe allergic reaction is rare but possible. Symptoms of a severe allergic reaction can include swelling under your skin, typically in your eyelids, lips, hands, or feet. They can also include swelling of your tongue, mouth, or throat, which can cause difficulty with breathing.Call your doctor right away if you have an allergic reaction to Botox. Call 911 or your local emergency number if your symptoms feel life threatening.What are some frequently asked questions about Botox?Find answers to some commonly asked questions about Botox.How long does it take Botox to work?Botox starts working within 1 to 3 days after it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s injected into your body. However, it might be several weeks after your injection before you notice your condition improving.Is Botox used for tension headaches?Yes, Botox is sometimes prescribed to treat tension headaches. But the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) hasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t approved Botox to treat tension headaches, so this is known as an off-label use.If you have questions about treatment options for tension headaches, talk with your doctor.How often can you get Botox injections?How often you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll be able to get Botox injections depends on the condition it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s being used to treat. In general, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox injections only once every 3 months. Your doctor will recommend how often you should receive Botox.What is Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Your doctor will recommend the dosage of Botox that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you. The following text discusses commonly used dosages, but the dosage you receive will be determined by your doctor.Forms and strengthsBotox is given as an injection into your body by a healthcare professional. For most of its uses, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox as an injection into a muscle or into multiple muscles. But the type of injection and exact injection sites vary depending on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re receiving the drug for.Botox comes as a powder inside vials. The powder is mixed with liquid to make a solution for injection. The drug is available in two strengths: 100 units and 200 units.Recommended dosagesYour doctor will recommend the dosage of Botox that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you. The following text discusses commonly used dosages for adults, but the dosage you receive will be determined by your doctor. For information on Botox dosages for children, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cChildren\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosages\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Dosage for migraine episodesTo prevent migraine episodes due to chronic migraine, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 155 units of Botox. This dose is divided across 31 different injection sites in certain muscles of your head or neck. You may receive these injections every 3 months.Dosage for excessive eye blinkingBotox may be used to treat excessive eye blinking that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s related to involuntary muscle spasms. For this use, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 1.25 to 2.5 units of Botox in certain muscles in the upper and lower eyelid of the affected eye. You\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll likely receive these injections every 3 months.If the recommended dosage isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t helping to treat your symptoms, your doctor may increase your Botox dosage by up to 5 units for each injection site. The maximum dosage for treating excessive eye blinking is 200 units per month. Dosage for muscle spasms in the neckFor treating involuntary muscle spasms in the neck, the Botox dosage varies depending on several factors. These include the position of your head and neck and where the muscle spasms occur. The recommended Botox dose for this condition is 50 units per injection site. You may receive injections every 3 months.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve never had Botox injections, your doctor will likely start you at a lower dosage. They may increase the dosage if you respond well to the drug. Dosage for excessive armpit sweatingFor treating severe excessive armpit sweating, your dose of Botox will be 50 units per injection site. You\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 10 to 15 injections in different areas of each armpit. Your doctor will recommend how often you should receive injections for your condition.Dosage for muscle spasticityBotox may be used to treat muscle spasticity in the arms or legs.For treating muscle spasticity in your arms, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 75 to 400 units of Botox across up to 18 sites in different muscles. For treating muscle spasticity in your legs, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 300 to 400 units of Botox across 16 sites in different muscles.Your doctor will recommend how often you should receive Botox for muscle spasticity. However, you likely won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t receive injections more often than every 3 months.Dosage for crossed or misaligned eyesFor crossed or misaligned eyes, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 1.25 to 5 units of Botox in the affected muscles.After 1 to 2 weeks, your doctor will examine your eyes. Depending on how well the drug worked for your condition, your doctor may increase your Botox dose. The maximum dose in this case is 25 units per muscle.The effect of Botox will decrease over 2 to 6 weeks. Your doctor may suggest additional injections for crossed or misaligned eyes as needed.Dosage for overactive bladderBotox is prescribed to treat an overactive bladder with loss of bladder control and frequent or urgent urination. For this purpose, the recommended dose is 100 units, divided into 20 injections into the muscle wall of the bladder. The maximum dose for an overactive bladder is 100 units.Your doctor will recommend how often you should receive Botox for overactive bladder. However, you likely won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t receive injections more often than every 3 months.Dosage for loss of bladder controlBotox is used to treat loss of bladder control that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s related to a disorder of the nervous system. For this use, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive 200 units of Botox, divided into 30 injections into the muscle wall of your bladder. The maximum dose for loss of bladder control is 200 units.Your doctor will recommend how often you should receive Botox for loss of bladder control. However, you likely won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t receive injections more often than every 3 months.Children\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosagesThe following discusses the recommended dosages of Botox for the conditions it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used for in children. However, your child\u00e2\u0080\u0099s doctor will recommend the right dosage for your child.Children\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage for excessive eye blinking or crossed or misaligned eyesThe dosage of Botox for children ages 12 years and older with either eye condition is the same as it is for adults. See the \u00e2\u0080\u009cDosage for excessive eye blinking\u00e2\u0080\u009d and \u00e2\u0080\u009cDosage for crossed or misaligned eyes\u00e2\u0080\u009d sections earlier for details.Children\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage for muscle spasticity in the arms or legsThe dosage of Botox for children ages 2 years and older with muscle spasticity depends on their body weight in kilograms (kg). Note that 1 kilogram is about 2.2 pounds (lb).For treating muscle spasticity in the arms, a child will receive 3 to 6 units per kg of body weight (units/kg) across up to 16 sites in different muscles. The maximum dose for this use is 6 units/kg or 200 units, whichever is lower.For treating muscle spasticity in the legs, a child will receive 4 to 8 units per kg of body weight (units/kg) across up to eight sites in different muscles. The maximum dose for this use is 8 units/kg or 300 units, whichever is lower.For a child receiving treatment for muscle spasticity in both their arms and legs, the total dose in a 3-month period should not exceed 10 units/kg or 340 units, whichever is lower.Your child\u00e2\u0080\u0099s doctor will recommend how often your child should receive Botox for muscle spasticity. However, they likely won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t receive injections more often than every 3 months.Children\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage for loss of bladder controlThe dosage of Botox for children ages 5 years and older with loss of bladder control who weigh 34 kg (about 75 lb) or more is the same as it is for adults. For more information, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cDosage for loss of bladder control\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.For children weighing less than 34 kg, the recommended dosage is 6 units/kg. Your child\u00e2\u0080\u0099s doctor will recommend how often your child should receive Botox for loss of bladder control. However, they likely won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t receive injections more often than every 3 months.Questions about Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosageHere are some common questions about Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage.What if I miss a dose of Botox? Call your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office to reschedule any missed appointments for Botox injections. The staff at your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office can help you set up another appointment.Will I need to receive Botox long term? Yes, in most cases, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive Botox long term for your condition. But be sure to talk with your doctor about this.How long does Botox take to work? Botox starts working within a few days after it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s been injected into your body. But it might be several weeks after the injection before you notice your condition improving.How is Botox given?Your doctor will explain how Botox is given. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll also explain how often you should get Botox for your condition. Depending on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re using Botox to treat, you may need to prepare for your injection. For example, if you have excessive armpit sweating, you may need to shave the area and avoid using deodorants in the 24 hours before your appointment.Your doctor may recommend general anesthesia if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re receiving injections in certain areas, such as your bladder. Your doctor will let you know how to prepare for your appointment and what to expect when you receive your Botox injections. Be sure to follow your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s instructions for when to receive Botox.Getting BotoxBotox comes as a powder inside vials. The powder is mixed with liquid to make a solution that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s injected into your body. You\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox injections from a healthcare professional.For most uses, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox as an injection into the muscle. But the type of injection and exact injection sites for Botox vary depending on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re receiving the drug for.For example, for migraine episode prevention, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox in these injection sites:your foreheadyour templesback of your headbase of your neckbetween your shouldersBut injection sites for overactive bladder (OAB) are very different. For OAB, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox injections directly into the muscle wall of your bladder.Botox and foodBotox is given as an injection. You can get Botox with or without having eaten any food.What should be considered before using Botox?Here are a few important considerations to keep in mind before you use Botox.InteractionsTaking medications, vaccines, foods, and other things with a certain drug can affect how the drug works. These effects are called interactions.Before receiving Botox, be sure to tell your doctor about all medications you take (including prescription and over-the-counter types). Also, describe any vitamins, herbs, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions these items may cause with Botox.Interactions with drugs or supplementsBotox can interact with several types of drugs, including:a group of antibiotics called aminoglycosidesanticholinergicsmuscle relaxersproducts other than Botox that contain botulinum toxinThis list doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t contain all types of drugs that may interact with Botox. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about these interactions and any others that may occur with use of Botox.Boxed warningBotox has a boxed warning. A boxed warning is the most serious warning from the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) about drug effects that may be dangerous.Botox may spread outside of the area where you receive the injection. This can lead to symptoms that are similar to botulism poisoning. These symptoms may include:hoarsenessdifficulty breathingdifficulty speakingdifficulty swallowingvision problems, such as blurry vision or double visionFor details, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWhat are Botox\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Other warningsBotox can sometimes cause harmful effects in people who have certain conditions. This is known as a drug-condition interaction. Other factors may also affect whether Botox is a good treatment option for you.Talk with your doctor about your health history before you take Botox. Be sure to tell them if any of the following factors apply to you:infection at an injection siteneuromuscular disorders, such as myasthenia gravisdifficulty breathing or swallowingdifficulty emptying your bladdera history of bleeding problemsplanned surgeryallergic reactionUse with alcoholThere aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t any known issues with drinking alcohol during Botox treatment.Keep in mind that alcohol can make you bleed more easily than usual. And bleeding is a possible side effect of Botox injections. You may need to avoid drinking alcohol for a few days before your injections.If you drink alcohol, talk with your doctor about the amount that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safe for you to drink during Botox treatment.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIf you can become pregnant, are breastfeeding, or are using birth control, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to consider whether Botox is a safe choice for you. Your doctor can discuss this with you.\u00c2\u00bbRefer to this Botox and reproductive health article for more information.What does Botox cost?As with any prescription drug, the cost of Botox can vary depending on many factors. These factors include your treatment plan, your insurance coverage, and other factors. To find current prices for Botox injections in your area, talk with your doctor.You won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t pick up Botox from a pharmacy. The drug is only sold by specialty pharmacies, and you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get Botox injections at your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office.You can visit the Botox website to view possible support options, including a Botox savings program. If you have questions about how to pay for your treatment, you can talk with your doctor or pharmacist. Ask a pharmacistQ: If I use Botox Cosmetic for cosmetic purposes, will it help prevent migraine episodes as well?AnonymousA:It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unlikely that Botox Cosmetic will help prevent migraine episodes. The number of injection sites and the doses given are much higher for helping prevent migraine episodes than for cosmetic purposes.There may be some similarities in the injection sites used. But the approved dose of Botox for migraine is 155 units given across seven different areas in your head and neck muscles. The approved dose of Botox Cosmetic is 20 to 40 units given in the specific areas desired.Note that the manufacturer of Botox and Botox Cosmetic warns against using these drugs for conditions other than what the FDA has approved for these drugs. So, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not recommended to use Botox Cosmetic for treating conditions the FDA has approved Botox for, such as preventing migraine episodes.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re interested in receiving Botox to help prevent migraine episodes, talk with your doctor to see whether Botox is right for you.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.Disclaimer: Healthline has made every effort to make certain that all information is factually correct, comprehensive, and up to date. However, this article should not be used as a substitute for the knowledge and expertise of a licensed healthcare professional. You should always consult your doctor or another healthcare professional before taking any medication. The drug information contained herein is subject to change and is not intended to cover all possible uses, directions, precautions, warnings, drug interactions, allergic reactions, or adverse effects. The absence of warnings or other information for a given drug does not indicate that the drug or drug combination is safe, effective, or appropriate for all patients or all specific uses.Botox imagesVIEW GALLERY1", "content_hash": "9a84e4ff0fc574d487a0032c2fd12ab84a1578631030646be71ded6a87b53cf6", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:31.709530+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1364", "title": "Dupixent (dupilumab): Uses, Side Effects, and Precautions", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/dupixent", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/dupixent", "text": "Key takeaways Dupixent is a prescription medication used to manage several inflammatory conditions, including eczema, asthma, COPD, and others. It works by blocking specific signaling proteins in your immune system \u00e2\u0080\u0094 specifically, interleukin-4 (IL-4) and interleukin-13 (IL-13) \u00e2\u0080\u0094 to reduce inflammation. Dupixent is given as an injection under your skin, typically every 1 to 4 weeks. More common side effects include injection site reactions, sore throat, and eye problems such as conjunctivitis (pink eye). Safety warning: You should not receive live vaccines during treatment with Dupixent. Dupixent (\u00e2\u0080\u009cdoo-PICKS-ent\u00e2\u0080\u009d) is a brand-name prescription medication used to manage several types of inflammatory conditions.The active ingredient in Dupixent is called dupilumab, which belongs to a class of biologic medications called monoclonal antibodies. No biosimilar versions of Dupixent are available at this time.Dupixent is manufactured by Regeneron Pharmaceuticals.Key termsBiologic medications (\u00e2\u0080\u009cbiologics\u00e2\u0080\u009d) are complex drugs made from natural, living sources. Biologics can be composed of proteins, sugars, nucleic acids (DNA or RNA), or a combination of these substances. They also may contain living entities, such as cells and tissues.Human monoclonal antibodies are lab-made proteins that act like natural antibodies in the immune system to fight diseases, such as cancer, autoimmune disorders, and infections.What is Dupixent used for?Specifically, Dupixent is approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for use to manage the following inflammatory conditions in certain situations:atopic dermatitis (eczema) in adults and some childrencertain types of asthma in adults and some childrenchronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in adultschronic rhinosinusitis with nasal polyps in adults and some childreneosinophilic esophagitis in adults and some childrenprurigo nodularis in adultsbullous pemphigoid in adultschronic spontaneous urticaria in adults and some childrenallergic fungal rhinosinusitis in adults and some childrenDupixent reduces inflammation associated with these conditions by blocking specific inflammation signals in your immune system called interleukin-4 (IL-4) and interleukin-13 (IL-13).For more details about how Dupixent works to manage your specific condition, talk with your doctor. What is Dupixent\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Dupixent comes as a liquid solution in prefilled syringes or prefilled pens. Dupixent is given as an injection under your skin. The dosage your doctor prescribes will depend on several factors, including:the type and severity of the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re prescribed Dupixent to treatyour ageyour weightother medical conditions you may haveBe sure to use only the Dupixent dosage your doctor prescribes for you. They will determine the best dosage to fit your needs for optimal effectiveness and safety.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Dupixent dosages by conditionWhat are Dupixent\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Side effects of Dupixent may vary depending on the condition the drug is being used to manage and other factors, such as:your ageother health conditions you haveother medications you may be takingThe most common side effects of Dupixent reported in clinical studies of the drug for its FDA-approved uses included:injection site reactionsconjunctivitisblepharitiskeratitisdry eyesoral herpes (cold sores) and other herpes simplex virus infectionsinsomniamuscle or joint painNote: This list does not include all of the more common side effects of Dupixent.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Side effects of Dupixent and how to manage themWhat should be considered before using Dupixent?Here is important information you should consider before starting Dupixent treatment.InteractionsTaking medications, vaccines, foods, and other things with a certain drug can affect how the drug works. These effects are called interactions.Dupixent is not known to interact with other medications, herbs, supplements, foods, or alcohol. The manufacturer did not list any interactions in the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information. However, certain interactions may still be possible even if they have not been reported with Dupixent.Before starting Dupixent treatment, talk with your doctor and pharmacist. Tell them about all prescription, over-the-counter, and other drugs you take. Also, tell them about any vitamins, herbs, and supplements you take. Sharing this information can help you avoid potential interactions.Dupixent and alcoholAlcohol is not known to interact with Dupixent. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s likely safe to consume alcohol while receiving Dupixent injections. If you have questions about drinking alcohol during treatment with Dupixent, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. They can tell you how much alcohol, if any, is safe to drink during Dupixent treatment.Dupixent and vaccinesYou should not receive live vaccines during your Dupixent treatment. This is because live vaccines contain weakened versions of the bacteria or virus that they\u00e2\u0080\u0099re meant to protect against. Getting a live vaccine during treatment with Dupixent can increase your risk of infection. Examples of live vaccines include measles, mumps, rubella (MMR), rotavirus, and chickenpox.If you need to receive a vaccine, talk with your doctor first to make sure it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safe.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIf you can become pregnant or are breastfeeding, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to consider whether Dupixent is a safe choice for you. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unclear whether Dupixent is safe for use during pregnancy or while breastfeeding.For more information, you can refer to this article on Dupixent and reproductive health. If you have other questions, talk with your doctor.WarningsDupixent can sometimes cause harmful effects in people who have certain conditions. These are known as drug-condition interactions. Other factors may also affect whether Dupixent is a good treatment option for you.Talk with your doctor about your health history before you inject Dupixent. Be sure to tell them if any of the following factors apply to you:history of joint painhistory of eye problems, such as pink eye or keratitisrisk factors for psoriasis, such as a family history of the condition, certain injuries, or smokingrisk factors for psoriatic arthritis, such as having psoriasis, a family history of the condition, or smokingtaking or stopping a steroid medicationactive parasitic infectionprevious allergic reaction to Dupixent or a similar drugpregnancy or breastfeeding Find a medical specialist in your area todayYour healthcare team may comprise several people who can provide support.Sometimes, a medical specialist will be required to help diagnose, manage, or treat a healthcare condition. You can find the following medical specialists in your area today:primary care doctorallergist or immunologistdermatologistear, nose, and throat (ENT) doctorpulmonologistOverdoseDo not inject more Dupixent than your doctor prescribes. Doing so may lead to harmful effects.What to do in case you use too much DupixentCall your doctor if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve used too much Dupixent. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach America\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Poison Centers, or use its online resource. However, if you have severe symptoms, immediately call 911 (or your local emergency number) or go to the nearest emergency room.Frequently asked questionsWhat does Dupixent do to your immune system?Dupixent is a monoclonal antibody drug, which works on very specific targets within your immune system. It\u00e2\u0080\u0098s not considered an immunosuppressant, which is a type of drug that suppresses the immune system more generally. Corticosteroids are an example of a group of drugs that are immunosuppressants.Dupixent works by blocking specific signaling proteins in your immune system \u00e2\u0080\u0094 specifically, interleukin-4 (IL-4) and interleukin-13 (IL-13) \u00e2\u0080\u0094 to reduce harmful inflammation associated with the conditions Dupixent is used to treat, such as atopic dermatitis (eczema), asthma, and COPD.Keep in mind that your immune system relies on inflammation signals to respond to certain vaccines. For information about receiving vaccines during Dupixent treatment, see \u00e2\u0080\u009cDupixent and vaccines\u00e2\u0080\u009d later in this article.For more details about how Dupixent affects your immune system, talk with your doctor.Is Dupixent a type of steroid?No. Dupixent is a monoclonal antibody drug, which works on specific targets within your immune system. It\u00e2\u0080\u0098s not considered an immunosuppressant, which is a type of drug that suppresses the immune system more generally. Corticosteroids are an example of a group of drugs that are immunosuppressants.What exactly does Dupixent do?Dupixent\u00e2\u0080\u0099s mechanism of action (how it works) is to block certain proteins from binding to their receptors in your immune system. These proteins are called interleukin-4 (IL-4) and interleukin-13 (IL-13).Usually, when IL-4 and IL-13 bind to their receptors, your immune system releases proteins called cytokines. This release of cytokines leads to inflammation like that associated with the conditions Dupixent is approved to treat.Can Dupixent cause weight gain or hair loss?It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unclear whether Dupixent causes weight gain or hair loss. These were not reported as side effects in studies of the drug.Some research on dupilumab, the active ingredient in Dupixent, suggests the drug may be associated with hair loss. A small study on dupilumab for atopic dermatitis found that some people experienced weight gain during treatment with the drug. But more research is needed to determine whether Dupixent causes weight gain or hair loss.Keep in mind that other drugs may be used together with Dupixent. These drugs, such as corticosteroids, often cause multiple side effects.If you have concerns about any side effects from Dupixent, talk with your doctor.Cost and savingsCosts of prescription drugs can vary depending on many factors. These factors include what your insurance plan covers and which pharmacy you use.If you have questions about how to pay for your prescription, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You can also visit the Dupixent manufacturer\u00e2\u0080\u0099s website to see support options, such as the Dupixent MyWay Copay Card.Learn more about Dupixent and cost.TakeawayDupixent (dupilumab) is a prescription biologic injection used to treat chronic inflammatory conditions, including moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis (eczema), asthma, COPD, and nasal polyps. It works by blocking IL-4 and IL-13 proteins to reduce immune system inflammation. While effective for long-term symptom management, Dupixent may cause side effects, such as injection site reactions, cold sores, or eye-related issues like conjunctivitis. Dosage varies by age, weight, and the specific condition being treated, but it is typically administered every two to four weeks. Talk with your doctor to understand the benefits, potential risks, and insurance coverage options for your specific treatment plan.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Dupixent imagesVIEW GALLERY6", "content_hash": "ea1c06d1200b55d06ffa46e5af9f9e291f1e40041afcb4238bcc7833f1ca6f52", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:35.094517+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1365", "title": "States and Elections Clause | U.S. Constitution Annotated | US Law | LII / Legal Information Institute", "url": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/constitution-conan/article-1/section-4/clause-1/states-and-elections-clause", "final_url": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/constitution-conan/article-1/section-4/clause-1/states-and-elections-clause", "text": "prev | next ArtI.S4.C1.2 States and Elections Clause Article I, Section 4, Clause 1: The Times, Places and Manner of holding Elections for Senators and Representatives, shall be prescribed in each State by the Legislature thereof; but the Congress may at any time by Law make or alter such Regulations, except as to the Places of chusing Senators. By its terms, Article I, Section 4, Clause 1, referred to as the Elections Clause, contemplates that state legislatures will establish the times, places, and manner of holding elections for the House of Representatives and the Senate, subject to Congress making or altering such state regulations (except as to the place of choosing Senators).1 FootnoteU.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 4, cl. 1. See Foster v. Love, 522 U.S. 67, 69 (1997) ( \u201c[I]t is well settled that the Elections Clause grants Congress \u2018the power to override state regulations\u2019 by establishing uniform rules for federal elections binding on the States.\u2019\u201d (quoting U.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 832\u201333 (1995))). The Supreme Court has interpreted the Elections Clause expansively, enabling states \u201cto provide a complete code for congressional elections, not only as to times and places, but in relation to notices, registration, supervision of voting, protection of voters, prevention of fraud and corrupt practices, counting of votes, duties of inspectors and canvassers, and making and publication of election returns.\u201d 2 Footnote Smiley v. Holm, 285 U.S. 355, 366 (1932) The Court has further recognized the states\u2019 ability to establish sanctions for violating election laws3 FootnoteId. at 369. as well as authority over recounts4 FootnoteRoudebush v. Hartke, 405 U.S. 15, 24, 25 (1972). and primaries.5 FootnoteUnited States v. Classic, 313 U.S. 299, 320 (1941). The Elections Clause, however, does not govern voter qualifications, which under Article I, Section 2, Clause 1, and the Seventeenth Amendment must be the same as the \u201cQualifications requisite for Electors of the most numerous Branch of the State Legislatures.\u201d 6 FootnoteU.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 2, cl. 1; U.S. Const. amend. XVII. See also Arizona v. Inter Tribal Council of Ariz., Inc., 570 U.S. 1, 17 (2013) ( \u201cPrescribing voting qualifications, therefore, \u2018forms no part of the power to be conferred upon the national government\u2019 by the Elections Clause, which is \u2018expressly restricted to the regulation of the times, the places, and the manner of elections.\u2019\u201d (quoting The Federalist No. 60 (Alexander Hamilton))). Similarly, the authority of states to establish the \u201cTimes, Places and Manner of holding Elections for Senators and Representatives\u201d does not include authority to impose additional qualification requirements to be a Member of the House of Representatives or a Senator, which are governed by the Constitution\u2019s Qualification Clauses at Article I, Section 2, Clause 2 for Members of the House and at Article I, Section 3, Clause 3 for the Senate.7 FootnoteU.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 2, cl. 2; U.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 3, cl. 3. See United States Term Limits v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779 (1995) State authority to regulate the times, places, and manner of holding congressional elections has been described by the Court as the ability \u201cto enact the numerous requirements as to procedure and safeguards which experience shows are necessary in order to enforce the fundamental rights involved.\u201d 8 FootnoteSmiley v. Holm, 285 U.S. 355, 366 (1932). The Court has upheld a variety of state laws designed to ensure that elections are fair and honest and orderly.9 FootnoteSee, e.g., Storer v. Brown, 415 U.S. 724 (1974) (restrictions on independent candidacies requiring early commitment prior to party primaries); Roudebush v. Hartke, 405 U.S. 15, 25 (1972) (recount for Senatorial election); Munro v. Socialist Workers Party, 479 U.S. 189 (1986) (requirement that minor party candidate demonstrate substantial support\u20141% of votes cast in the primary election\u2014before being placed on ballot for general election). The Court, however, has held that courts should not modify election rules if the election is imminent and \u201c'[n]o bright line separates permissible election-related regulation from unconstitutional infringements.\u2019\u201d Purcell v. Gonzalez, 549 U.S. 1, 5 (2006) (per curiam) (quoting Timmons v. Twin Cities Area New Party, 520 U.S. 351, 359 (1997)). In Purcell v. Gonzalez, the Court observed that \u201cthe imminence of the election and the inadequate time to resolve the factual disputes\u201d required the Court to \u201cof necessity allow the election to proceed without an injunction suspending the voter identification rules.\u201d Purcell, 549 U.S. at 5\u20136. See also Republican Nat\u2019l Comm. v. Democratic Nat\u2019l Comm., No. 19A1016, slip op. (U.S. Apr. 2020) (per curiam) (noting that \u201clower federal courts should ordinarily not alter the election rules on the eve of the election\u201d ) (citing Purcell v. Gonzalez, 549 U.S. 1 (2006) (per curiam); Frank v. Walker, 574 U.S. 929 (2014); Veasey v. Perry, 574 U.S. 951 (2014)). But the Court distinguished state laws that go beyond \u201cprotection of the integrity and regularity of the election process,\u201d and instead operate to disadvantage a particular class of candidates10 Footnote U.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 835 (1995) or negate the need for a general election.11 FootnoteFoster v. Love, 522 U.S. 67, 69 (1997) (explaining that the Elections Clause \u201cis a default provision; it invests the State with responsibility for the mechanics of congressional elections, but only so far as Congress declines to preempt state legislative choices\u201d ); see id. at 74 (holding that a Louisiana statute that deemed the winner of the primary to be the winner of the general election void and preempted by federal law which set the date of the election for federal offices). The Court noted that the Elections Clause does not allow states to set term limits, which the Court viewed as \u201cdisadvantaging a particular class of candidates and evading the dictates of the Qualifications Clause,\u201d 12 FootnoteU.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 832 (1995) ( \u201cPetitioners make the related argument that Amendment 73 merely regulates the \u201cManner\u201d of elections and that the amendment is therefore a permissible exercise of state power under Article I, Section 4, Clause 1 (the Elections Clause) to regulate the \u201cTimes, Places and Manner\u201d of elections. We cannot agree.\u201d ). or ballot labels identifying candidates who disregarded voters\u2019 instructions on term limits or declined to pledge support for them.13 FootnoteCook v. Gralike, 531 U.S. 510 (2001). In its 1995 decision in U.S. Term Limits v. Thornton, the Court explained: \u201c[T]he Framers understood the Elections Clause as a grant of authority to issue procedural regulations, and not as a source of power to dictate electoral outcomes, to favor or disfavor a class of candidates, or to evade important constitutional restraints.\u201d 14 FootnoteThornton, 514 U.S. at 833\u201334. See also Burdick v. Takushi, 504 U.S. 428, 433 (1992) (states have an interest in \u201cseeking to assure that elections are operated equitably and efficiently\u201d ); Tashjian v. Republican Party of Conn., 479 U.S. 208, 217 (1986) ( \u201cthe power to regulate the time, place, and manner of elections does not justify, without more, the abridgment of fundamental rights.\u201d ); Anderson v. Celebrezze, 460 U.S. 780, 788 n.9 (1983) (states may adopt \u201cgenerally applicable and evenhanded restrictions that protect the integrity and reliability of the electoral process itself.\u201d ). The Supreme Court has held that Article I, Section 4, Clause 1, provides for Congress, not the courts, to regulate how states exercise their authority over Senate and House elections,15 FootnoteRucho v. Common Cause, No. 18-422, slip op. (U.S. June 2019). See also Arizona v. Inter Tribal Council of Ariz., Inc., 570 U.S. 1 (2013); Ex parte Siebold, 100 U.S. 371, 392 (1880) ( \u201cThe power of Congress . . . is paramount, and may be exercised at any time, and to any extent which it deems expedient.\u201d ). although courts may hear cases concerning claims of one-person, one-vote violations and racial gerrymandering.16 FootnoteShaw v. Reno, 509 U.S. 630 (1993); see also Wesberry v. Sanders, 376 U.S. 1 (1964); Wright v. Rockefeller, 376 U.S. 52 (1964); Baker v. Carr, 369 U.S. 186 (1962); Gomillion v. Lightfoot, 364 U.S. 339 (1960); Colegrove v. Green, 328 U.S. 549 (1946); Wood v. Broom, 287 U.S. 1 (1932). For example, in its 2019 Rucho v. Common Cause decision, the Court held that partisan gerrymandering claims\u2014claims that one political party has gerrymandered congressional districts to the disadvantage of the other party\u2014are not justiciable by courts because \u201cthe only provision in the Constitution [Article I, Section 4, Clause 1] that specifically addresses the matter assigns it to the political branches\u201d 17 FootnoteRucho v. Common Cause, No. 18-422, slip op. at 29 (U.S. June 2019). and such claims present political questions\u2014 \u201coutside the courts\u2019 competence and therefore beyond the courts\u2019 jurisdiction\u201d \u2014that are not for courts to decide.18 FootnoteId. at 7. The Court observed that \u201c[a]mong the political question cases the Court has identified are those that lack \u2018judicially discoverable and manageable standards for resolving [them].\u2019\u201d Id. (quoting Baker v. Carr, 369 U.S. 186 (1962)); see also id. ( \u201cThis Court\u2019s authority to act . . . \u2018is grounded in and limited by the necessity of resolving according to legal principles, a plaintiff\u2019s particular claim of legal right.\u2019 The question here is whether there is an \u2018appropriate role for the Federal Judiciary\u2019 in remedying the problem of partisan gerrymandering\u2014whether such claims are claims of legal right, resolvable according to legal principles, or political questions that must find their resolution elsewhere.\u201d (quoting Gill v. Whitford, No. 16-1161, slip op. at 8, 13 (U.S. June 2018))). Although noting that the \u201cdistricting plans at issue here are highly partisan, by any measure,\u201d 19 FootnoteId. at 2. the Rucho Court observed that partisan gerrymandering claims raise particular problems for courts to adjudicate. First, the Court noted that the Framers had expected partisan interests to inform how states drew district lines.20 FootnoteId. at 12. Consequently, the Court reasoned that the problem is not whether partisan gerrymandering has occurred but when it has \u201cgone too far.\u201d 21 FootnoteId. at 13 (citing Vieth v. Jubelirer541 U.S 267, 296 (2004) (plurality opinion)). See also Hunt v. Cromartie, 526 U.S. 541, 555 (1999) ( \u201cOur prior decisions have made clear that a jurisdiction may engage in constitutional political gerrymandering . . . .\u201d ). Second, the Court observed that there is no obvious standard by which to assess whether a partisan gerrymander has gone too far.22 FootnoteId. see also Vieth v. Jubelirer, 541 U.S. 267 (2004); Davis v. Bandemer, 478 U.S. 109 (1986);Gaffney v. Cummings, 412 U.S. 735 (1973)). In Gill v. Whitford, the Court observed that \u201cthis Court is not responsible for vindicating generalized partisan preferences. The Court\u2019s constitutionally prescribed role is to vindicate the individual rights of the people appearing before it.\u201d Gill v. Whitford, No. 16-1161, slip op. at 21 (U.S. June 2018). The Court stated: \u201cThe initial difficulty in settling on a \u2018clear manageable and politically neutral\u2019 test for fairness is that it is not even clear what fairness looks like in this context. There is a large measure of \u2018unfairness\u2019 in any winner-take-all system.\u201d 23 FootnoteRucho, slip op. at 17; see also Vieth, 541 U.S. at 291 ( \u201c'Fairness\u2019 does not seem to us a judicially manageable standard. . . . Some criterion more solid and more demonstrably met than [fairness] seems to us necessary to enable the state legislatures to discern the limits of their districting discretion, to meaningfully constrain the discretion of the courts, and to win public acceptance for the courts\u2019 intrusion into a process that is the very foundation of democratic decisionmaking.\u201d ). The Court in Rucho further emphasized that it did not condone partisan gerrymanders but that Congress is constitutionally authorized to address the issue.24 FootnoteRucho, slip op. at 9 ( \u201cCongress has regularly exercised its Elections Clause power, including to address partisan gerrymandering.\u201d ). Likewise, in Husted v. A. Philip Randolph Institute, the Court upheld a state law providing for removing voters from voting roles based on indicators that they had moved, noting, among other things, that the state law was consistent with federal law and that the Court had \u201cno authority to dismiss the considered judgment of Congress and the Ohio Legislature regarding the probative value of a registrant\u2019s failure to send back a return card.\u201d 25 FootnoteHusted v. A. Philip Randolph Inst., No. 16-960, slip op. at 25, 26 (U.S. June 11, 2018). In its 2023 Moore v. Harper decision, the Supreme Court held that the Elections Clause, in Article I, Section 4 of the U.S. Constitution, does not protect a state legislature from a state court reviewing whether the state legislature\u2019s exercise of its Election Clause authority is consistent with its state constitution.26 FootnoteMoore v. Harper, No. 21-1271 (U.S. June 27, 2023). Rejecting an argument that the Elections Clause insulated state legislatures from the \u201cordinary exercise of state judicial review,\u201d 27 FootnoteId. at 15. the Court observed: \u201cState courts retain the authority to apply state constitutional restraints when legislatures act under the power conferred upon them by the Elections Clause.\u201d 28 FootnoteId. at 29. The Court, however, cautioned that state court power to review state rules regarding \u201c[t]he Times, Places and Manner of holding Elections for Senators and Representatives\u201d was limited to \u201cthe ordinary bounds of judicial review\u201d and that state courts should not \u201carrogate to themselves the power vested in state legislatures to regulate federal elections.\u201d 29 FootnoteId. The Court further stated: \u201cIn interpreting state law in this area, state courts may not so exceed the bounds of ordinary judicial review as to unconstitutionally intrude upon the role specifically reserved to state legislatures by Article I, Section 4, of the Federal Constitution. Because we need not decide whether that occurred in today\u2019s case, the judgment of the North Carolina Supreme Court is affirmed.\u201d Id. at 30. The Court addressed what constitutes regulation by a state \u201cLegislature\u201d for purposes of the Elections Clause in its 2015 decision in Arizona State Legislature v. Arizona Independent Redistricting Commission.30 Footnote No. 13-1314 (2015). There, the Court rejected the Arizona legislature\u2019s challenge to the validity of the Arizona Independent Redistricting Commission (AIRC) and AIRC\u2019s 2012 map of congressional districts.31 FootnoteId. at 2\u20133. The Commission had been established by a 2000 ballot initiative, which removed redistricting authority from the legislature and vested it in the AIRC.32 Footnote Id. The legislature asserted that this arrangement violated the Elections Clause because the Clause contemplates regulation by a state \u201cLegislature\u201d and \u201cLegislature\u201d means the state\u2019s representative assembly.33 FootnoteId. at 2. The Court disagreed and held that Arizona\u2019s use of an independent commission to establish congressional districts is permissible because the Elections Clause uses the word \u201cLegislature\u201d to describe \u201cthe power that makes laws,\u201d a term that is broad enough to encompass the power provided by the Arizona constitution for the people to make laws through ballot initiatives.34 FootnoteId. at 18. The Court also found that the use of the commission was permissible under 2 U.S.C. \u00a7 2a (c), a statutory provision that the Court construed as safeguarding to \u201ceach state full authority to employ in the creation of congressional districts its own laws and regulations.\u201d Id. at 19. In so finding, the Court noted that the word \u201cLegislature\u201d has been construed in various ways depending upon the constitutional provision in which it is used, and its meaning depends upon the function that the entity denominated as the \u201cLegislature\u201d is called upon to exercise in a specific context.35 FootnoteId. at 18. Here, in the context of the Elections Clause, the Court found that the function of the \u201cLegislature\u201d was lawmaking and that this function could be performed by the people of Arizona via an initiative consistent with state law.36 FootnoteId. See also Ohio ex rel. Davis v. Hildebrant, 241 U.S. 565, 568 (1916) (holding that a state\u2019s referendum system to override redistricting legislation \u201cwas contained within the legislative power,\u201d rejecting the argument that the referendum was not part of the \u201cLegislature\u201d ). The Court also pointed to dictionary definitions from the time of the Framers;37 FootnoteArizona, No. 13-1314, slip op. at 24 (noting that \u201cdictionaries, even those in circulation during the founding era, capaciously define the word \u2018legislature\u2019\u201d to include as \u201c[t]he power that makes laws\u201d and \u201cthe Authority of making laws\u201d ). the Framers\u2019 intent in adopting the Elections Clause;38 FootnoteId. at 25 ( \u201cThe dominant purpose of the Elections Clause . . . was to empower Congress to override state election rules, not to restrict the way States enact legislation. . . . [T]he Clause \u2018was the Framers\u2019 insurance against the possibility that a State would refuse to provide for the election of representatives to the Federal Congress.\u2019\u201d ). the \u201charmony\u201d between the initiative process and the Constitution\u2019s \u201cconception of the people as the font of governmental power;\u201d 39 FootnoteId. at 30 ( \u201cThe Framers may not have imagined the modern initiative process in which the people of a State exercise legislative power coextensive with the authority of an institutional legislature. But the invention of the initiative was in full harmony with the Constitution\u2019s conception of the people as the font of governmental power.\u201d ). and the practical consequences of invalidating the Arizona initiative.40 FootnoteId. at 31, 33 (noting that it would be \u201cperverse\u201d to interpret the term \u201cLegislature\u201d to exclude the initiative, because the initiative is intended to check legislators\u2019 ability to determine the boundaries of the districts in which they run, and that a contrary ruling would invalidate a number of other state provisions regarding initiatives and referendums). Footnotes 1 U.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 4, cl. 1. See Foster v. Love, 522 U.S. 67, 69 (1997) ( \u201c[I]t is well settled that the Elections Clause grants Congress \u2018the power to override state regulations\u2019 by establishing uniform rules for federal elections binding on the States.\u2019\u201d (quoting U.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 832\u201333 (1995))). 2 Smiley v. Holm, 285 U.S. 355, 366 (1932) 3 Id. at 369. 4 Roudebush v. Hartke, 405 U.S. 15, 24, 25 (1972). 5 United States v. Classic, 313 U.S. 299, 320 (1941). 6 U.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 2, cl. 1; U.S. Const. amend. XVII. See also Arizona v. Inter Tribal Council of Ariz., Inc., 570 U.S. 1, 17 (2013) ( \u201cPrescribing voting qualifications, therefore, \u2018forms no part of the power to be conferred upon the national government\u2019 by the Elections Clause, which is \u2018expressly restricted to the regulation of the times, the places, and the manner of elections.\u2019\u201d (quoting The Federalist No. 60 (Alexander Hamilton))). 7 U.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 2, cl. 2; U.S. Const. art. I, \u00a7 3, cl. 3. See United States Term Limits v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779 (1995) 8 Smiley v. Holm, 285 U.S. 355, 366 (1932). 9 See, e.g., Storer v. Brown, 415 U.S. 724 (1974) (restrictions on independent candidacies requiring early commitment prior to party primaries); Roudebush v. Hartke, 405 U.S. 15, 25 (1972) (recount for Senatorial election); Munro v. Socialist Workers Party, 479 U.S. 189 (1986) (requirement that minor party candidate demonstrate substantial support\u20141% of votes cast in the primary election\u2014before being placed on ballot for general election). The Court, however, has held that courts should not modify election rules if the election is imminent and \u201c'[n]o bright line separates permissible election-related regulation from unconstitutional infringements.\u2019\u201d Purcell v. Gonzalez, 549 U.S. 1, 5 (2006) (per curiam) (quoting Timmons v. Twin Cities Area New Party, 520 U.S. 351, 359 (1997)). In Purcell v. Gonzalez, the Court observed that \u201cthe imminence of the election and the inadequate time to resolve the factual disputes\u201d required the Court to \u201cof necessity allow the election to proceed without an injunction suspending the voter identification rules.\u201d Purcell, 549 U.S. at 5\u20136. See also Republican Nat\u2019l Comm. v. Democratic Nat\u2019l Comm., No. 19A1016, slip op. (U.S. Apr. 2020) (per curiam) (noting that \u201clower federal courts should ordinarily not alter the election rules on the eve of the election\u201d ) (citing Purcell v. Gonzalez, 549 U.S. 1 (2006) (per curiam); Frank v. Walker, 574 U.S. 929 (2014); Veasey v. Perry, 574 U.S. 951 (2014)). 10 U.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 835 (1995) 11 Foster v. Love, 522 U.S. 67, 69 (1997) (explaining that the Elections Clause \u201cis a default provision; it invests the State with responsibility for the mechanics of congressional elections, but only so far as Congress declines to preempt state legislative choices\u201d ); see id. at 74 (holding that a Louisiana statute that deemed the winner of the primary to be the winner of the general election void and preempted by federal law which set the date of the election for federal offices). 12 U.S. Term Limits, Inc. v. Thornton, 514 U.S. 779, 832 (1995) ( \u201cPetitioners make the related argument that Amendment 73 merely regulates the \u201cManner\u201d of elections and that the amendment is therefore a permissible exercise of state power under Article I, Section 4, Clause 1 (the Elections Clause) to regulate the \u201cTimes, Places and Manner\u201d of elections. We cannot agree.\u201d ). 13 Cook v. Gralike, 531 U.S. 510 (2001). 14 Thornton, 514 U.S. at 833\u201334. See also Burdick v. Takushi, 504 U.S. 428, 433 (1992) (states have an interest in \u201cseeking to assure that elections are operated equitably and efficiently\u201d ); Tashjian v. Republican Party of Conn., 479 U.S. 208, 217 (1986) ( \u201cthe power to regulate the time, place, and manner of elections does not justify, without more, the abridgment of fundamental rights.\u201d ); Anderson v. Celebrezze, 460 U.S. 780, 788 n.9 (1983) (states may adopt \u201cgenerally applicable and evenhanded restrictions that protect the integrity and reliability of the electoral process itself.\u201d ). 15 Rucho v. Common Cause, No. 18-422, slip op. (U.S. June 2019). See also Arizona v. Inter Tribal Council of Ariz., Inc., 570 U.S. 1 (2013); Ex parte Siebold, 100 U.S. 371, 392 (1880) ( \u201cThe power of Congress . . . is paramount, and may be exercised at any time, and to any extent which it deems expedient.\u201d ). 16 Shaw v. Reno, 509 U.S. 630 (1993); see also Wesberry v. Sanders, 376 U.S. 1 (1964); Wright v. Rockefeller, 376 U.S. 52 (1964); Baker v. Carr, 369 U.S. 186 (1962); Gomillion v. Lightfoot, 364 U.S. 339 (1960); Colegrove v. Green, 328 U.S. 549 (1946); Wood v. Broom, 287 U.S. 1 (1932). 17 Rucho v. Common Cause, No. 18-422, slip op. at 29 (U.S. June 2019). 18 Id. at 7. The Court observed that \u201c[a]mong the political question cases the Court has identified are those that lack \u2018judicially discoverable and manageable standards for resolving [them].\u2019\u201d Id. (quoting Baker v. Carr, 369 U.S. 186 (1962)); see also id. ( \u201cThis Court\u2019s authority to act . . . \u2018is grounded in and limited by the necessity of resolving according to legal principles, a plaintiff\u2019s particular claim of legal right.\u2019 The question here is whether there is an \u2018appropriate role for the Federal Judiciary\u2019 in remedying the problem of partisan gerrymandering\u2014whether such claims are claims of legal right, resolvable according to legal principles, or political questions that must find their resolution elsewhere.\u201d (quoting Gill v. Whitford, No. 16-1161, slip op. at 8, 13 (U.S. June 2018))). 19 Id. at 2. 20 Id. at 12. 21 Id. at 13 (citing Vieth v. Jubelirer, 541 U.S 267, 296 (2004) (plurality opinion)). See also Hunt v. Cromartie, 526 U.S. 541, 555 (1999) ( \u201cOur prior decisions have made clear that a jurisdiction may engage in constitutional political gerrymandering . . . .\u201d ). 22 Id. see also Vieth v. Jubelirer, 541 U.S. 267 (2004); Davis v. Bandemer, 478 U.S. 109 (1986);Gaffney v. Cummings, 412 U.S. 735 (1973)). In Gill v. Whitford, the Court observed that \u201cthis Court is not responsible for vindicating generalized partisan preferences. The Court\u2019s constitutionally prescribed role is to vindicate the individual rights of the people appearing before it.\u201d Gill v. Whitford, No. 16-1161, slip op. at 21 (U.S. June 2018). 23 Rucho, slip op. at 17; see also Vieth, 541 U.S. at 291 ( \u201c'Fairness\u2019 does not seem to us a judicially manageable standard. . . . Some criterion more solid and more demonstrably met than [fairness] seems to us necessary to enable the state legislatures to discern the limits of their districting discretion, to meaningfully constrain the discretion of the courts, and to win public acceptance for the courts\u2019 intrusion into a process that is the very foundation of democratic decisionmaking.\u201d ). 24 Rucho, slip op. at 9 ( \u201cCongress has regularly exercised its Elections Clause power, including to address partisan gerrymandering.\u201d ). 25 Husted v. A. Philip Randolph Inst., No. 16-960, slip op. at 25, 26 (U.S. June 11, 2018). 26 Moore v. Harper, No. 21-1271 (U.S. June 27, 2023). 27 Id. at 15. 28 Id. at 29. 29 Id. The Court further stated: \u201cIn interpreting state law in this area, state courts may not so exceed the bounds of ordinary judicial review as to unconstitutionally intrude upon the role specifically reserved to state legislatures by Article I, Section 4, of the Federal Constitution. Because we need not decide whether that occurred in today\u2019s case, the judgment of the North Carolina Supreme Court is affirmed.\u201d Id. at 30. 30 No. 13-1314 (2015). 31 Id. at 2\u20133. 32 Id. 33 Id. at 2. 34 Id. at 18. The Court also found that the use of the commission was permissible under 2 U.S.C. \u00a7 2a (c), a statutory provision that the Court construed as safeguarding to \u201ceach state full authority to employ in the creation of congressional districts its own laws and regulations.\u201d Id. at 19. 35 Id. at 18. 36 Id. See also Ohio ex rel. Davis v. Hildebrant, 241 U.S. 565, 568 (1916) (holding that a state\u2019s referendum system to override redistricting legislation \u201cwas contained within the legislative power,\u201d rejecting the argument that the referendum was not part of the \u201cLegislature\u201d ). 37 Arizona, No. 13-1314, slip op. at 24 (noting that \u201cdictionaries, even those in circulation during the founding era, capaciously define the word \u2018legislature\u2019\u201d to include as \u201c[t]he power that makes laws\u201d and \u201cthe Authority of making laws\u201d ). 38 Id. at 25 ( \u201cThe dominant purpose of the Elections Clause . . . was to empower Congress to override state election rules, not to restrict the way States enact legislation. . . . [T]he Clause \u2018was the Framers\u2019 insurance against the possibility that a State would refuse to provide for the election of representatives to the Federal Congress.\u2019\u201d ). 39 Id. at 30 ( \u201cThe Framers may not have imagined the modern initiative process in which the people of a State exercise legislative power coextensive with the authority of an institutional legislature. But the invention of the initiative was in full harmony with the Constitution\u2019s conception of the people as the font of governmental power.\u201d ). 40 Id. at 31, 33 (noting that it would be \u201cperverse\u201d to interpret the term \u201cLegislature\u201d to exclude the initiative, because the initiative is intended to check legislators\u2019 ability to determine the boundaries of the districts in which they run, and that a contrary ruling would invalidate a number of other state provisions regarding initiatives and referendums). U.S. Constitution Annotated Toolbox Explanation of the Constitution - from the Congressional Research Service", "content_hash": "bfd1797e4e2ef2709b40462f77258a19c9a51f55072d921bfbf16c878d1641cd", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:35.402387+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1366", "title": "Eylea Injection Overview", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/eylea", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/eylea", "text": "Key takeaways Eylea is prescribed to prevent vision loss from conditions like wet age-related macular degeneration and diabetic macular edema by targeting and blocking a protein called vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF). Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects may range from mild issues like eye pain to serious ones like retinal detachment, infection, increased eye pressure, and heart or blood vessel problems. A healthcare professional injects Eylea into the eye, with the dosage and frequency depending on the specific eye condition being treated. Long-term treatment may be needed to manage these conditions. Eylea (aflibercept) is a brand-name biologic drug prescribed to help prevent vision loss caused by certain eye conditions. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a liquid solution given by healthcare professionals as an injection into the eye.Eylea basicsEylea contains the active ingredient aflibercept. (An active ingredient is what makes a medication work.) It belongs to a group of drugs called vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) inhibitors.VEGF is a protein that causes abnormal blood vessels to develop in the retina, which can break open and cause bleeding inside the eye.Eylea targets VEGF and blocks its actions on blood vessels. This helps to slow down abnormal blood vessel growth and vision loss from certain eye conditions.Eylea is a brand-name biologic that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s also available in biosimilar versions, such as Ahzantive (aflibercept-mrbb), Enzeevu (aflibercept-abzv), and Pavblu (aflibercept-ayyh).Biosimilars have the same active ingredient core name as the brand-name drug (also called the reference product), but with additional letters following a hyphen at the end. This is to show that each biosimilar version is distinct from other biosimilars that may be developed.Like generic drugs, biosimilar drugs are typically as effective as their reference brand-name counterparts and tend to cost less.For more information about the availability of biosimilar versions of Eylea, talk with your doctor.Note: Eylea is available in a version that contains a longer-acting form of aflibercept. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s called Eylea HD and is also a liquid solution given as an injection into the eye. This article focuses mainly on Eylea. To learn more about Eylea HD, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.What is Eylea used for?Eylea is specifically used in adults to slow down the progression of vision loss from:wet age-related macular degenerationmacular edema following retinal vascular occlusiondiabetic macular edemadiabetic retinopathyEylea is also used to treat retinopathy of prematurity (ROP), an eye condition that may occur in infants born prematurely or weighing less than a certain weight. With ROP, abnormal blood vessels grow in the infant\u00e2\u0080\u0099s retina. If left untreated, the retina could become damaged, which may lead to vision loss or even blindness.What are Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Like most drugs, Eylea may cause mild or serious side effects. The following lists describe some of the more common side effects that Eylea may cause. These lists don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t include all possible side effects.Keep in mind that side effects of a drug can depend on:your ageother health conditions you haveother medications you may be takingYour doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about the potential side effects of Eylea and suggest ways to help reduce them.Mild side effectsHere\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a short list of some of the mild side effects that Eylea can cause. To learn about other mild side effects, talk with your doctor or pharmacist, or read Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information.Mild side effects of Eylea that have been reported include:bleeding in the eyeeye painvitreous detachmenteye floatersblurry visionMild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days or a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.For more information about some of these side effects, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Serious side effectsSerious side effects from Eylea can occur, but they typically aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common. (An exception in the list is cataracts, which was one of the more commonly reported side effects of Eylea.) If you have serious side effects from Eylea, call your doctor right away. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Serious side effects of Eylea that have been reported include:retinal tear and detachment, which happens when your retina detaches from the back of your eyeendophthalmitis, which is an infection of the fluids or tissues inside your eyeincreased pressure in your eyeheart or blood vessel problems, such as a stroke*cataracts, which occur when your lens becomes cloudy and doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t let as much light into your eyeallergic reaction*retinal vasculitis, which is inflammation of the retina\u00e2\u0080\u0099s blood vessels, with or without blood vessel blockage\u00e2\u0080 * For more information on this side effect, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.\u00e2\u0080 Though this side effect wasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t reported in studies of Eylea, reports of this side effect did occur after the drug became available.Side effect focusLearn more about some of the side effects Eylea may cause.Heart or blood vessel problems, such as a strokeAfter receiving an Eylea injection, you may have a risk of blood clots. Blood clots can sometimes cause a stroke, heart attack, or a lack of blood flow to certain areas of the body.In studies, these side effects weren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common in people using Eylea.What might helpBefore starting Eylea treatment, discuss the risks of blood clots and symptoms of heart attack and stroke with your doctor.For example, heart attack symptoms can include:pain or discomfort in your chestfeeling weak, lightheaded, or faintbreaking out in a cold sweatpain or discomfort in your jaw, neck, back, or one or both of your armsshortness of breathStroke symptoms can occur suddenly and may include:numbness or weakness in your face, arm, or leg, usually occurring on one side of the bodyconfusion, or difficulty speaking or understanding speechdifficulty with seeing in one or both of your eyesdifficulty walkingdizziness, loss of balance, or lack of coordinationsevere headacheIf you have any of these symptoms after receiving Eylea, seek emergency medical care right away. Call 911 or your local emergency number. Or have someone take you to the nearest emergency room.Seeing floatersAfter receiving Eylea, you may notice squiggly lines or small dark spots in your vision. These lines and spots float across your vision, so they\u00e2\u0080\u0099re called floaters.Often, floaters disappear after a while. And they don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t usually affect your vision.But sometimes, floaters can indicate a serious eye condition such as a retinal tear or detachment. (With retinal detachment, your retina detaches from the back of your eye.) These conditions are possible side effects of Eylea.What might helpMost often, floaters don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t require treatment. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll usually disappear on their own.Tell your doctor if you have symptoms that may suggest a more serious eye condition. Symptoms of a retinal tear or detachment can include:having a lot of new floaters that appear suddenlyseeing flashes of light that appear suddenlyseeing a dark shadowhaving blurred visionBlurry visionAfter receiving an Eylea injection, you may experience blurry vision. This side effect may disappear after a while, but it can also be a symptom of endophthalmitis, which is a possible serious side effect of Eylea.With endophthalmitis, you have a severe infection in the vitreous humor (the clear gel-like substance that fills the posterior portion of the eye).What might helpTo be safe, don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t drive after receiving an Eylea injection. Only drive or use machinery when your vision is no longer blurry.Be sure to tell your doctor right away if you have symptoms of endophthalmitis. In addition to blurry vision, symptoms may include:eye paineye rednesssensitivity to lightIf you have an eye infection, your doctor will treat it as needed. Be sure to tell your doctor if you have blurry vision that doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t go away after getting Eylea injections.Allergic reactionSome people may have an allergic reaction to Eylea. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve had an allergic reaction in the past to aflibercept (the active ingredient in Eylea) or any of the other ingredients in Eylea, you cannot use this medication.Symptoms of a mild allergic reaction can include:skin rashitchinessflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)A more severe allergic reaction is rare but possible. Symptoms of a severe allergic reaction can include swelling under your skin, typically in your eyelids, lips, hands, or feet. Allergic reaction can also cause severe inflammation in the eye. In addition, it can result in swelling of your tongue, mouth, or throat, which can cause difficulty breathing.Call your doctor right away if you have an allergic reaction to Eylea. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number.Eylea injection priceThe costs of prescription drugs can vary depending on many factors. These factors include what your insurance plan covers and whether you get the drug from a pharmacy or your doctor administers it.If you have questions about the cost of your Eylea prescription and how to pay for it, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You can also visit the Eylea manufacturer\u00e2\u0080\u0099s website to see whether it has support options that you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re eligible for.What are some frequently asked questions about Eylea?Find answers to some commonly asked questions about Eylea.Is Eylea similar to either Avastin or Lucentis?Eylea, Avastin, and Lucentis all belong to a group of drugs called vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) inhibitors. But they don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t all have the same uses.Lucentis treats eye conditions similar to those of Eylea. And like Eylea, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s also given as an intravitreal injection, which is an injection into the eye.Avastin, on the other hand, is used for certain types of cancer, such as kidney cancer and colon cancer. Avastin may sometimes be considered for age-related macular degeneration (AMD). But AMD is an off-label use for Avastin. With off-label use, a drug that the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved to treat one condition is prescribed for another condition the FDA has not approved.When used to treat certain types of cancer, Avastin is usually administered by intravenous (IV) infusion, which is an injection into a vein given over a period of time. But when used to treat eye conditions, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s given as an injection into the eye.Eylea, Avastin, and Lucentis all block VEGF. At high levels, VEGF can cause abnormal blood vessels to grow in your eye, resulting in fluid leakage. By blocking VEGF, these drugs can decrease fluid leakage into your macula, which is the center of your retina.What\u00e2\u0080\u0099s the success rate of treatment with Eylea?Success rates with Eylea treatment can differ for each person and for each eye condition being treated.For example, in studies of Eylea, more people with wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD) had their vision preserved than people with macular edema. (For more information about wet AMD and macular edema, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWhat is Eylea used for?\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.)Talk with your doctor to find out Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible success rate for your condition.How does Eylea work?Eylea works by blocking the process that causes blood vessels to leak in the back of your eye. The drug also prevents new blood vessels from forming around your retina.Keep in mind that Eylea doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t cure eye conditions, including wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD). But the drug can slow down the progression of AMD and other conditions, and help you keep your vision.How long does Eylea stay in your system?Eylea can stay in your system for about a month.Eylea HD is a version of Eylea that contains a longer-lasting injectable form of aflibercept. This means that if your doctor prescribes Eylea HD, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive injections less frequently than with Eylea.Note that Eylea HD is not approved to treat all of the same conditions as Eylea, and the two forms are not interchangeable. Your doctor can tell you more about Eylea HD and whether it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you.If you have questions about how long Eylea stays in your system, talk with your doctor.What is Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Your doctor will recommend the dosage of Eylea that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you. This section describes commonly used dosages, but your doctor will determine the dosage you receive.Forms and strengthEylea comes as a solution inside single-use vials and prefilled syringes. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s available in one strength: 2 milligrams (mg) per 0.05 milliliters (mL).Recommended dosagesYour doctor will prescribe an appropriate dosing schedule based on why you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re receiving Eylea. The recommended dose for each injection will be 2 mg/0.05 mL.For example, if you have:Wet age-related macular degeneration (AMD), you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive an Eylea injection in your eye once every 4 weeks (about every 28 days) for the first 3 months of treatment. Then your doctor may recommend that you get a dose once every 8 weeks. But some people may need to stay on a 4-week dosing schedule. After a year of treatment, your doctor may change your dosing schedule to receiving the drug once every 12 weeks.Diabetic retinopathy or diabetic macular edema, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll start Eylea treatment with an injection in your eye once every 4 weeks for the first 5 months. Then your doctor may recommend that you get an injection once every 4 or 8 weeks.Macular edema due to a vein blockage, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive one Eylea injection in your eye once every 4 weeks.An infant receiving treatment for retinopathy of prematurity will have one injection of 0.4 mg/0.01 mL in the affected eye. Their doctor will monitor their condition closely afterward. Treatment may be given to both eyes on the same day as needed, and the doctor may recommend additional injections.For more information about the conditions Eylea is used to treat, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWhat is Eylea used for?\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Questions about Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosingHere are some common questions about Eylea\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosing.What if I miss a dose of Eylea? It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important that you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t miss any doses of Eylea. If you miss an appointment with your doctor to get your dose of the drug, call your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office right away. Their medical staff can help you reschedule your appointment. Keep in mind that stopping Eylea treatment may cause your eye condition to get worse.Will I need to use Eylea long term? The conditions that Eylea treats are long-lasting diseases and may require long-term use of Eylea. (The exception is retinopathy of prematurity, which may get better after just one dose of Eylea.) Ask your doctor how long you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need to use Eylea.Should I take Eylea with food? Eylea is injected into your eye. So how well your body absorbs the drug isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t affected by eating. You can receive Eylea injections on either a full or empty stomach.How long does Eylea take to work? Every person will respond differently to Eylea treatment. Ask your doctor how long you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need to wait before the treatment starts working for you. Your doctor will monitor your vision throughout your treatment. You can also monitor your vision at home using the Amsler grid test.How is Eylea given?Your doctor will explain how you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive Eylea. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll also explain how much you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive and how often. Be sure to follow your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s instructions when receiving doses of Eylea.Receiving EyleaEylea comes as a solution inside single-use vials and prefilled syringes. Your doctor will administer it as an intravitreal injection, which is an injection into your eye.Receiving Eylea with other drugsBefore injecting Eylea into your eye, your doctor will give you medications to numb pain and prevent infection.Talk with your doctor about which drugs they\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll use for these purposes.Questions for your doctorYou may have questions about Eylea and your treatment plan. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to discuss all your concerns with your doctor.Here are a few tips that might help guide your discussion:Before your appointment, write down questions like: How will Eylea affect my body, mood, or lifestyle?Bring someone with you to your appointment if doing so will help you feel more comfortable.If you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t understand something related to your condition or treatment, ask your doctor to explain it to you.Remember, your doctor and other healthcare professionals are available to help you. And they want you to get the best care possible. So, don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t be afraid to ask questions or offer feedback on your treatment.What should be considered before receiving Eylea?Some important things to discuss with your doctor when considering treatment with Eylea include:your overall healthany medical conditions you may haveAlso, be sure to tell your doctor if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re taking any medications, herbs, vitamins, or supplements.InteractionsTaking medications, vaccines, foods, and other things with a certain drug can affect how the drug works. These effects are called interactions.Drug interactions aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t expected with Eylea. And it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unknown which drugs interact with Eylea. But it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s still important to tell your doctor about any medications, herbs, or vitamins you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re using. This is because some of these products may interfere with how well Eylea works.Before starting Eylea, be sure to tell your doctor about all medications you take, including prescription and over-the-counter medications. Also describe any vitamins, herbs, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions these items may cause with Eylea.WarningsEylea may not be right for you if you have certain medical conditions or other factors that affect your health. Talk with your doctor about your health history before you start Eylea treatment. Factors to consider include those in the following list:infection in or around your eyeinflammation in your eyeprevious allergic reaction to Eylea or any of its ingredientsglaucomaheart disease or other risk factors for heart attack or strokeUse with alcoholSome medications interact with alcohol. But Eylea isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t one of them.However, if you drink alcohol, before starting Eylea, ask your doctor or pharmacist if it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safe for you to drink alcohol.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIt\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unknown whether Eylea is harmful if used during pregnancy. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s also unknown whether Eylea passes into breast milk and would harm a child who is breastfed.Talk with your doctor about pregnancy and breastfeeding if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re considering treatment with Eylea.What to ask your doctorIf you have questions about using Eylea, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. They may tell you about other treatments you can use for your condition.Some possible questions to ask your doctor about Eylea treatment include:Will Eylea cure my wet age-related macular degeneration?Can I develop glaucoma by using Eylea?If my diabetes were better managed, could the damage to my eyes be reversed?How can I reduce my anxiety about receiving an Eylea injection into my eye?To learn more about Eylea, see these articles:Side Effects of Eylea: What You Need to KnowEylea and Cost: What You Need to KnowDosage Details for EyleaTo get information on different conditions and tips for improving your health, subscribe to any of Healthline\u00e2\u0080\u0099s newsletters. You may also want to check out the online communities at Bezzy. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a place where people with certain conditions can find support and connect with others.Ask a pharmacistQ: Which vitamins or supplements can I take to help preserve my vision?AnonymousA:Some vitamins and supplements may help preserve your vision and slow the worsening of your vision due to certain eye conditions.Vitamins A, B, C, and E all play an important role in maintaining healthy vision. For instance:Vitamin A helps maintain a clear cornea, which is the outer covering of your eye.Vitamin B1 (thiamine) helps ensure proper cell function, including that of eye cells, and makes energy for the cells in your eyes.Vitamin B2 (riboflavin) acts as an antioxidant, which fights free radicals in your body. (Free radicals are compounds that can cause harm, including harm to your eyes, if their levels are too high in your body.)Vitamin B3 (niacin) acts as an antioxidant and also makes energy for the cells in your eyes.Vitamins B6, B9, and B12 work together to lower levels of homocysteine, which is a protein in your body that may be associated with inflammation, including inflammation in your eyes.Vitamins C and E are powerful antioxidants that may protect your eyes against damaging free radicals.Lutein and zeaxanthin act as antioxidants and help filter potentially harmful blue light, protecting your eyes from damage.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like to know more about vitamins and supplements that help with vision, talk with your doctor. And before taking any vitamins or supplements, always be sure to check with your doctor or pharmacist.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.Disclaimer: Healthline has made every effort to make certain that all information is factually correct, comprehensive, and up to date. However, this article should not be used as a substitute for the knowledge and expertise of a licensed healthcare professional. You should always consult your doctor or another healthcare professional before taking any medication. The drug information contained herein is subject to change and is not intended to cover all possible uses, directions, precautions, warnings, drug interactions, allergic reactions, or adverse effects. The absence of warnings or other information for a given drug does not indicate that the drug or drug combination is safe, effective, or appropriate for all patients or all specific uses.Eylea imagesVIEW GALLERY1", "content_hash": "9a33c50dc7d6a880a199364e50b5cadf5e886ab01842642c7e9182c56c0b390e", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:37.688722+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1367", "title": "Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article", "text": "Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 On behalf of the Federal Government of Nigeria, I thank the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation and the International Association of Deposit Insurers for convening this important gathering at a time when financial systems across the world face both unprecedented opportunities and emerging risks. N NDIC July 22, 2026 6 min read OpeningIt is my distinct pleasure to welcome you all to Abuja for the 2026 IADI Africa Regional Committee Annual Meeting and Workshop. On behalf of the Federal Government of Nigeria, I thank the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation and the International Association of Deposit Insurers for convening this important gathering at a time when financial systems across the world face both unprecedented opportunities and emerging risks.The theme of this workshop \u2013 Safeguarding Stability: Public Awareness and Crisis Readiness for a Stronger Future \u2013 is strategic. It rests on one fundamental truth: there can be no economic growth without financial system stability, and there can be no financial stability without public trust.Stability as the Foundation for GrowthFinancial stability is often discussed in technical terms, yet its impact is felt in the everyday lives of citizens. It affects the ability of businesses to access credit, households to save securely, investors to commit capital, and governments to deliver development programmes. When the public has confidence in financial institutions, savings increase, investment expands, and economic opportunities multiply.Monetary and fiscal policy alone cannot drive prosperity if the financial sector is vulnerable to panic, capital flight, or systemic distress. The banking system is the nervous system of the macroeconomy. When depositors trust that their money is safe, capital flows productively, credit expands, and businesses grow.Deposit Insurance as Financial InfrastructureHistorically, deposit insurance was seen as a technical, back-office mechanism for handling bank liquidations after failure. Guided by the revised IADI Core Principles, specifically Core Principle 10 on Public Awareness and Core Principle 11 on Crisis Preparedness we now recognise deposit insurance for what it truly is: a proactive, strategic engine for public trust and economic stability.Public trust is fragile. In the digital age, rumours and misinformation can spread across social platforms in seconds, creating liquidity shocks even for solvent institutions. If a depositor does not know their funds are protected, they will act on fear. Building public awareness in normal times is not a public-relations exercise; it is a core risk-mitigation strategy, and our messaging must reach every segment of society, from retail depositors and MSMEs to underserved communities in rural areas.Crisis preparedness follows the same logic. It is not about predicting every shock, but about building systems resilient enough to absorb them. Frameworks, communication channels, and roles must already exist before uncertainty arrives; simulation exercises and coordination mechanisms must already be functioning. Preparedness is therefore not an event, it is a culture. The most successful crisis response is often the one that never becomes visible, because effective preparation prevented panic from occurring in the first place. That requires seamless, one-voice coordination among the Ministry of Finance, the Central Bank, the Deposit Insurance Corporation, and oversight bodies, so that when a crisis hits, depositors retain swift, certain access to their funds.Nigeria\u2019s Reform JourneyNigeria\u2019s reform record speaks directly to the principles this workshop advances. Under the economic reform agenda of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu\u2019s administration, we have pursued a comprehensive programme of fiscal and financial transformation: unifying the foreign exchange market, removing a distortionary fuel subsidy, and ending the Central Bank\u2019s unsustainable Ways and Means financing of government deficits \u2013 restoring a critical boundary between fiscal and monetary policy.Additionally, two important developments bear directly on this audience\u2019s mandate. First, in March 2026, the Central Bank concluded its two-year banking sector recapitalisation exercise. Thirty-three of Nigeria\u2019s thirty-seven banks met the revised minimum capital requirements ranging from \u20a6500 billion for internationally authorised banks to \u20a650 billion for regional banks raising a combined \u20a64.65 trillion (over USD3.5 Billion) in fresh capital, over 70 per cent of it from domestic investors. Capital adequacy ratios across the sector now exceed Basel benchmarks, and all banks continued to operate normally throughout, with no disruption to customer access. A better-capitalised banking system is a more resilient one, better able to absorb shocks and sustain lending without recourse to the deposit insurance fund. For deposit insurance, the significance is direct: stronger bank balance sheets mean a stronger financial safety net.Second, in October 2025, Nigeria was officially removed from the Financial Action Task Force grey list, a designation that had constrained our financial system since February 2023. This was the product of two years of sustained, coordinated reform across our Financial Intelligence Unit, the Central Bank, the EFCC, and the Ministry of Justice \u2013 strengthening our anti-money laundering framework, operationalising a national beneficial ownership register, and improving inter-agency coordination. A financial system credible in the eyes of the world is one in which depositors are more likely to place, and keep, their confidence.Deposit Insurance and Inclusive GrowthDeposit insurance does more than protect savings, it supports financial inclusion. When people trust financial institutions, they save more; when savings increase, banks lend more; when lending expands, businesses invest and jobs are created. This matters enormously across Africa, where expanding financial inclusion remains one of our greatest opportunities for accelerating inclusive growth.A Continental ImperativeAfrica\u2019s financial landscape is evolving rapidly. Cross-border banking, fintech innovation, and digital payment rails mean instability no longer respects geographical borders, even as the African Continental Free Trade Area opens enormous opportunities for trade and investment. Realising them requires financial systems resilient enough to manage emerging risks together.This is why platforms like the IADI Africa Regional Committee matter: they align our frameworks with international best practice while adapting them to African realities. And Africa should not merely adopt global standards, we should help shape them. Our populations are younger, our mobile money penetration is among the highest in the world, and our experience navigating financial inclusion at scale offers lessons for the global community. No single institution preserves financial stability alone \u2013 central banks, deposit insurers, supervisors, finance ministries, resolution authorities, and the media each have a role to play, and our coordination must be as seamless as the crises we prepare for.ConclusionLet me close with one simple thought: confidence cannot be legislated, purchased, or imposed. It must be earned \u2013 through strong institutions, transparency, effective communication, preparedness, and consistent action. The stronger our institutions, the greater the confidence they inspire; the greater the confidence, the more resilient our financial systems become; and the more resilient our financial systems, the stronger our economies and the greater the prosperity we can create for our people.I commend the International Association of Deposit Insurers, the Africa Regional Committee, and the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation for convening this important dialogue.Over the next few days, as you deliberate on how to operationalise IADI Core Principles 10 and 11, I urge you to keep the ultimate beneficiary in mind: the ordinary African citizen.Every framework you refine, every simulation you run, and every communication strategy you design protects the savings of a small business owner, the salary of a worker, and the financial integrity of our nations.I wish you fruitful, insightful, and impact-driven deliberations.On this note, it is my honour to declare the 2026 IADI Africa Regional Committee Workshop officially open.God bless the Federal Republic of Nigeria, God bless your respective nations; and God bless Africa.Thank you. All Articles Share More Articles July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks June 15, 2026 Sale of Chattels of Closed Primary Mortgage Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid. Browse all articles", "content_hash": "45ddf5f6327ffb6656b1e47b42ac82af63061b47d46a54cbd923ead52ad22d92", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:38.459520+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1368", "title": "Repatha (Evolocumab): Uses, Side Effects, Dosage, and Alternatives", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/repatha", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/repatha", "text": "Key takeaways Repatha is used to help reduce the risk of heart attack, stroke, and heart surgery for adults with risk factors for heart disease. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s also used to lower cholesterol levels in adults and children with specific genetic conditions causing high cholesterol. Common side effects of Repatha may include respiratory infections, urinary tract infections, and injection site reactions. Serious side effects could involve high blood pressure and increased blood sugar levels. Adults with heart disease may receive Repatha via injection, with dosage varying by condition. Or they may use it alone or combined with other cholesterol-lowering medications like statins. Repatha (evolocumab) is a prescription drug that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used in certain situations to decrease serious heart-related risks and lower cholesterol. Repatha comes as a liquid solution for injection under your skin.Doctors prescribe Repatha to:decrease the risk of heart attack or stroke and decrease the need for heart surgery in some adultsdecrease LDL cholesterol in adults and some children with high cholesterolFor some uses, doctors may prescribe Repatha together with a low fat diet and other medications. Repatha basicsRepatha is a biologic medication. Biologics are made from parts of living organisms.The active ingredient in Repatha is evolocumab. (An active ingredient is what makes a medication work.) Repatha isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t available in a biosimilar form. (Biosimilars are like generic drugs. But unlike generics, which are made for non-biologic drugs, biosimilars are made for biologic drugs.)Repatha side effectsLike most drugs, Repatha may cause mild or serious side effects. The following lists describe some of the side effects that Repatha may cause. For a full list of all side effects reported with Repatha, see the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information.Mild side effectsSerious side effects\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 upper respiratory infection, such as influenza (the flu) or the common cold\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 urinary tract infection (UTI)\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 bruising, discoloration, and pain at the injection site\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 back pain\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 joint pain\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 muscle spasm\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 mild allergic reaction\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 high blood pressure\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 increased blood sugar levels, which may lead to diabetes\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 serious allergic reactionThe side effects of Repatha may vary depending on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re using it to treat. For a more in-depth guide, see this article on Repatha\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects and how to manage them. You can also talk with your doctor or pharmacist.How much does Repatha cost?Whether you have health insurance or not, cost may be a factor when you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re considering Repatha. What you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll pay for Repatha may depend on several things, such as your treatment plan and the pharmacy you use.Here are things to consider regarding cost:Comparing pharmacies: The price of Repatha may vary depending on which pharmacy you use, so it can help to compare prices across pharmacies to find the lowest cost. Drug coupons: You may be able to find drug coupons on prescription discount websites that can reduce the cost of your medication. These coupons cannot be used with insurance copays or benefits, but the discounted price may be lower than what you would pay through insurance.Financial assistance: Some websites provide details about drug assistance programs, ways to make the most of your insurance coverage, and links to savings cards and other services. Two such websites are: Medicine Assistance ToolNeedyMeds\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Does Medicare Cover Repatha?How does Repatha work?Repatha is a type of cholesterol-lowering medication called a PCSK9 inhibitor. It works by targeting a specific protein in your liver that typically stops your body from getting rid of \u00e2\u0080\u009cbad\u00e2\u0080\u009d LDL cholesterol. By attaching to the PCSK9 and blocking it, Repatha allows your liver to clear cholesterol from your blood more effectively. This process lowers your overall LDL levels, which can help reduce your risk of serious heart issues like heart attacks or strokes.\u00c2\u00bbMore details:How Repatha WorksWhat is Repatha\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Repatha comes in prefilled, single-dose auto-injectors called Repatha SureClick. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s given as an injection under your skin.The typical recommended dosage of Repatha is:140 milligram (mg) every 2 weeks, or420 mg every monthThis dosage is the same for adults and children. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that the dosage your doctor prescribes will depend on several factors, including your specific condition and how your body responds to Repatha. If you have questions about your dosage, talk with your doctor.More detailsTo learn more about Repatha\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosing and administration, take a look at these articles:Dosage Details for Repatha (Evolocumab)Best Time of Day to Inject RepathaCan I Inject Repatha a Day Early?Are there alternatives to Repatha?Yes, depending on your condition, other treatment options may be available. Talk with your doctor for details about other treatments for your heart health and cholesterol levels, including:inclisiran (Leqvio)alirocumab (Praluent)atorvastatin (Lipitor)pravastatinrosuvastatin (Crestor)ezetimibe (Zetia)fenofibrate (Antara, Lipofen)niacin (Niacor)The best treatment for you will depend on your personal health factors. Your doctor can help you weigh the pros and cons of Repatha or another medication. The list below includes things to keep in mind. Why Repatha may be right for youRepatha can be self-administered at home. Some other injection medications can only be given by a healthcare professional in their office.Repatha is approved for use in adults and some children, while some medications may only be approved for adults.Some medications need to be taken daily. Repatha is injected once a month or every other week, so there are fewer doses to keep track of.Why Repatha may not be right for youRepatha is only available as an injection. Some people may prefer capsules or tablets instead.Some forms of Repatha contain latex. If you have a latex allergy, be sure to let your doctor know. Repatha is not available as a biosimilar or generic, so some medications may cost less.What should be considered before using Repatha?Before you start Repatha, talk with your doctor about your treatment plan. Some health factors can affect how your body responds to Repatha, either making the drug less effective or increasing the risk of serious side effects.Be sure to discuss:your overall healthany other medical conditions you haveany other medications you takewhether you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re pregnant, breastfeeding, or planning for either Your doctor will let you know whether Repatha is a safe and effective treatment option for you.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Repatha Interactions: Alcohol, Medications, and OthersWhat to ask your doctorIf you have heart disease or high cholesterol, your doctor may recommend Repatha.If you have questions about taking Repatha or you wonder whether it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s an option for you, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. Here are some questions you may wish to ask:What side effects might I have with Repatha based on my condition? And how can I treat them?How long should I expect side effects from Repatha to last?What should I do if I\u00e2\u0080\u0099m having difficulty injecting doses of Repatha?What should I do if I become pregnant while I\u00e2\u0080\u0099m receiving Repatha?Read more about treatment options for high cholesterol. Also, learn about injectable alternatives to statins and more statin alternatives.To learn more about Repatha, see these articles:Dosage Details for RepathaRepatha and Price: Reducing Long-Term Drug Costs and MoreSide Effects of Repatha: What You Need to KnowRepatha Interactions: Alcohol, Medications, and OthersCan You Take Repatha While Pregnant or Breastfeeding?Does Repatha Suppress the Immune System?To get information on different conditions and tips for improving your health, subscribe to any of Healthline\u00e2\u0080\u0099s newsletters. You may also want to check out the online communities at Bezzy. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a place where people with certain conditions can find support and connect with others.Ask a pharmacistQ: If I\u00e2\u0080\u0099m taking Repatha with another cholesterol-lowering drug, such as a statin, do I have an increased risk of side effects?AnonymousA:It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible. Taking Repatha with a statin may increase the risk of certain side effects that can be caused by either drug. For example, both Repatha and statins may cause muscle pain.But most people who took Repatha in studies also took statins or other cholesterol medications. And many of these people took the combination without severe side effects.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re concerned about your risk of side effects with Repatha, talk with your doctor. Also, be sure to tell them about all of your current medications before starting Repatha.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.TakeawayRepatha is a prescription injection that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribed to reduce the risk of heart attacks and strokes in adults with higher risks of heart problems. Doctors also prescribe it for adults and children over 10 who have specific genetic conditions that cause naturally high cholesterol. Repatha can cause mild side effects like cold symptoms or soreness at the injection site, but serious reactions are rare. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re managing heart risks or high cholesterol, Repatha could be a helpful option to discuss with your doctor.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Repatha imagesVIEW GALLERY2", "content_hash": "9f212d53f556d4cef0ace9cc875fc6a5e2d90c98ce157fa0667977b0be26da11", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:40.054987+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1369", "title": "NDIC\n                                                Articles", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/articles", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/articles", "text": "NDIC Articles Expert insights, opinion pieces, and in-depth analysis from NDIC on deposit insurance, banking stability and depositor protection. Sort by date All articles Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 22, 2026 speech On behalf of the Federal Government of Nigeria, I thank the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation and the International Association of Deposit Insurers for convening this important gathering at a time when financial systems across the world face both unprecedented opportunities and emerging risks. MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 21, 2026 Speech This year\u2019s theme, \u201cSafeguarding Stability: Public Awareness and Crisis Readiness for a Stronger Future,\u201d NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 Feature Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria July 1, 2026 Announcement Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks June 19, 2026 Announcement Sale of Chattels of Closed Primary Mortgage Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid. June 15, 2026 Announcement NDIC and Nile University, Immersion Challenge, Business School Students May 21, 2026 Announcement Disposal of Landed Property, Microfinance Banks (In-Liquidation) April 16, 2026 Announcement Resolution of Failed Banks: NDIC Commences Process to Conclude the Liquidation of 89 MFBs & PMB April 15, 2026 Announcement Notice of Intention to Terminate Liquidation Activities April 8, 2026 Featured Sale of Assets of Closed Micro Finance Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid February 11, 2026 Announcement NDIC, NIESV Strengthen Partnership on Failed Bank Asset Valuation December 2, 2025 Press Release GENERAL PROCUREMENT ACTIVITIES FOR 2025 September 1, 2025 Announcement NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC IN RESPECT OF HOUSING ESTATES FORMERLY ACQUIRED BY AHOCOL SAVINGS AND LOANS LTD. (IN-LIQUIDATION) August 26, 2025 Announcement NOTICE TO BENEFICIARIES, ALLOTTEES AND GENERAL PUBLIC IN RESPECT OF SOME HOUSING ESTATES FORMERLY ACQUIRED BY AHOCOL SAVINGS AND LOANS LTD. (IN-LIQUIDATION) DISPOSAL OF HARBOUR TUG BOAT OCEAN LEGACY- MARINE VESSEL FOR THE DEFUNCT HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) July 28, 2025 Announcement NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC FOR THE DISPOSAL OF HARBOUR TUG BOAT OCEAN LEGACY-MARINE VESSEL FOR THE DEFUNCT HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) LOCATED AT BONNY RIVER, PORTHARCOURT RIVERS STATE. NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC FOR DISPOSAL OF LANDED PROPERTY AND OTHER PHYSICAL ASSETS OF HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) July 28, 2025 Announcement Wale Edun Inaugurates New NDIC Management July 27, 2025 Announcement NOTICE TO CREDITORS OF DEFUNCT COMMERCIAL TRUST BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) July 10, 2025 Announcement The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), the Official Liquidator of the underlisted defunct bank (in-liquidation), is in the process of paying liquidation dividends to the defunct bank\u2019s Creditors; Notice to General Public for Disposal of Properties Belonging to Fortune Bank (IN-LIQ), United Commercial Bank (IN -LIQ) and Heritage Bank (IN-LIQ) July 3, 2025 Announcement NDIC HAS COMMENCED PAYMENT OF \u20a646.6 BILLION AS FIRST TRANCHE OF LIQUIDATION DIVIDENDS TO DEPOSITORS WITH FUNDS ABOVE THE INSURED LIMIT April 28, 2025 Featured The 2025 Stakeholders Workshop of the House Committee on Insurance and Actuarial Matters With the NDIC April 25, 2025 Announcement NDIC MD/CEO Addresses 2024 Management Workshop January 10, 2025 Speech KEYNOTE ADDRESS BY THE MANAGING DIRECTOR/CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER, NDIC, MR. BELLO HASSAN, OON, FCA, FCIB, AT THE 2024 MANAGEMENT WORKSHOP FOR SENIOR MANAGEMENT AND EXECUTIVE STAFF OF THE CORPORATION IN COLLABORATION WITH THE BUREAU OF PUBLIC PROCUREMENT (BPP) HOLDING AT BRISTOL PALACE HOTEL, KANO BETWEEN 9TH \u2013 11TH JANUARY 2025 Invitation to Tender for the Supply of Vehicles For the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation December 10, 2024 Announcement Invitation to Tender for the Supply of Desktop and Laptop Computers for the NDIC December 10, 2024 Announcement MD/CE of NDIC Opening Speech at FICAN 2023 November 29, 2024 Speech ADDRESS BY THE MANAGING DIRECTOR/CHIEF EXECUTIVE, NIGERIA DEPOSIT INSURANCE CORPORATION (NDIC), MR. BELLO HASSAN, AT THE OPENING CEREMONY OF THE 20TH EDITION OF THE WORKSHOP FOR BUSINESS EDITORS AND MEMBERS OF THE FINANCE CORRESPONDENTS ASSOCIATION OF NIGERIA (FICAN) HELD AT PROTEA HOTEL, OWERRI, IMO STATE ON WEDNESDAY 29TH NOVEMBER 2023 Invitation to Tender for the Supply and Installation of Battery Bank for the Solar Power System for NDIC Kano Zonal Offices November 27, 2024 Announcement Sale of Assets of Closed Micro Finance Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid November 26, 2024 Announcement Notice to General Public Disposal of Landed Property and Other Physical Assets of Heritage Bank (IN-LIQ) November 26, 2024 Announcement NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC FOR DISPOSAL OF LANDED PROPERTY AND OTHER PHYSICAL ASSETS OF HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) November 11, 2024 Announcement NDIC Commences Auction of Landed Properties, Chattels of Defunct Heritage Bank (In-Liq) November 10, 2024 Announcement Notice to the General Public on the Disposal of Physical Assets of Heritage Bank (IN-LIQ) October 4, 2024 Announcement NDIC Invites Expression of Interest from Legal Advisers and Management Consultants for Strategic Organisational Restructuring October 4, 2024 Announcement INVITATION TO TENDER FOR THE SUPPLY AND INSTALLATION OF IP-CCTV SECURITY SURVEILLANCE SYSTEM FOR (NDIC) LAGOS OFFICE September 3, 2024 Announcement UPDATE ON PAYMENT TO DEPOSITORS OF HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) August 12, 2024 Announcement NDIC COMMENCES LIQUIDATION OF HERITAGE BANK June 3, 2024 Announcement SALE OF ASSETS OF CLOSED MICRO FINANCE BANKS BY PUBLIC AUCTION AND PUBLIC COMPETITIVE BID May 14, 2024 Announcement INVITATION FOR EXPRESSION OF INTEREST (EOI) FOR THE VALUATION OF A MULTI-STOREY BUILDING May 14, 2024 Announcement NOTICE TO DEPOSITORS OF CLOSED ULTIMATE BENEFIT MICROFINANCE BANK (MFB) February 15, 2024 Announcement SALE OF ASSETS OF CLOSED MICRO FINANCE BANKS BY PUBLIC AUCTION AND PUBLIC COMPETITIVE BID February 13, 2024 Announcement NOTICE TO DEPOSITORS OF CLOSED FORTIS MICROFINANCE BANK (MFB) December 8, 2023 NOTICE TO DEPOSITORS OF FORTUNE INTERNATIONAL BANK & IDUMUJE MFB (IN-LIQUIDATION) July 6, 2023 NDIC ADDRESSES ALLEGATIONS OF FINANCIAL IMPROPRIETY INVOLVING STAFF MEMBER June 25, 2023 Announcement NDIC SEEKS STAKEHOLDERS' INPUTS \u2014 DIFFERENTIAL PREMIUM ASSESSMENT SYSTEM FRAMEWORK June 5, 2023 Press Release REQUEST FOR EXPRESSION OF INTEREST FOR THE ACQUISITION OF ELECTRONIC DOCUMENT MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (EDMS) FOR NDIC May 31, 2023 Announcement NOTICE TO DEPOSITORS OF RECENTLY CLOSED MICROFINANCE BANKS (MFBs) AND FOUR PRIMARY MORTGAGE BANKS (PMBs) May 25, 2023 Announcement NDIC ASSURES SPEEDY PAYMENT OF CLAIMS TO DEPOSITORS OF CLOSED MFBs AND PMBS May 23, 2023 Announcement NDIC Lauds Judiciary Solicitors on Diligent Prosecution of Failed Bank Cases May 3, 2023 Announcement MD/CE Speech at NDIC\u2019S Special Day at the 34th Enugu International Trade Fair March 31, 2023 Speech SPEECH DELIVERED BY THE MANAGING DIRECTOR/CHIEF EXECUTIVE (MD/CE), NIGERIA DEPOSIT INSURANCE CORPORATION (NDIC), MR BELLO HASSAN, ON THE OCCASION OF NDIC\u2019S SPECIAL DAY AT THE 34TH ENUGU INTERNATIONAL TRADE FAIR ON THURSDAY 30TH MARCH, 2023 NDIC Emerges as ITF 2022 Best Contributing Employer in Human Resources Development March 27, 2023 Announcement Invitation to Tender for the Supply and Installation of Hyper Convergence Infrastructure March 21, 2023 Announcement Invitation to Tender for the Supply and Installation of Helpdesk Software March 7, 2023 Announcement NDIC's MD/CE Keynote Speech at 19th Edition FICAN 2022 January 3, 2023 Speech Address by the MD/CE of NDIC at the 43rd Kano International Trade Fair 2022 December 9, 2022 Public Statement ADDRESS BY THE MANAGING DIRECTOR/CHIEF EXECUTIVE, NIGERIA DEPOSIT INSURANCE CORPORATION (NDIC), MR. BELLO HASSAN DURING THE CORPORATION\u2019S SPECIAL DAY AT THE 43RD KANO INTERNATIONAL TRADE FAIR ON THURSDAY 8TH DECEMBER, 2022 Stakeholders Canvass Support for NDIC ACT Amendment Bill December 8, 2022 Announcement NDIC Critical to Financial Inclusion Achievement Showcased at the International Financial Inclusion Conference 2022 November 16, 2022 Press", "content_hash": "120a9120296c667b4df401a7f1171054a159a28fafad19646fd9360c5eca4219", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:41.134826+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1370", "title": "Rexulti (Brexpiprazole) Overview", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/rexulti", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/rexulti", "text": "Key takeaways Rexulti is a prescription medication used to treat certain mental health conditions, such as depression. This drug can cause side effects, including weight gain, sleepiness, and feeling restless. More serious side effects are possible with Rexulti, but these are not common. Rexulti can interact with some medications, such as certain antibiotics. Rexulti is used to treat the following:depression (also known as major depressive disorder) in adults when taken with an antidepressantschizophrenia in adults and certain childrenagitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease in adultsFor the type of agitation the drug is prescribed to treat, Rexulti is meant to be taken daily. A person should not take it only when they\u2019re experiencing agitation.To learn more about Rexulti\u2019s uses, see the \u201cIs Rexulti used for depression?\u201d and \u201cDoes Rexulti have other uses?\u201d sections.Note: As a person\u2019s condition progresses, they may need help reading or understanding certain information about their treatment plan. This article contains details that may help caregivers learn more about key aspects of Rexulti.Rexulti medication basicsRexulti contains the active ingredient brexpiprazole. (An active ingredient is what makes a drug work.) Rexulti is not available as a generic drug.Based on studies, Rexulti was found to be safe and effective for treating depression, schizophrenia, and agitation from dementia caused by Alzheimer\u2019s disease. What are Rexulti\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Like most drugs, Rexulti may cause mild or serious side effects. The lists that follow describe some of the more common side effects. These lists do not include all possible side effects. Your doctor or pharmacist can provide complete side effect information about Rexulti.Keep in mind that side effects of a drug can depend on:your ageother health conditions you haveother medications you may be takingYour doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about the potential side effects of Rexulti. They can also suggest ways to help reduce side effects.Note: After the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approves a drug, it tracks and reviews side effects of the medication. Sharing your experience helps make medications safer for everyone by giving doctors and researchers more information about how the drug works in real life. If you develop a side effect while taking Rexulti and want to tell the FDA about it, visit MedWatch or call 800-332-1088.Mild side effectsHere\u2019s a short list of some of the mild side effects that Rexulti can cause. To learn about other mild side effects, talk with your doctor or pharmacist, or read Rexulti\u2019s prescribing information.Mild side effects of Rexulti that have been reported include:weight gainsleepinessakathisia (feeling restless)nasopharyngitis (the common cold)headacheconstipationstrange dreams or insomnia (difficulty sleeping)tirednessMild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days to a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Serious side effectsSerious side effects from Rexulti can occur, but they are not common. If you have serious side effects from Rexulti, call your doctor right away. However, if you think you\u2019re having a medical emergency, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Serious side effects of Rexulti that have been reported include:sexual side effects, such as compulsive behaviors including sexual urgesproblems with your metabolism, including type 2 diabetes and issues with lipids (fats)increased risk of stroketardive dyskinesia, a disorder that causes involuntary movementsneuroleptic malignant syndrome (NMS), a rare side effect that causes fast heart rate, high fever, and muscle rigiditylow white blood cell levelorthostatic hypotension (sudden drop in blood pressure when you\u2019re standing up), which can lead to syncope (fainting) and fallsseizuresdifficulty regulating body temperaturedifficulty swallowingslowed thinking or reflexes, which may cause problems while driving or operating heavy machineryboxed warnings: increased risk of death in older adults with psychosis related to dementiasuicidal thoughts or behavior in children and adults ages 24 years and youngerallergic reaction, which was not reported in studies of Rexulti, but can still occurFor more information on Rexulti\u2019s boxed warnings and allergic reaction, see the \u201cSide effect focus\u201d section.Note: If you have symptoms of a serious side effect such as NMS, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Side effect focusLearn more about some of the side effects Rexulti may cause.Boxed warningsRexulti has boxed warnings. These are serious warnings about a medication from the Food and Drug Administration (FDA). Rexulti\u2019s boxed warnings are described here.Risk of death in older adults with psychosis related to dementia: Typically, Rexulti should not be used in older adults (ages 65 years and older) who have psychosis related to dementia. But Rexulti may be prescribed to older adults with dementia for treating agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease. (For more information about this use, see the \u201cDoes Rexulti have other uses?\u201d section.)With psychosis, you may experience impaired mental well-being. Symptoms can include:hallucinations (seeing or hearing things that are not really there)delusions (false beliefs)depressionanxietyWith dementia, you have changes in your mental status. These changes can include:memory lossalterations in your language, thinking, speech, or behaviorRexulti may increase the risk of death in older people who have psychosis related to dementia. Causes of death in studies of older people with this condition were mainly due to cardiovascular (heart and blood vessel) problems or infections.Risk of suicidal thoughts or behaviors: Antidepressant medications can increase suicidal thoughts and behaviors in children and adults ages 24 years and younger. Rexulti is not considered an antidepressant (it\u2019s classified as an atypical antipsychotic). But it\u2019s used to treat depression when taken together with an antidepressant.The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has not approved Rexulti for treating depression in children. But it may be prescribed to children ages 13 years and older for schizophrenia.If you\u2019ve ever had thoughts of self-harm, talk with your doctor before taking Rexulti. They can discuss the risks of Rexulti treatment with you.What might helpIt\u2019s not clear why Rexulti may increase the risk of death in older adults with psychosis related to dementia. Keep in mind that other things can affect this risk. This includes having other health conditions or taking other medications. If you\u2019re concerned about this risk, ask your doctor about the safety of taking Rexulti.Rexulti can also increase the risk of suicidal thoughts or behavior. This risk is higher in people who have had a mental health condition, such as depression or bipolar disorder.Be sure to share your medical history with your doctor before taking Rexulti. Tell them your health history, including whether you\u2019ve had any suicidal thoughts or behaviors in the past.Help is out thereIf you or someone you know is in crisis and considering suicide or self-harm, please seek support:Call or text the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at 988 or chat at 988lifeline.org. Caring counselors are available to listen and provide free and confidential support 24/7.Text HOME to the Crisis Text Line at 741741 to connect with a volunteer crisis counselor for free and confidential support 24/7.Not in the United States? Find a helpline in your country with Befrienders Worldwide.Call 911 or your local emergency services number if you feel safe to do so.If you\u2019re calling on behalf of someone else, stay with them until help arrives. You may remove weapons or substances that can cause harm if you can do so safely.If you\u2019re not in the same household, stay on the phone with them until help arrives.Allergic reactionSome people may have an allergic reaction to Rexulti. While allergic reaction was not reported in studies of Rexulti, it can still happen.Symptoms of a mild allergic reaction can include:skin rashitchinessflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)A more severe allergic reaction is rare but possible. Symptoms of a severe allergic reaction can include swelling under your skin, typically in your eyelids, lips, hands, or feet. They can also include swelling of your tongue, mouth, or throat, which can cause you to have difficulty breathing.Call your doctor right away if you have an allergic reaction to Rexulti. But if you think you\u2019re having a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number.Is Rexulti used for depression?If you have depression, your doctor may suggest Rexulti as a treatment option. To learn more about its use for depression, read on. For information about other conditions Rexulti is prescribed to treat, see the section that directly follows.Rexulti is used in adults with major depressive disorder (MDD), which is also commonly called depression.Brief periods of sadness are natural for everyone. But with depression, you have ongoing, intense feelings of sadness. These feelings affect your quality of life, sleep, and other aspects of your life.For MDD, Rexulti is prescribed together with an antidepressant. This is considered combination therapy.Rexulti belongs to a group of drugs called second-generation antipsychotics, also called atypical antipsychotics. These are newer drugs that have fewer serious side effects than older antipsychotic drugs. It\u2019s thought that Rexulti works for depression by helping to balance certain chemicals in your brain.For more information, talk with your doctor about the pros and cons of using Rexulti for MDD.Does Rexulti have other uses?If you have schizophrenia or agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease, your doctor may discuss Rexulti as a treatment for your condition. (Rexulti is also prescribed to treat depression. To learn more about this use, see the section preceding this one.)Rexulti for schizophreniaRexulti is used to treat schizophrenia, which is a complex mental health condition. For this purpose, doctors prescribe the drug to adults and children ages 13 years and older.Schizophrenia has varying symptoms, including:intrusive thoughtsmovement disordershallucinations (seeing or hearing things that are not really there)agitationsleep problemsdisorganized speechResearch suggests that people with schizophrenia have imbalances in brain chemicals called neurotransmitters. It\u2019s thought that Rexulti works by regulating levels of two neurotransmitters: dopamine and serotonin.Your doctor can provide more information to you about the benefits and risks of Rexulti use for schizophrenia.Rexulti for agitationRexulti is used to treat agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease in adults.With agitation, you have feelings of restlessness, irritability, and worry. Many things can cause agitation, such as being in stressful situations, taking certain medications, or having certain medical conditions.Doctors prescribe Rexulti to treat agitation specifically resulting from dementia caused by Alzheimer\u2019s disease. Dementia is a condition that causes problems with thinking, memory, and communication. Alzheimer\u2019s disease is a type of dementia that worsens over time. It\u2019s usually diagnosed in adults ages 65 years and older.For this use, Rexulti is meant to be taken daily. A person should not take it only when they\u2019re experiencing agitation.It\u2019s not known how Rexulti works to treat agitation. It\u2019s thought that the drug\u2019s regulation of levels of two neurotransmitters (brain chemicals), dopamine and serotonin, may help ease agitation.What is Rexulti\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Your doctor will recommend the dosage of Rexulti that\u2019s right for you. This section describes commonly used dosages, but always take the dosage your doctor prescribes.Form and strengthsRexulti comes as oral tablets. It\u2019s available in these strengths:0.25 milligrams (mg)0.5 mg1 mg2 mg3 mg4 mgRecommended dosagesYour dosage of Rexulti will depend on:the condition you\u2019re taking Rexulti to treatyour agehow well your body responds to the drugother medications you may be takingany Rexulti side effects that you developother health conditions you have, such as liver or kidney problemshow well your body breaks down certain medicationsThe dosages of Rexulti discussed in the next sections are prescribed for adults. For dosages prescribed for children, see the \u201cChildren\u2019s dosage\u201d section.Dosage for depressionFor depression, you\u2019ll take Rexulti once each day, along with another depression medication.Your doctor will start you on a low dose of Rexulti, such as 0.5 mg, and they\u2019ll monitor your body\u2019s response to treatment. After your first few weeks of treatment, your doctor will likely increase your Rexulti dosage.The maximum dosage of Rexulti for depression is 3 mg once daily.Dosage for schizophreniaFor schizophrenia, you\u2019ll take a low dose, usually 1 mg, of Rexulti once daily on days 1 to 4 of treatment. Then your doctor will increase your daily dose to 2 mg for days 5 to 7. If needed, they may increase your daily dose more, starting on day 8.The maximum dosage for schizophrenia is 4 mg once daily.Dosage for agitationFor agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease, you\u2019ll take a low dose, usually 0.5 mg, of Rexulti once daily for days 1 to 7 of treatment. Then your doctor will increase your daily dose to 1 mg for days 8 to 14 of treatment. If needed, they may increase your daily dose more, starting on day 15.The maximum dosage for agitation is 3 mg once daily.Children\u2019s dosageDoctors may prescribe Rexulti for treating schizophrenia in children ages 13 years and older. For this purpose, your child will take a low dose, usually 0.5 mg, of Rexulti once daily for 4 days. Then their doctor will increase their daily dose to 1 mg for days 5 to 7. If needed, they may increase your child\u2019s daily dose more, starting on day 8.The maximum children\u2019s dosage for schizophrenia is 4 mg once daily.How is Rexulti taken?Rexulti is a tablet that you take by swallowing. Taking Rexulti with other drugsFor depression, Rexulti is taken together with an antidepressant. Examples of antidepressant drugs that may be used with Rexulti include:paroxetine (Paxil)sertraline (Zoloft)venlafaxine (Effexor XR)vortioxetine (Trintellix)duloxetine (Cymbalta)For schizophrenia, Rexulti may be taken on its own or with other drugs. For agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease, Rexulti is typically taken on its own.Talk with your doctor to learn about your treatment plan and recommended medications.Questions about taking RexultiHere\u2019s a list of common questions related to taking Rexulti.What if I miss a dose of Rexulti? If you miss a dose of Rexulti, take it as soon as you remember. But do not double up on your next dose. Doing so can increase the risk of side effects from Rexulti. If it\u2019s close to when you\u2019d take your next dose, you should just skip the missed dose. Then you should take your usual dose at your regular time. You can also try using a reminder tool to stay on track with your doses.Will I need to use Rexulti long term? There\u2019s no specific timeline for using Rexulti. You and your doctor will discuss your treatment plan. If Rexulti is working to reduce your symptoms, you may take it long term.Can Rexulti be chewed, crushed, or split? No, you should take Rexulti tablets whole. Crushing, chewing, or splitting the tablets may change how they work in your body. If you have difficulty taking Rexulti, try these tips for how to swallow pills. Or ask your doctor or pharmacist for suggestions on making Rexulti easier to take.Should I take Rexulti with food? You can take Rexulti with or without food. Eating around the time of your doses does not change how the drug works in your body.How long does Rexulti take to work? It may take a few days to several weeks for Rexulti to start reducing your symptoms. How quickly the drug works depends on individual factors, such as your condition and how your body responds to Rexulti. Ask your doctor what you can expect with treatment.Questions for your doctorYou may have questions about Rexulti and your treatment plan. It\u2019s important to discuss all your concerns with your doctor.Here are a few tips that might help guide your discussion:Before your appointment, write down questions like: How will Rexulti affect my body, mood, or lifestyle?Bring someone with you to your appointment if doing so will help you feel more comfortable.If you do not understand something related to your condition or treatment, ask your doctor to explain it to you.Remember, your doctor and other healthcare professionals are available to help you. They want you to get the best care possible, so do not be afraid to ask questions or offer feedback on your treatment.What should I know about Rexulti vs. Abilify?Rexulti and Abilify both belong to a group of drugs called atypical antipsychotics, also referred to as second-generation antipsychotics. These are newer drugs that have fewer serious side effects than older antipsychotic drugs (called first-generation antipsychotics).Rexulti and Abilify have some similar uses and effects, but they also have some differences. For instance, Rexulti contains the active ingredient brexpiprazole, while Abilify contains the active ingredient aripiprazole. (An active ingredient is what makes a drug work.)Rexulti and Abilify are used to treat depression and schizophrenia. (For depression, Rexulti or Abilify is taken with an antidepressant.) But both drugs are also used to treat other conditions.Rexulti comes as an oral tablet. Abilify also comes as an oral tablet.Two other forms of Abilify are available under the brand names Abilify Maintena and Abilify Asimtufii. These are both extended-release liquid suspensions for injection into muscle. \u201cExtended release\u201d means the drug is slowly released into your body over a long period of time. And \u201cliquid suspension\u201d is a type of liquid mixture. (Abilify Maintena and Abilify Asimtufii are not used for all the conditions Abilify is prescribed to treat.)To learn more about these two drugs, see this Abilify versus Rexulti comparison. And be sure to talk with your doctor if you\u2019d like to know which drug may be right for you.What should I know about Rexulti vs. Latuda?Rexulti and Latuda have some similarities and differences. They both belong to a group of drugs called atypical antipsychotics, also referred to as second-generation antipsychotics. These are newer drugs that have fewer serious side effects than older antipsychotic drugs (called first-generation antipsychotics).Rexulti and Latuda have different active ingredients. (An active ingredient is what makes a drug work.) Rexulti contains the active ingredient brexpiprazole, while Latuda contains the active ingredient lurasidone hydrochloride.These medications are both used to treat schizophrenia in adults and certain children.Rexulti is also used in adults to treat depression (when taken with an antidepressant) and agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease. Latuda is also used to treat depression due to bipolar I disorder in adults and some children. For this use, doctors may also prescribe lithium (Lithobid) or valproate with Latuda for adults.For more information, check with your doctor about which drug they recommend for your condition.How does Rexulti compare with the alternative drugs Vraylar and Seroquel?Rexulti, Vraylar, and Seroquel work in similar ways. They all belong to a group of drugs called atypical antipsychotics, also referred to as second-generation antipsychotics. These medications are newer drugs that have fewer serious side effects than older antipsychotic drugs (called first-generation antipsychotics).The following table highlights some of the similarities and differences between these medications.Drug nameActive ingredientFormUsesRexultibrexpiprazoleoral tablet\u2022 depression (when taken together with an antidepressant)\u2022 schizophrenia\u2022 agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s diseaseVraylarcariprazineoral capsule\u2022 depression (when taken together with an antidepressant)\u2022 schizophrenia\u2022 depression due to bipolar I disorder\u2022 manic or mixed episodes of bipolar I disorderSeroquelquetiapineoral tablet\u2022 schizophrenia\u2022 depression due to bipolar I disorder or bipolar II disorder\u2022 manic or mixed episodes of bipolar I disorderAnother form of Seroquel called Seroquel XR is available. This is an extended-release tablet that is prescribed for the same conditions as Seroquel. (\u201cExtended release\u201d means the drug is slowly released into your body over a long period of time.) But it also treats depression when taken together with an antidepressant.For some uses, doctors may prescribe Rexulti or Seroquel for certain children. Vraylar is typically only prescribed for adults.If you\u2019d like more information about how these medications compare, talk with your doctor. They can discuss all your treatment options and the benefits and risks of each drug.What are some frequently asked questions about Rexulti?Here are answers to some commonly asked questions about Rexulti.Will I have withdrawal symptoms if I stop taking Rexulti?No, you will not. Rexulti does not cause physical dependence, so stopping it suddenly does not lead to withdrawal. With dependence, your body needs a drug in order to feel like it usually does. Suddenly stopping a drug you\u2019re dependent on can lead to withdrawal, which can cause uncomfortable symptoms.Note that suddenly stopping Rexulti could worsen symptoms of the condition you were using the drug to treat. If you want or need to stop taking Rexulti, talk with your doctor. They\u2019ll guide you on how to stop Rexulti treatment to help avoid or decrease worsening symptoms.Is Rexulti used for anxiety or bipolar disorder?No, Rexulti is not approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for anxiety or bipolar disorder. The drug may be used off-label for these conditions. (With off-label use, a drug is used to treat conditions other than those it\u2019s been approved for.)You can also ask your doctor for information about using Rexulti for anxiety or bipolar disorder. They can also provide information about other treatment options for either condition.Keep in mind that, in rare cases, Rexulti can cause anxiety as a side effect. If you\u2019re experiencing anxiety during Rexulti treatment, talk with your doctor. They can discuss options with you to help manage your anxiety.What\u2019s the half-life of Rexulti, and how long does it stay in your system?Rexulti\u2019s active ingredient brexpiprazole has a half-life of 91 hours. This means it takes 91 hours for half of a dose of brexpiprazole to be cleared from your body.In general, it takes about four to five half-lives for a full dose of a drug to be fully cleared from your body.How long a drug stays in a person\u2019s system can vary based on different factors. These include genetics and how well their liver and kidneys are working. Rexulti can stay in the body for about 2 to 3 weeks.How does Rexulti work?Rexulti\u2019s exact mechanism of action is not known. (A drug\u2019s mechanism of action describes how it works.)But this type of medication is thought to work by regulating certain neurotransmitters in the brain. (Neurotransmitters are brain chemicals.)Specifically, Rexulti is thought to affect dopamine and serotonin. It\u2019s believed this drug works by balancing these chemicals to help reduce symptoms of the conditions it treats.Rexulti costCosts of prescription drugs can vary depending on many factors. These factors include what your insurance plan covers and which pharmacy you use.For more information on ways to save on the price of the drug, see this Rexulti cost article. If you have questions about how to pay for your prescription, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You can also visit the Rexulti manufacturer\u2019s website to learn about support options. For example, it offers a savings card that you may be eligible for.What should be considered before taking Rexulti?Talk with your doctor about all your medications and any other health conditions you have before starting treatment with Rexulti.Tell your doctor if you have kidney or heart problems, diabetes, high cholesterol, or high triglycerides. And let them know if you\u2019ve ever had seizures or any other medical problems.Additionally, tell your doctor if you\u2019re pregnant, planning to become pregnant, or planning to breastfeed while taking Rexulti. Antipsychotics such as Rexulti may increase certain risks if used in pregnancy.These and other considerations are described here.InteractionsTaking medications, vaccines, and foods with a certain drug can affect how the drug works. These effects are called interactions.Before taking Rexulti, be sure to tell your doctor about all medications you take, including prescription and over-the-counter types. Also, describe any vitamins, herbs, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions with Rexulti that these items may cause.Interactions with drugs or supplementsRexulti can interact with several types of drugs. Rexulti is broken down in your liver by certain enzymes (types of proteins). If you take drugs with Rexulti that are also broken down by these enzymes, the drugs may interact and cause side effects.Some types of drugs can increase the effects of Rexulti. In this case, your doctor may need to lower the dose of Rexulti to lessen your risk of adverse reactions. Examples of these drugs include:certain antidepressant drugs, such as: bupropion (Wellbutrin SR, Wellbutrin XL)paroxetine (Paxil)duloxetine (Cymbalta)certain antifungal drugs, such as fluconazole (Diflucan)quinidine, which is used to treat heart rhythm problemscertain antibiotics, such as clarithromycinCertain other drugs can reduce the effectiveness of Rexulti by clearing it faster than usual from your body. In this case, your doctor may need to increase your dose of Rexulti. Some examples of these drugs include:the antibiotic rifampin (Rifadin)seizure medications, such as carbamazepine (Tegretol, Equetro) and phenytoin (Phenytek, Dilantin)This list does not contain all types of drugs that may interact with Rexulti. For additional information, see this Rexulti interactions article. Your doctor or pharmacist can also tell you more about these interactions and any others that may occur when using Rexulti.Other interactionsRexulti may also interact with herbs and supplements.For example, St. John\u2019s wort, which some people take to ease symptoms of depression, may reduce the effects of Rexulti. You should not take this herb with Rexulti. Tell your doctor if you are taking this herb before starting treatment with Rexulti.Boxed warningsRexulti has boxed warnings. These are the most serious warnings about a medication from the Food and Drug Administration (FDA). Rexulti\u2019s boxed warnings are described here.Risk of death in older adults with psychosis related to dementia: Typically, Rexulti should not be used in older adults (ages 65 years and older) who have psychosis related to dementia. (With psychosis, you lose touch with reality. And with dementia, you have changes in your mental status.) This is because Rexulti can increase the risk of death in older adults with this condition.But Rexulti may be prescribed to older adults with this type of psychosis for treating agitation caused by dementia due to Alzheimer\u2019s disease. (For more information about this use, see the \u201cDoes Rexulti have other uses?\u201d section.)Risk of suicidal thoughts or behaviors: Antidepressant medications can increase suicidal thoughts and behaviors in children and adults ages 24 years and younger. Rexulti is not considered an antidepressant (it\u2019s classified as an atypical antipsychotic). But it\u2019s used to treat depression together with an antidepressant.While doctors do not prescribe Rexulti to children for depression, they may prescribe the drug to some children for schizophrenia.For more information about these warnings, see the \u201cWhat are Rexulti\u2019s side effects?\u201d section.Other warningsRexulti can sometimes cause harmful effects in people who have certain conditions. This is known as a drug-condition interaction. Other factors may also affect whether Rexulti is a good treatment option for you.Talk with your doctor about your health history before you take Rexulti. Be sure to tell them if any of the following factors apply to you:liver problemsallergic reactiondifficulty metabolizing certain drugs, including Rexultikidney problemsdiabetesheart or blood pressure problemsseizurescholesterol problemslow white blood cell countdifficulty regulating body temperaturefallsdelayed thinking or reflexes or excessive sleepiness from Rexulti, which can make driving or operating heavy machinery dangerousUse with alcoholDrinking alcohol with Rexulti may increase your risk of certain side effects.For example, Rexulti can cause sleepiness and certain movement problems. Drinking alcohol may make these side effects worse. Taking Rexulti and drinking alcohol may also affect your liver function.If you drink alcohol, ask your doctor whether it\u2019s safe to do so during Rexulti treatment.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIf you can become pregnant or are breastfeeding, it\u2019s important to consider whether Rexulti is a safe choice for you.Taking Rexulti during the third trimester of pregnancy may increase the risk of extrapyramidal symptoms (which involve movement problems) or withdrawal symptoms in infants exposed to the drug. It\u2019s not known whether Rexulti is safe to use while breastfeeding.For more information, you can refer to this Rexulti reproductive health article. If you have additional questions, talk with your doctor.What should be done in case of overdose?Do not take more Rexulti than your doctor prescribes. Using more than this can lead to serious side effects. For a list of Rexulti\u2019s possible side effects, see the \u201cWhat are Rexulti\u2019s side effects?\u201d section.What to do in case you take too much RexultiCall your doctor if you think you\u2019ve taken too much Rexulti. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach America\u2019s Poison Centers or use its online resource. However, if you have severe symptoms, immediately call 911 (or your local emergency number) or go to the nearest emergency room.Ask a pharmacistQ: Will I need to stop taking Rexulti if I\u2019m taking an antibiotic for an infection?AnonymousA:It depends on the antibiotic your doctor prescribes to treat the infection. But most antibiotics are fine to take with Rexulti.Some types of drugs can increase the effects of Rexulti. This includes certain antibiotics.If you\u2019re prescribed an antibiotic that increases your risk of side effects from Rexulti, your doctor may have you temporarily stop taking Rexulti until your infection clears.Examples of antibiotics that can interact with Rexulti include:clarithromycinerythromycin (Ery-Tab)Keep in mind that if you\u2019re prescribed a medication that you\u2019ll apply topically, such as erythromycin eye ointment, it likely will not interact with Rexulti.If your doctor or dentist prescribes an antibiotic to treat an infection, make sure they\u2019re aware that you\u2019re taking Rexulti. They can check for any drug interactions and recommend a treatment that\u2019s safe for you.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.Disclaimer: Healthline has made every effort to make certain that all information is factually correct, comprehensive, and up to date. However, this article should not be used as a substitute for the knowledge and expertise of a licensed healthcare professional. You should always consult your doctor or another healthcare professional before taking any medication. The drug information contained herein is subject to change and is not intended to cover all possible uses, directions, precautions, warnings, drug interactions, allergic reactions, or adverse effects. The absence of warnings or other information for a given drug does not indicate that the drug or drug combination is safe, effective, or appropriate for all patients or all specific uses.Rexulti imagesVIEW GALLERY6", "content_hash": "d8808ee8f323b9b1157e213bbb721642d4a470a65bebcb81e9a3e051631e22bd", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:42.818545+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1371", "title": "World Legal Materials from North America", "url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/namerica", "final_url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/namerica", "text": "Antigua and Barbuda Bahamas Barbados Belize Canada Costa Rica Cuba Dominica Dominican Republic El Salvador Grenada Guatemala Haiti Honduras Jamaica Mexico Nicaragua Panama St. Kitts and Nevis Saint Lucia Saint Vincent and Grenadines Trinidad and Tobago Regional Institutions For further information see Cornell Law Library's \"Foreign and International Law Sources on the Internet\" Antigua and Barbuda: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Privy Council Decisions | Antigua and Barbuda Online | Mission to UN Bahamas: Constitution | Government | Parliamentary Elections Act | Privy Council Decisions | Selected Laws | Offshore Business Law | Government Links | Central Bank Barbados: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government Information Service | Government Information Network | Parliament | Agencies and Ministries | Prime Minister | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Privy Council Decisions | Copyright Act | Offshore Business Law Belize: Constitution | Government | Prime Minister | Chamber of Commerce and Industry | Privy Council Decisions | Legislation | Offshore Business Law | BelizeLaw.org | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Canada: Constitution | Alternate copy | Constitutional Resources | Government | Parliament | Agencies | Governor General | Department of Justice | Supreme Court | Supreme Court Opinions | Human Rights Tribunal | Courts & Case Law | Statutes | Canadian Legal Information Institute | Virtual Canadian Law Library | Access to Justice Network | Quicklaw Legal Database | Legal Resources | Citizenship & Immigration | Canadian Bar Association | Legal Links | Government Links | Other Legal Resources | Legal Links by Jurisdiction | Other Legal Materials | More Legal Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Costa Rica: Constitution | President | Legislative Assembly | Judiciary | Case Law (Spanish) | Supreme Tribunal of Elections | Offshore Business Law | Legislation Links | Government Links | Other Legal Links | More Legal Resources | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Cuba: Constitution | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Government | Penal Code | Foreign Investment Act | Electoral Law | Legal Immigration Program | Other Legal Materials | Mission to UN Dominica: Constitution | Government | Privy Council Decisions | Electoral Law Dominican Republic: Constitution (Spanish) | President | Electoral Law | Legislation Links | More Legal Resources (Spanish) | Government Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN El Salvador: Constitution (Spanish) | Government | President | Tribunal Supremo Electoral | Electoral Law | Legislation Links | Intellectual Property | Government Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Grenada: Constitution | Government | Ministries | Privy Council Decisions | Electoral Law | Offshore Business Law | Legal Materials Guatemala: Constitution | Government | Electoral Tribunal | Legislature | Legislation Links | Government Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Haiti: Constitution (French & English) | Parliament | Ministries | Electoral Law (French) | Legislation Links | Consulate (Chicago) | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Honduras: Constitution (Spanish) | National Congress | Monetary Law | Central Bank of Honduras Law | Government Links | Other Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Jamaica: Constitution | Constitution Overview | Government | Supreme Court | Supreme Court Judgments | Government Agencies & Ministries | Ministry of Justice | Jamaica Information Service | Privy Council Decisions | Selected Laws | National Library | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Mexico: Constitution | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Supreme Court | Senate | Chamber of Deputies | Judiciary | Electoral Tribunal | Superior Court of Justice | Attorney General | Intellectual Property | Selected Laws | Mexlaw | Legislation Links | Government Links | Other Legal Links | Legal Information | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Nicaragua: Constitution (selected provisions in English) | Alternate copy (Spanish) | President | National Assembly | Legislation | Selected Laws | Electoral Law | Government Links | Central Bank | Mission to UN Panama: Constitution (Spanish) | President | Judiciary | Electoral Law | Legislation | Offshore Business Law | Government Links | Other Legal Materials | Other Legal Links St. Kitts and Nevis: Constitution | Government | Privy Council Decisions | Legal Links | Mission to UN Saint Lucia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Government Information Service | Governor General | Privy Council Decisions | Government Links | Other Links | Mission to UN Saint Vincent and the Grenadines: Constitution | Privy Council Decisions | Telecommunications Law | Electoral Law | Legislation Links | International Financial Services Authority | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Trinidad and Tobago: Constitution | Government | Prime Minister | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Judiciary | Court of Appeals Judgments | High Court Judgements | Court Rules | Privy Council Decisions | Legislation Links | Business Law | Government Links | Central Bank | Mission to UN Regional Institutions: Organization American States | Inter-American Court of Human Rights | Caribbean Community (CARICOM) | Council of the Americas | NAFTA Secretariat | Organization of the Eastern Caribbean States | Eastern Caribbean Supreme Court | Caribbean Financial Action Task Force | Parliamentary Confederation of the Americas", "content_hash": "c8915c20b65bb4d912f14b277f8974684c478ad38b822f63292cdff33deebef1", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:43.036804+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1372", "title": "Your Guide to Skyrizi: How to Use it and What to Expect", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/skyrizi", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/skyrizi", "text": "Key takeaways Skyrizi (risankizumab-rzaa) is a prescription injection used to treat moderate to severe plaque psoriasis and active psoriatic arthritis in adults and children 6 years and older. It also treats Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s disease and ulcerative colitis in adults. Skyrizi is typically given once every 8 to 12 weeks. However, your specific Skyrizi dose and frequency will depend on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re treating. Skyrizi\u00e2\u0080\u0099s price can vary based on factors like your insurance coverage and treatment schedule. Skyrizi (risankizumab-rzaa) is a prescription biologic drug used to treat certain chronic inflammatory conditions. Biologics are advanced medications made from living cells rather than chemicals.Skyrizi is an interleukin-23 (IL-23) antagonist. It blocks IL-23, a natural protein involved in immune and inflammatory responses. By targeting this protein, Skyrizi helps lower the overactive inflammation that causes symptoms.What Is Skyrizi Used For?Skyrizi is approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to treat the following inflammatory disorders:Moderate to severe plaque psoriasis: For adults and children ages 6 years and older who can use systemic therapy (injections or pills) or phototherapy.Active psoriatic arthritis: For adults and children ages 6 years and older. It can be used alone or with non-biologic medications like methotrexate.Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s disease: For adults with moderately to severely active Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s disease.Ulcerative colitis: For adults with moderately to severely active ulcerative colitis.Will I need to use Skyrizi long term? Yes, if Skyrizi is working for you without causing serious or bothersome side effects, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll probably use it long term. What are Skyrizi\u00e2\u0080\u0099s forms, strengths, and dosages?Skyrizi comes in several liquid solution forms and strengths. Your doctor will determine the right dosage based on your condition and, for children, their body weight.Plaque psoriasis and psoriatic arthritisYou\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll take Syrizi as a subcutaneous injection. A healthcare professional can show you or a caregiver how to give the injection.Forms and strengths: 150 milligrams per milliliter (mg/mL) single-dose prefilled pen or syringe, and 55 mg/0.37 mL prefilled syringe (for children).Adults: 150 mg at Weeks 0 and 4, then every 12 weeks.Children ages 6 and older: Dosage is based on weight: Weighing less than 40 kilograms (kg) or 88 pounds (lbs): 55 mg at Weeks 0 and 4, then every 12 weeks.Weighing 40 kg or more: 150 mg at Weeks 0 and 4, then every 12 weeks.Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s disease and ulcerative colitis (adults only)You\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive Syrizi via an intravenous (IV) infusion administered by a healthcare professional in a medical facility.Starter (induction) IV phase:Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage: 600 mg via IV infusion over at least 1 hour at weeks 0, 4, and 8.Ulcerative colitis dosage: 1,200 mg via IV infusion over at least 2 hours at Weeks 0, 4, and 8. Maintenance subcutaneous phase:Dosage: Starting at Week 12 and then every 8 weeks, you receive an injection of 180 mg or 360 mg.Forms and strengths: Prefilled cartridges for on-body injector (180 mg or 360 mg) or prefilled syringes (90 mg or 180 mg). Note: If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re using 90 mg/mL syringes, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need two injections for a 180 mg dose and four for 360 mg. If using 180 mg/1.2 mL syringes, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need one for a 180 mg dose and two for 360 mg.What to do if you take too much SkyriziCall your doctor if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken too much Skyrizi. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach Poison Help or use its online resource. If you have severe symptoms, call 911 or your local emergency number immediately or go to the nearest emergency room.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Skyrizi Dosage GuideHow should I inject Skyrizi at home?For Skyrizi injections under your skin, a healthcare professional will likely give you your first few doses, then show you or a caregiver how to inject at home. Skyrizi must be given by an adult if the child is ages 6 to 9 years. For children ages 10 and older, it should be given by or under the supervision of an adult.How to inject Skyrizi at homeFollow these steps for using the prefilled pen, syringe, or on-body injector:Let it warm up: Remove the carton from the refrigerator and let it reach room temperature, out of direct sunlight, in its carton. Do not warm it in any other way. Warming times are: Prefilled pen: 30 to 90 minutes Prefilled syringe: 15 to 30 minutes On-body injector: 45 to 90 minutes (it will not work if left out for less than 45 minutes) Inspect the liquid: It should look clear to yellow (slightly yellow for 90 mg/mL syringe and 600 mg/10 mL vial) and may contain tiny white or clear particles. Do not use if cloudy, discolored, frozen, or containing large flakes.Choose your site: Inject into the front of your thighs or your abdomen (at least 2 inches away from your belly button). Caregivers may also use the upper, outer arm. Avoid skin that is tender, bruised, red, hard, scarred, has stretch marks, or is affected by psoriasis.Follow the instructions: Each form has a different set of instructions, so follow the instructions that come with the medication. You can visit the drug manufacturer\u00e2\u0080\u0099s website for more information on how to self-inject Skyrizi using the prefilled pen, prefilled syringe, or on-body injector.Missed dose: If you miss a dose, take it as soon as possible and resume your regular schedule.You can take your dose of Skyrizi with or without food.Receiving a Skyrizi IV infusionFor Skyrizi IV infusions, a healthcare professional will administer the dose over the course of at least 1 hour. You\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive your infusions in a clinic, hospital, or infusion center. Your doctor will instruct you on what to expect from these infusions and how to prepare.Medical PerspectiveHow is Skyrizi different from other treatment options for plaque psoriasis?\u00e2\u0080\u009cSkyrizi, like some other biologic drugs, is a systemic therapy. Systemic therapies are drugs that affect your entire body. With Skyrizi, the drug acts on your immune system to help reduce inflammation related to plaque psoriasis.The other common type of treatment for plaque psoriasis is topical therapy. Topical therapies are applied directly to the site of inflammation or dryness. These drugs are typically corticosteroids that come as creams or ointments. Corticosteroids are drugs that lower the responsiveness of the body\u00e2\u0080\u0099s immune system.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like to know more about Skyrizi versus other drugs for plaque psoriasis, talk with your doctor.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u0094 The Healthline Pharmacist TeamRead more: What Are the Treatment Options for Plaque Psoriasis?Quotes represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.What are Skyrizi\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Like most drugs, Skyrizi may cause mild or serious side effects. Mild side effects of Skyrizi can include:fatigue (low energy)fungal infections of the skin or nailsupper respiratory infections (URI), such as the common coldjoint painfeverabdominal pain or back painanemia (low level of red blood cells)urinary tract infection (UTI)pain, discoloration, or swelling at the injection siteheadacheMild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days or a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Serious side effects from Skyrizi aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common. They include:serious infections, such as pneumonialiver damagesevere allergic reaction\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Skyrizi side effectsWhat should I consider before starting Skyrizi?Before prescribing Skyrizi, your doctor will thoroughly evaluate your medical history and recommend the following pre-treatment steps:Tuberculosis (TB) testing: Your doctor must test you for TB before starting Skyrizi. Skyrizi is not suitable if you have active TB. If you have latent (inactive) TB, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll receive treatment before starting Skyrizi. Liver function tests: For Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s or colitis, your doctor must check your liver enzymes and bilirubin via blood tests before starting, during the first 12 weeks of treatment, and periodically afterward. This is to determine whether you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re at risk for hepatitis B, which would require preventive treatment.Vaccinations: Complete all age-appropriate vaccines before starting. Avoid receiving live vaccines immediately before, during, or after treatment, as you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll be more likely to get the infection the vaccine was meant to protect you from.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re looking to connect with others with your condition, check out the online communities at Bezzy. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a place where people can find support and connect with others.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIt\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not known whether Skyrizi can harm an unborn baby or pass into breast milk. Because monoclonal antibodies cross the placenta, Skyrizi may suppress the immune system of infants exposed in the womb. If you become pregnant, you are encouraged to join the Glow Pregnancy Registry by calling 1-877-302-2161 or visiting the registry\u00e2\u0080\u0099s website. \u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Skyrizi and reproductive healthHow much does Skyrizi cost?Costs of prescription drugs can vary depending on many factors. These factors include where you live, what your insurance plan covers, and which pharmacy you use. You may be eligible for a program called myAbbVie Assist, which helps you understand your insurance coverage and how to lower the cost of Skyrizi. For more information and to find out if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re eligible for support, call 800-222-6885 or visit the program website.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Skyrizi Cost and Financial AssistanceNext stepsIf you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re considering starting Skyrizi or you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve just started treatment, here are some next steps:Schedule your screenings: Call your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office to schedule your TB test and baseline liver function blood test (for Crohn\u00e2\u0080\u0099s or colitis).Request injection training: Before attempting to self-inject at home, ask a healthcare professional to show you how to prepare and administer the injection safely.Establish a reliable tracking system: Since Skyrizi maintenance doses are given weeks apart (every 8 or 12 weeks), mark your calendar or set a digital reminder for your upcoming doses.Get a sharps disposal container: Ensure you have a puncture-resistant container ready to safely discard your used prefilled pens, syringes, or cartridges. You can request a sharps container from the manufacturer at no additional cost by calling 1-866-759-7494 or visiting www.SKYRIZI.com.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Skyrizi imagesVIEW GALLERY1", "content_hash": "bb487fb38b0fb6c58287f5071121711f61c45077008caaed07b248fc66bd8f50", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:45.177481+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1373", "title": "World Legal Materials from South America", "url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/samerica", "final_url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/samerica", "text": "Argentina Bolivia Brazil Chile Colombia Ecuador Guyana Paraguay Peru Suriname Uruguay Venezuela Regional Institutions For further information see Cornell Law Library's \"Foreign and International Law Sources on the Internet\" Argentina: Constitution | Alternate copy (PDF - Spanish) | Government | President | Senate | Chamber of Deputies | Ministries | Ministry of Justice | Judiciary | Supreme Court | Penal Procedure Code | Environmental Law | Electoral Law | Statutes (only summaries) | Law Resources | Legal Database | Argentinean legislation | Bar Association | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Bolivia: Constitution (Spanish) | Government | President | Vice President | National Congress | Electoral Law | Telecommunications Law | Selected Laws | Bolivian legislation | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Brazil: Constitution | Alternate copy (Portuguese) | Alternate copy | Government | President | Senate | Chamber of Deputies | Government Agencies | Attorney General | Supremo Tribunal Federal: Decisions | Superior Tribunal de Justica: Decisions | Supreme Labor Court | Supreme Military Tribunal | Federal Audit Court | Civil Code (PDF) | Intellectual Property | Telecommunications Law | Electoral Law | Legislation Links | Other Legal Links | Brazil Links | Brazilian Bar Association | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Chile: Constitution | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Government | President | Senate | Chamber of Deputies | Ministry of Justice | Ministries | Library of the National Congress | Intellectual Property Law | Civil Law | Criminal Law | Telecommunications Law | Environmental Law | Electoral Law | Laws (searchable) | Case Law | Legislation Links | Bar Association | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Colombia: Constitution (Spanish - PDF) | Government | President | Senate | Ministries | Judiciary | Attorney General | Electoral Law | Case Law | Legislation Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Ecuador: Constitution (Spanish) | Government | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Intellectual Property Law | Electoral Law | Legislation | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Guyana: Constitution (Spanish) | Government Information Agency | President | Parliment | Ministries | Laws (PDF) | Guyana Online | Guyana Links | Guyana News and Information | Electoral Law | Alternate Site | Legislation | Bank of Guyana | Foreign Embassies Paraguay: Constitution | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Senate | President | Penal Code | Criminal Procedure Code | Electoral Law | Legislation Links | Central Bank Peru: Constitution (Spanish) | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Judiciary | Ministry of Justice | Constitutional Tribunal | Legislature | Laws and Legislative Resolutions (Spanish) | Intellectual Property | Electoral Law | Government Links | Legislation Links | Other Legal Materials | Central Reserve Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Suriname: Constitution (English & Dutch) | Alternate copy | National Assembly Members | Ministries | Electoral Law | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Uruguay: Constitution (Spanish) | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Government | Parliament | Criminal Procedure Code (Spanish) | Electoral Law | Official Gazette | Government Links | Bar Association | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Venezuela: Constitution (Spanish) | Alternate copy (Spanish) | Government | Supreme Court | National Assembly | Government Agencies | Labor Law | Civil Code | Military Justice Code | Telecommunication Law | Other Legislation Links | Legal Links | Central Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Regional Institutions: Organization American States | Inter-American Court of Human Rights | Andean Community | CARICOM | Latin American Integration Association | Mercosur Trade Center | Free Trade Area of the Americas | Latin Union | Parliamentary Confederation of the Americas | Justice Studies Center of the Americas", "content_hash": "b1f745500aba45224db94258c86dd9ddf183ee71a395ea23f9f00826c1ae45d1", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:45.534900+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1374", "title": "Everything happening at\n                                                NDIC", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/media", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/media", "text": "Everything happening at NDIC News, official articles, event galleries and video updates covering the Corporation's activities, engagements and public announcements \u2014 in one place. News Gallery Articles Videos Latest NDIC News View all All Press Releases Announcements Speeches Features Press Release October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award Speech September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 Press Release August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms Press Release July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja Press Release July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Press Release June 30, 2026 NDIC Highlights Expanded Deposit Protection and Accelerated Reimbursement Systems Press Release June 22, 2026 NDIC and Federal High Court Strengthen Partnership for Efficient Justice and Financial System Protection Press Release May 29, 2026 NDIC and NCGC Partner to Strengthen Banking System Resilience Through Unified Risk Management Press Release May 25, 2026 NDIC Reiterates Commitment to Enhance Financial System Stability Press Release May 21, 2026 Youth Leadership: NDIC, NILE University host immersion challenge for business school students Press Release May 11, 2026 NDIC, CDIC Taiwan Benchmark Deposit Insurance Experience Press Release April 7, 2026 NDIC Provides Educational Platform for Students on Financial System Stability View more news In pictures Our Gallery View all 16 photos Featured album International Women's Day NDIC April 2026 NDIC emerges as 2nd and 5th at the Third Edition of the FG\u2019s National Service Innovation Competition During its First Outing Mar 29, 2023 \u00b7 4 photos Insights NDIC Articles View all Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 22, 2026 speech On behalf of the Federal Government of Nigeria, I thank the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation and the International Association of Deposit Insurers for convening this important gathering at a time when financial systems across the world face both unprecedented opportunities and emerging risks. MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 21, 2026 Speech This year\u2019s theme, \u201cSafeguarding Stability: Public Awareness and Crisis Readiness for a Stronger Future,\u201d NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 Feature Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria July 1, 2026 Announcement Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks June 19, 2026 Announcement Sale of Chattels of Closed Primary Mortgage Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid. June 15, 2026 Announcement View more articles Watch NDIC Videos View all Understanding NDIC's Mandate Paying Depositor What Are the Major Challenges when A Bank Fails?", "content_hash": "1bd06e997da1d07f5ad2136cb3b39d90d7f5f988c02e3391a5725713227d22d3", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:46.155381+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1375", "title": "Trintellix Overview: Side Effects, Uses, Dosage, and Risks", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/trintellix", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/trintellix", "text": "Trintellix at a glanceApproved uses: The treatment of major depressive disorder in adults.Available forms: Oral forms in 5 mg, 10 mg, and 20 mg strengths.Works by: Boosting serotonin activity in the brain by blocking serotonin reabsorption and stimulating serotonin receptors to improve mood.Common side effects: Nausea, constipation, vomiting, dizziness, and dry mouth.Interactions: MAO inhibitors, blood thinners, NSAIDs, and other drugs that boost serotonin levels (triptans, SSRIs, tramadol, and others).Boxed warning: Increased risk of suicidal thoughts and behaviors in younger patients.Other serious risks: Serotonin syndrome (potentially life threatening), abnormal bleeding, manic episodes, angle-closure glaucoma, dangeriosly low blood sodium, and withdrawal symptoms.Generic version: None.Trintellix contains the active drug ingredient vortioxetine and belongs to a class of drugs called antidepressants. It comes as a tablet you take by mouth.At this time, Trintellix is only available as a brand-name drug. It isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t available as a generic medication.Note: Trintellix has a boxed warning about the possible risk of suicidal thoughts and behaviors. A boxed warning is the most serious warning from the Food and Drug Administration (FDA). For details, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effects of Trintellix\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Read on to learn about Trintellix\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects, dosage, and more.Uses for TrintellixTrintellix is used in adults to treat major depressive disorder (MDD), which is also referred to as depression. A person with MDD feels sad or depressed for a prolonged period of time. Symptoms may include:ongoing sadness or hopelessnesschanges in your sleep pattern, such as insomnia or sleeping more than usuallosing interest in activities that used to make you happyanxietyIt\u00e2\u0080\u0099s thought that people with depression may have a lower amount of a chemical called serotonin in their brain. Though it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not known exactly how Trintellix works to treat depression, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s believed to increase serotonin and its activity in your brain.Side effects of TrintellixLike most drugs, Trintellix may cause mild to serious side effects. The following lists contain some of the more common side effects Trintellix may cause, but they don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t include all possible side effects.Keep in mind that side effects of a drug can depend on your age, other health conditions you have, and other medications you take.For more information about potential side effects of this medication, talk with your doctor or pharmacist, or check out this Trintellix side effects article. Note: After the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) approves a drug, it tracks and reviews side effects of the medication. Sharing your experience helps make medications safer for everyone by giving doctors and researchers more information about how the drug works in real life. If you develop a side effect while taking Trintellix and want to tell the FDA about it, visit MedWatch or call 800-FDA-1088.Mild side effectsHere\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a short list of some of the mild side effects Trintellix can cause. To learn about other mild side effects, talk with your doctor or pharmacist, or read the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information.Mild side effects of Trintellix that have been reported include:diarrheaconstipationunusual dreamsdizzinessdry mouthitchingnausea and vomiting (for more information, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section)Mild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days to a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Serious side effectsSerious side effects from Trintellix can occur, but they aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common. If you have serious side effects from this drug, call your doctor right away. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number.Serious side effects of Trintellix that have been reported include:serotonin syndrome (high levels of the chemical serotonin)bleedingclosed-angle glaucoma, an eye conditionlow sodium level in your bloodsexual side effects, such as low libidoallergic reactionboxed warning: risk of suicidal thoughts and behaviorsFor more information about some of these side effects, including the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s boxed warning, see the following \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effect focus\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Side effect focusLearn more about some of the side effects Trintellix may cause.Boxed warningTrintellix has a boxed warning. This is the most serious warning from the FDA. It alerts doctors and patients about drug effects that may be dangerous.Risk of suicidal thoughts or behaviors: Although rare, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible for antidepressants such as Trintellix to cause suicidal thoughts and actions in people ages 18 to 24 years. (Trintellix is not recommended for use in children at this time.)What might helpBefore starting Trintellix, tell your doctor if you have a history of depression or suicidal thoughts or behaviors. They may monitor you more often for mood changes, especially when you start taking Trintellix or when your dosage changes.While you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re taking this medication, your family or friends should also watch for changes in your mood or suicidal thoughts or behaviors. They should let you and your doctor know of any changes they notice as soon as possible.If you do have suicidal thoughts or behaviors during Trintellix treatment, tell your doctor right away. They may recommend changing your medication.Help is out thereIf you or someone you know is in crisis and considering suicide or self-harm, please seek support:Call or text the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at 988 or chat at 988lifeline.org. Caring counselors are available to listen and provide free and confidential support 24/7.Text HOME to the Crisis Text Line at 741741 to connect with a volunteer crisis counselor for free and confidential support 24/7.Not in the United States? Find a helpline in your country with Befrienders Worldwide.Call 911 or your local emergency services number if you feel safe to do so.Sexual side effectsSexual side effects often occur from taking antidepressants such as Trintellix, and they can affect both males and females.Examples of sexual side effects that Trintellix may cause include:low libido (sex drive)an orgasm or ejaculation that takes longer than usualinability to have an orgasm or ejaculateerectile dysfunctionNote: The use of binary terms such as \u00e2\u0080\u009cmale\u00e2\u0080\u009d and \u00e2\u0080\u009cfemale\u00e2\u0080\u009d in this article reflects the language of the sources we\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve used. Unless otherwise noted, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s unclear whether the research we reference included participants with expansive gender identities.What might helpIf you develop any sexual side effects from taking Trintellix, talk with your doctor. They may be able to recommend treatment options to decrease your sexual side effects.Nausea and vomitingYou may experience nausea and vomiting while taking Trintellix. In studies, these two side effects commonly occurred in people taking the drug.What might helpSome side effects may lessen as you continue taking Trintellix. For example, in the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s studies, nausea usually lasted for about 2 weeks. But in some people, this side effect lasted longer.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re experiencing nausea or vomiting from taking Trintellix, talk with your doctor. They may be able to recommend ways to relieve these side effects or they may recommend that you take another medication to avoid these side effects.Allergic reactionSome people may have an allergic reaction to Trintellix.Symptoms of a mild allergic reaction can include:skin rashitchingflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)A more severe allergic reaction is rare but possible. Symptoms of a severe allergic reaction can include swelling under your skin \u00e2\u0080\u0094 typically in your eyelids, lips, hands, or feet. They can also include swelling of your tongue, mouth, or throat, which can cause difficulty breathing.Call your doctor right away if you have an allergic reaction to Trintellix. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number.Frequently asked questions about TrintellixFind answers to some commonly asked questions about Trintellix.Are reviews available from people who\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken Trintellix?While the manufacturer doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have reviews on its website, it does feature first-person testimonials. Learning about the experiences of others who\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken Trintellix may help you decide whether the drug is right for you.It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that everyone\u00e2\u0080\u0099s body responds differently to medications. You can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t reliably predict how your body will react to a treatment based on someone else\u00e2\u0080\u0099s experience.Is Trintellix used for anxiety, ADHD, OCD, or bipolar disorder?Not at this time. Trintellix is only used to treat major depressive disorder (MDD). It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not used to treat anxiety, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD), obsessive-compulsive disorder (OCD), or bipolar disorder. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not known whether the drug is a safe or effective treatment option for these conditions.However, your doctor might recommend taking Trintellix off-label for any of these conditions except for bipolar disorder. (Off-label use is when a drug is prescribed for a condition it hasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t been approved to treat.)Studies suggest that Trintellix may be effective for treating anxiety and ADHD, though more research is needed. You should take Trintellix for these conditions only if your doctor prescribes it.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re interested in taking Trintellix off-label, talk with your doctor.Does Trintellix cause weight gain, sleepiness, headache, insomnia, or hair loss?No, you shouldn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have these side effects from taking Trintellix.In studies of people taking Trintellix, no major changes in weight were reported. But other antidepressants, such as amitriptyline, may cause weight gain. And although Trintellix doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t cause hair loss, this can be a side effect of other antidepressants, such as fluoxetine (Prozac).Sleepiness, headache, and insomnia also aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t reported side effects of Trintellix. But you may develop these symptoms if you suddenly stop taking Trintellix. (This is referred to as discontinuation syndrome.) So it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s recommended that you do not stop taking Trintellix without first talking with your doctor.If you need to stop taking Trintellix, your doctor will likely recommend that you slowly stop taking it over time. This will allow your body to adjust, so you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re less likely to have these side effects.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re experiencing weight gain, sleepiness, headache, insomnia, or hair loss during your treatment with Trintellix, talk with your doctor. They may be able to determine what\u00e2\u0080\u0099s causing these symptoms and suggest the right treatment options to address them.Is Trintellix an SSRI?No, Trintellix isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI). These drugs work by increasing serotonin levels in your brain. Although Trintellix is an antidepressant and does affect serotonin levels, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not considered an SSRI. Trintellix\u00e2\u0080\u0099s mechanism of action (how it works) to treat depression isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t completely understood. Will I have withdrawal symptoms from stopping Trintellix?It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible that you may have withdrawal symptoms, also called discontinuation syndrome, if you suddenly stop taking Trintellix. This was reported in people who were taking 15 milligrams (mg) to 20 mg of Trintellix daily. Symptoms may include:nauseasweatingchanges in mood, such as irritability, agitation, anxiety, or feeling more emotionaldizziness\u00e2\u0080\u009cpins and needles\u00e2\u0080\u009d feeling in your arms, legs, hands, or feettremorconfusionheadachesleepinessinsomniaseizuresringing in your earshypomania (a milder form of mania)It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible to lessen or avoid withdrawal symptoms when stopping Trintellix by slowly reducing your dose over time. If you need to stop taking Trintellix, talk with your doctor about the best way to do so.Is Trintellix a controlled substance?No, Trintellix isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t a controlled substance (a medication regulated by the federal government). In most cases, controlled substances can be misused and may even cause dependence. Misuse is taking a medication in a different way than how it was prescribed. Dependence is when you need to take a medication to function as usual.Most medications used to treat depression aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t controlled substances.Trintellix dosageThe following information is about commonly used dosages of Trintellix, but always take the dosage your doctor prescribes. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll determine the dosage that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you.Form and strengthsTrintellix is available as a tablet that you take by mouth. It comes in strengths of 5 milligrams (mg), 10 mg, and 20 mg.Recommended dosagesYou\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll take this medication by mouth once daily. Your doctor will determine the best dose of Trintellix for you to take. They may start you on a dose and then increase or decrease it based on how well the drug is working for you. Questions about Trintellix\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosageHere are answers to a few questions about taking Trintellix.Can Trintellix be chewed, crushed, or split? The manufacturer of Trintellix doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t make any recommendations on whether the drug can be chewed, crushed, or split. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having difficulty swallowing your Trintellix tablet, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You can also check out these tips for swallowing pills.Should I take Trintellix with food? You can take your dose of Trintellix with or without food.Is there a best time of day to take Trintellix? You can take Trintellix in the morning or at night, but try to take it at about the same time each day. This helps to keep a steady level of the drug in your system.What if I miss a dose of Trintellix? If you miss your dose of Trintellix, talk with your doctor or pharmacist about the best time to take your next dose. In some cases, they may recommend taking your dose as soon as you remember. Or they may recommend skipping your missed dose and taking your next dose as scheduled.Will I need to take Trintellix long term? If Trintellix is working to treat your depression, your doctor will likely recommend that you take it long term.How long does Trintellix take to work? Trintellix begins working after you take your first dose. However, it can take up to 2 weeks for Trintellix to reach a steady level in your body, so you may not see the maximum benefits of treatment for 2 weeks.\u00c2\u00bbLEARN MORE:Dosage Guide for TrintellixSimilar drugsOther drugs are available that can treat your condition. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like to explore an alternative to Trintellix, talk with your doctor. They can tell you about other medications that might work well for you.The following drugs are similar to Trintellix:sertraline (Zoloft)escitalopram (Lexapro)vilazodone (Viibryd)bupropion (Wellbutrin SR, Wellbutrin XL)fluoxetine (Prozac)venlafaxine (Effexor XR)citalopram (Celexa)To learn more about how these drugs compare, check out the Trintellix vs. other drugs section of this article.Trintellix cost and savingsPrescription drug costs can vary depending on many factors, including what your insurance plan covers and which pharmacy you use.If you have questions about how to pay for your prescription, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. You can also visit the Trintellix manufacturer\u00e2\u0080\u0099s website to see if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re eligible for any of their support options.\u00c2\u00bbMORE:Check out this article to learn more about saving money on prescriptions.Factors to consider when taking TrintellixBefore starting Trintellix, talk with your doctor about any other medications you take and other medical conditions you may have. This will help them determine if Trintellix may be a safe treatment option for you.InteractionsTaking a medication with certain vaccines, foods, and other things can affect how the medication works. These effects are called interactions.Before taking Trintellix, be sure to tell your doctor about all medications you take, including prescription and over-the-counter types. Also, describe any herbs, vitamins, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions these items may cause with Trintellix.Interactions with drugs or supplementsTrintellix can interact with several types of drugs. These include:monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs), such as: phenelzine (Nardil)selegiline (Emsam)tranylcypromine (Parnate)serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors (SNRIs), such as: duloxetine (Cymbalta)venlafaxine (Effexor XR)desvenlafaxine (Pristiq)selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs), such as: fluoxetine (Prozac)citalopram (Celexa)escitalopram (Lexapro)migraine medications called triptans, such as: sumatriptan (Imitrex)eletriptan (Relpax)rizatriptan (Maxalt)tricyclic antidepressants (TCAs), such as: amitriptylineimipramine (Tofranil)nortriptyline (Pamelor)the pain medications fentanyl (Subsys) and tramadol (Ultram)the mood stabilizer lithium (Lithobid)the anxiety drug buspironeamphetamines, such as: amphetamine salts (Adderall XR)lisdexamfetamine (Vyvanse)blood thinners, such as: aspirinclopidogrel (Plavix)heparinwarfarin (Jantoven)drugs that increase the breakdown of Trintellix, such as: rifampin (Rimactane)carbamazepine (Tegretol)phenytoin (Dilantin)drugs that reduce your body\u00e2\u0080\u0099s ability to break down Trintellix, such as: bupropion (Wellbutrin SR, Wellbutrin XL)fluoxetine (Prozac)paroxetine (Paxil)quinidineThis list does not contain all types of drugs that may interact with Trintellix. Trintellix may interact with the herbal supplement St. John\u00e2\u0080\u0099s wort. This supplement can also increase serotonin levels, which in turn may increase your risk of serotonin syndrome, a serious side effect.Other interactionsTrintellix may cause false positive results for methadone on some urine drug tests. Let your healthcare professional or testing center know that you take Trintellix if you need a drug screen.Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about these interactions and any others that may occur with Trintellix.Boxed warningTrintellix has a boxed warning. This is the most serious warning from the FDA. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s possible for antidepressants such as Trintellix to cause suicidal thoughts or behaviors in people ages 18 to 24 years. For more information, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cSide effects of Trintellix\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Other warningsTrintellix may not be right for you if you have certain medical conditions or other factors that affect your health. Talk with your doctor about your health history before taking Trintellix. Factors to discuss include those listed here.allergic reactionbipolar disorderbleeding disordersglaucoma or other eye conditionslow sodium levels in the blood or a condition called syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH)Trintellix and alcoholIf you drink alcohol while taking Trintellix, you may have an increased risk of certain side effects. For example, both alcohol and Trintellix can cause dizziness, bleeding, nausea, and vomiting. So taking both substances together can increase these risks even more. If you want to drink alcohol during Trintellix treatment, talk with your doctor about how much, if any, is safe for you to consume.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIf you can become pregnant or are breastfeeding, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to consider whether Trintellix is a safe choice for you and your child. You can refer to this Trintellix reproductive health article for more information. If you have additional questions, talk with your doctor.OverdoseDo not take more Trintellix than your doctor prescribes, as this can lead to serious side effects.Symptoms of overdoseSymptoms caused by an overdose can include:nauseadizzinessdiarrheastomach problems or discomfortitchingsleepinessflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)What to do in case you take too much TrintellixCall your doctor if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken too much Trintellix. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach America\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Poison Centers or use its online resource. However, if you have severe symptoms, immediately call 911 or your local emergency number, or go to the nearest emergency room.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Trintellix imagesVIEW GALLERY3", "content_hash": "23d2fac0dee399b08cd34ff9b6bf3791c6e59f9c9562b2f5c6fe5f72ca3503ad", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:47.835304+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1376", "title": "World Legal Materials from Australasia", "url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/australasia", "final_url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/australasia", "text": "American Samoa Australia Cook Islands Fiji Kiribati The Maldives Marshall Islands Micronesia Nauru New Zealand Niue Samoa Solomon Islands Tokelau Tonga Tuvalu Vanuatu Regional Institutions For further information see Cornell Law Library's \"Foreign and International Law Sources on the Internet\" American Samoa: Constitution | Government | Case Search | Legislation | Bar Association | Samoa Code | Rules of Court | Administrative Code | Treaties, Cessions & Federal Laws Australia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Alternate copy | Other Constitutional Documents | Australasian Legal Information Institute | High Court Decisions | High Court of Australia | Federal Court of Australia | Family Court | Human Rights and Equal Opportunity Commission | Cases & Legislation | Legislation Links | ComLaw (searchable database) | Government | Parliament | Legislation from Parliament | Attorney General | Environment Australia | Australian Law on the Internet | Researching Australian Law | Other Legal Materials | Reserve Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Cook Islands: Constitution | Government | Government Information | Ministries | High Court Decisions (1977-2001) | Selected Legislation | Offshore Business Law | Other Legal Materials Fiji: Constitution | Government | President | Prime Minister | Parliament | Attorney General | Ministries | Fiji High Court Decisions (1976-2007) | Legislation | Reserve Bank Kiribati: Constitution | Legislation | Court System | Case Law | High Court Decisions (1975-2007) | Cases & Legislation | Legislation links The Maldives: Constitution (PDF) | Government | President | Ministries | Attorney General | Commercial Law | Maldives Monetary Authority | Mission to UN Marshall Islands: Constitution | Government | President | Court System | Cases & Legislation | Legal Resources | Embassy (Washington D.C.) Micronesia: Constitution | Government | Congress | Bills | Supreme Court Decisions | Cases & Legislation | Consolidated Legislation | Sessional Legislation | Other Legal Links | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Nauru: Constitution | Government Links | Legislation | Cases | Mission to UN New Zealand: Constitutional Act | Bill of Rights Act | Constitutional Documents | Goverment | Parliament | Case Law | Courts & Ministry of Justice | Judicial Decisions Online | Directory of Decisions | Ministry for the Environment | Overview of New Zealand Law | New Zealand Law Online | Other Legal Materials | Reserve Bank | Embassy (Washington D.C.) | Mission to UN Niue: Constitutional Act | Government | Court System | Cases & Legislation Samoa: Constitution | Government | Court System | Cases & Legislation | Sources of Law Solomon Islands: Constitution (PDF) | Government | Court System | Cases & Legislation Tokelau: Tokelau Act | Government | Laws | Legislation links | Legislation on the Web | Court System Tonga: Constitution | Government | Legislation Online | Court System | Cases & Legislation Tuvalu: Constitution | Government | Court System | Cases & Legislation Vanuatu: Constitution | Alternate Copy | Government | Court System | Cases & Legislation | Sources of Law | Vanuatu Law Reports | Offshore Business Law | Legislative Links | Other Legal Links Regional Institutions: Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation | Pacific Islands Forum | Secretariat of the Pacific Community | University of the South Pacific School of Law", "content_hash": "53fb2497f6f878e5e438c7dc1875f905174c0a3eab1882e3e4c0fca47c264b64", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:48.321590+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1377", "title": "NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail", "text": "NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award N NDIC October 2, 2026 2 min read Rep of Chairman, Independent Corrupt Practices and Other Related Offences Commission(ICPC), Mr. Olusegun Adigun (middle), supported by Publisher &amp; Editor-in-Chief, Verbatim News Magazine, Mr. Tobs Agbaebu, while presenting Verbatim Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award 2026 to the rep of MD/CE, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Ms. Hawwau Gambo at the Verbatim 2026 Award ceremony in Abuja.The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) has been awarded the 2026 Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award for demonstrating exemplary commitment to ethics, transparency and accountability in public service by Verbatim Magazine.The award was presented to the Managing Director/Chief Executive Officer of the Corporation, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, who was represented by the Head of Communication and Public Affairs, Ms. Hawwau Gambo, at the 2026 Verbatim Awards, organised by Verbatim Print & Broadcast Limited in partnership with the Independent Corrupt Practices and Other Related Offences Commission (ICPC) in Abuja.The NDIC earned the prestigious recognition following the Corporation\u2019s emergence as second overall in the 2025 Ethics and Integrity Compliance Scorecard (EICS) of the ICPC. The EICS is an integrity-assessment framework developed by the ICPC to promote ethical standards, accountability and anti-corruption practices in the public service. The framework evaluates Ministries, Departments and Agencies (MDAs) of the Federal Government of Nigeria across four key areas of Management Culture and Structure; Financial Management System; Administrative Systems; and Anti-Corruption Initiatives.The Chairman of the ICPC, Dr. Musa Adamu Aliyu, SAN, who was represented by the Director, Systems Study and Review Department (SSRD), Mr. Olusegun Adigun, delivered a keynote address at the ceremony, titled: \u201cThe Power of Integrity in National Development: Strengthening Public Institutions, Restoring Trust and Driving Prosperity.\u201dReceiving the award on behalf of the NDIC, Managing Director/Chief Executive, Mr. Thompson O. Sunday, the Head of Communication and Public Affairs, Ms. Hawwau Gambo, commended Verbatim Print & Broadcast Limited for recognising the Corporation\u2019s performance based on the ICPC\u2019s independently validated integrity scorecard.She reaffirmed the Corporation\u2019s commitment to sustaining the highest standards of transparency, accountability and ethical governance in the discharge of its mandates of deposit guarantee, bank supervision (in collaboration with the CBN), failure resolution and bank liquidation. Ms Gambo noted that the award was a reflection of the Corporation\u2019s sustained efforts to maintaining the confidence of stakeholders in the discharge of its mandates. As the NDIC continues to protect depositors, engender confidence in the banking sector and contribute to financial system stability, the recognition serves as both an affirmation of its achievements and an impetus to further deepen compliance with the highest standards of professionalism, excellence and public trust.Ms. Hawwau Gambo,Head, Communication & Public AffairsOctober 2, 2026 All News Share More News September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders June 30, 2026 NDIC Highlights Expanded Deposit Protection and Accelerated Reimbursement Systems Browse all news", "content_hash": "e2fcf48a86d4b2a66658ad6720643ef6b4cb06fdeefa2abcec09750e14cbd4f8", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:48.990776+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1378", "title": "Ubrelvy Overview: Side Effects, Uses, Dosage, and Risks", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/ubrelvy", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/ubrelvy", "text": "Ubrelvy at a glanceApproved uses: The treatment of acute migraine attacks with or without aura in adults.Available forms: Oral tablets in 50 mg and 100 mg strengths.Works by: Blocking calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) protein receptors to stop pain signals and inflammation.Common side effects: Nausea, sleepiness, fatigue, sedation, and dry mouth.Interactions: Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (like ketoconazole and clarithromycin), strong CYP3A4 inducers (like rifampin, st. john\u00e2\u0080\u0099s wort, and phenytoin), and moderate CYP3A4 inhibitors or grapefruit juice.Boxed warning: None.Other serious risks: Severe allergic reactions, new or worsening high blood pressure, and Raynaud\u00e2\u0080\u0099s phenomenon.Generic version: None.See the Ubrelvy coupon.Ubrelvy is used to immediately treat migraine symptoms in adults. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not prescribed to help prevent migraine symptoms. To learn more about Ubrelvy\u00e2\u0080\u0099s uses, see the \u00e2\u0080\u009cUbrelvy for migraine\u00e2\u0080\u009d section.Ubrelvy basicsUbrelvy is a brand-name medication. It contains the active ingredient ubrogepant. (An active ingredient is what makes a drug work.) A generic version of the drug isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t currently available.Ubrelvy belongs to a group of drugs called calcitonin gene-related peptide antagonists.Ubrelvy cost and savingsWhether you have health insurance or not, cost may be a factor when you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re considering Ubrelvy. What you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll pay for Ubrelvy may depend on several things, such as your treatment plan and the pharmacy you use.Here are a few things to consider regarding the cost of Ubrelvy:Comparing pharmacies: The price of Ubrelvy may vary depending on which pharmacy you use, so it can help to compare prices across pharmacies to find the lowest cost.Savings program: If you have questions about how to pay for your prescription, talk with your doctor or pharmacist. The Ubrelvy Complete Savings Card may be available to you.Ubrelvy dosageYour doctor will recommend the dosage of Ubrelvy that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you. The following text describes commonly used dosages, but always follow the dosage instructions that your doctor provides.Form and strengthsUbrelvy comes as a tablet you swallow. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s available in the following strengths:50 milligrams (mg)100 mgRecommended dosageYou\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll take 50 mg or 100 mg of Ubrelvy when you need immediate treatment for a migraine episode. Then, you can take a second dose 2 hours after your first dose if needed.You should not take more than 200 mg of the drug within 24 hours. This is the maximum dosage of the drug.Also, you should not take Ubrelvy for more than eight migraine episodes in 30 days. The safety of taking Ubrelvy more often than this isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t known. So talk with your doctor about how often you should take this drug.How to take UbrelvyYour doctor will explain how you should take Ubrelvy, how much to take, and how often to take it. Be sure to follow your doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s instructions.Ubrelvy comes as tablets that you swallow. You should take the medication as soon as you feel a migraine episode starting.It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to note that you should avoid taking a second dose of Ubrelvy if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve consumed any grapefruit or grapefruit juice within 24 hours of your first dose. Doing so may increase the side effects of Ubrelvy. This is because grapefruit makes the drug stay in your body for longer than usual and can increase its side effects.About taking UbrelvyHere are some answers to a few common questions related to taking Ubrelvy:Will I need to take Ubrelvy long term? If Ubrelvy works well for you, your doctor may recommend that you take it long term as needed for migraine episodes. You should discuss your migraine treatment plan with your doctor.How long does Ubrelvy take to work? Ubrelvy starts to work quickly. Most people get relief from migraine symptoms within 2 hours of taking a dose. And the effects of Ubrelvy may last for up to a day or longer.Can Ubrelvy be chewed, crushed, or split? No, you shouldn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t crush, chew, or split Ubrelvy tablets. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not known whether doing these things will change how the medication works. If you have difficulty swallowing pills, talk with your doctor about other treatment options.Should I take Ubrelvy with food? You can take Ubrelvy with or without food. But keep in mind that both Ubrelvy and migraine may cause nausea. So you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll have to find out how well your body tolerates Ubrelvy either with food or on an empty stomach.OverdoseDo not take more Ubrelvy than your doctor prescribes. Doing so can lead to serious side effects. Call your doctor if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken too much Ubrelvy. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach America\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Poison Centers, or you can use its online resource. But if you have severe symptoms, immediately call 911 or your local emergency number. Or go to the nearest emergency room.Ubrelvy for migraineUbrelvy is used for immediate treatment of migraine symptoms in adults. It isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t used to help prevent migraine symptoms.With migraine, you can have symptoms such as:severe headachesnauseavomitingvisual or sensory changes called an auraPeriods when symptoms occur are referred to as migraine episodes or migraine attacks. Ubrelvy can treat migraine episodes that happen with or without an aura. \u00c2\u00bbOnline Care:Need a refill for your migraine medication? Get prescribed in as little as 15 minutes with Optum Perks.Optum Perks is owned by RVO Health. By clicking on this link, we may receive a commission. Learn more.Frequently asked questions about UbrelvyHere are answers to some commonly asked questions about Ubrelvy.What\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Ubrelvy\u00e2\u0080\u0099s mechanism of action? What\u00e2\u0080\u0099s its half-life?Ubrelvy belongs to a group of drugs called CGRP antagonists. The mechanism of action for these drugs is to block the effects of a protein in your body called CGRP. (The mechanism of action describes how a drug works.)Studies show that this protein plays a major role in triggering migraine symptoms.Because CGRP is responsible for pain and inflammation tied to migraine, scientists theorize that medications such as Ubrelvy work by blocking CGRP. Levels of CGRP are increased during migraine episodes. And Ubrelvy helps bring these levels down.Ubrelvy has a half-life of 5 to 7 hours. This means your body will get rid of half of a dose of the drug 5 to 7 hours after you take your dose. It takes about five half-lives for your body to fully clear a drug.If you have more questions about how Ubrelvy works, talk with your doctor.Is Ubrelvy a triptan?No, Ubrelvy doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t belong to the group of drugs called triptans. Instead, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a CGRP antagonist.Some other drugs used to manage migraine are triptans. These drugs include rizatriptan (Maxalt, Maxalt-MLT) and sumatriptan (Imitrex).If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like information about taking a triptan for migraine treatment, talk with your doctor.Is Ubrelvy a controlled substance?No, Ubrelvy isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t a controlled substance. Controlled substances have the potential to be misused. (With misuse, a drug is taken in a way other than how it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribed.) But Ubrelvy doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t carry a risk of misuse.Lasmiditan (Reyvow) is an example of a migraine drug that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a controlled substance.Talk with your doctor or pharmacist if you have questions about controlled substances. Does Ubrelvy cause weight loss?No, weight loss wasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t seen in people during Ubrelvy\u00e2\u0080\u0099s studies. Another drug used for migraine, topiramate (Topamax, Trokendi XR), may cause weight loss. But Ubrelvy isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t known to do this.Keep in mind that migraine episodes can cause nausea and vomiting. In some cases, these symptoms could lead to weight loss.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having weight loss with Ubrelvy, talk with your doctor. They can recommend ways to help you manage a weight that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s healthy for you.Is Ubrelvy used for tension headaches?No, Ubrelvy is not approved for treating tension headaches. (These headaches cause pain that may feel like a tight band around your forehead.) Ubrelvy is approved to treat migraine headaches.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like to learn about treatment options for tension headaches, talk with your doctor.Side effects of UbrelvyLike most drugs, Ubrelvy may cause mild or serious side effects. The following lists describe some of the more common side effects of Ubrelvy. These lists don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t include all possible side effects.The side effects of a drug can vary from person to person. And they may depend on:your ageyour overall healthother medications you may be takingthe dosage of medication you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re takingother factorsYour doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about the possible side effects of Ubrelvy. They can also suggest ways to help reduce the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects.Mild side effectsHere\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a list of some of the mild side effects that Ubrelvy can cause. To learn about other mild side effects, talk with your doctor or pharmacist or read Ubrelvy\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information.Mild side effects of Ubrelvy can include:sleepinessnauseadry mouthMild side effects of many drugs may go away within a few days or a couple of weeks. But if they become bothersome, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Serious side effectsSerious side effects from Ubrelvy can occur, but they aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t common. If you have serious side effects from Ubrevly, call your doctor right away. If you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, you should call 911 or your local emergency number.Serious side effects of Ubrelvy that have been reported include:high blood pressureRaynaud phenomenon (reduced blood flow in the extremities)Allergic reactionSome people may have an allergic reaction to Ubrelvy.Symptoms of a mild allergic reaction can include:skin rashitchinessflushing (temporary warmth, redness, or deepening of skin color)A more severe allergic reaction called anaphylaxis is rare but possible. Symptoms of a severe allergic reaction can include:swelling under your skin, typically in your eyelids, lips, hands, or feet swelling of your tongue, mouth, or throat, which can cause difficulty breathinghives and itchy skinCall your doctor right away if you have an allergic reaction to Ubrelvy. But if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number.Alternatives to UbrelvyUbrelvy is used to manage migraine in adults. Specifically, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s used for immediate treatment of migraine symptoms. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not used to prevent migraine symptoms.Other drugs are used to treat migraine symptoms. Examples include:rimegepant (Nurtec ODT)eletriptan (Relpax)lasmiditan (Reyvow)triptans, such as sumatriptan (Imitrex) and rizatriptan (Maxalt, Maxalt-MLT) Some examples of medications that prevent migraine symptoms include:erenumab (Aimovig)galcanezumab (Emgality)topiramate (Topamax, Trokendi XR)To learn more about alternatives to Ubrelvy, talk with your doctor. What to know about Ubrelvy vs. NurtecUbrelvy and Nurtec ODT are both used to treat migraine episodes in adults. Ubrelvy comes as an oral tablet, while Nurtec is available as an orally disintegrating tablet (ODT). To learn more, see this Ubrelvy vs. Nurtect ODT comparison article.What to know about Ubrelvy vs. ImitrexUbrelvy and Imitrex are both used to treat migraine episodes in adults. Ubrelvy comes as an oral tablet, while Imitrex is available in several forms: an oral tablet, a subcutaneous injection, and a nasal spray. To learn more, see this Ubrelvy vs. Imitrex comparison article.Ubrelvy interactionsUsing certain medications, vitamins, or foods alongside certain drugs can affect how they all work. These effects are called interactions.Interactions can change a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s effect in your body, which can lead to two possible outcomes:The drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s effect is lowered so that it doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t work as well as usual.The drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s effect is raised so that it lasts for longer in your body and may cause increased side effects.Before taking Ubrelvy, be sure to tell your doctor about all medications you take, including prescription and over-the-counter types. Also, describe any vitamins, herbs, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions Ubrelvy may cause with these items.Interactions with drugs or supplementsUbrelvy can interact with certain drugs that increase effects of Ubrelvy in your body. These drugs include:certain HIV medications, such as cobicistat (Tybost), ritonavir (Norvir), and nelfinavir mesylate (Viracept)certain antibiotics, including ciprofloxacin (Cipro)antifungals, such as fluconazole (Diflucan)verapamil (Verelan), a blood pressure drugcyclosporine (Neoral), an immunosuppressant drugfluvoxamine (Luvox), an antidepressantUbrelvy can also interact with certain medications in a way that leads to lower effects of Ubrelvy in your body. These drugs include:rifampin (Rifadin), an antibioticseizure medications, such as phenytoin (Dilantin) and carbamazepine (Tegretol)barbituratesThese lists do not contain all types of drugs that may interact with Ubrelvy. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you more about these interactions and any others that may occur with Ubrelvy.Note: Taking certain medications with Ubrelvy is contraindicated. (A contraindication is a factor or condition that could prevent your doctor from prescribing a drug due to a risk of harm.) Ask your doctor for more information about medications that are contraindicated with Ubrelvy.Other interactionsIn addition to the medications described previously, Ubrelvy can also interact with other substances. For example:Grapefruit or grapefruit juice may increase side effects of Ubrelvy by increasing the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s effect in your body.St. John\u00e2\u0080\u0099s wort can lower the effect of Ubrelvy in your body.Ubrelvy pregnancy or breastfeedingThere isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t enough information available about the effects of taking Ubrelvy during pregnancy or while breastfeeding in humans. But in animal studies, Ubrelvy has been shown to cause fetal harm during pregnancy and low birth weight in lactating animals. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re pregnant or breastfeeding, or planning to become pregnant or to breastfeed, talk with your doctor about the safety of taking Ubrelvy.\u00c2\u00bbMORE:Refer to this Ubrelvy reproductive health article for more information.Ubrelvy precautionsUbrelvy may not be right for you if you have certain medical conditions or other factors that affect your health. Talk with your doctor about your health history before you take Ubrelvy. Some factors to consider include those in the following list:kidney problemsliver problemshigh blood pressureRaynaud phenomenonallergic reactionpregnancybreastfeedingAsk a pharmacistQ: Can I take Ubrelvy with acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Motrin)?AnonymousA:There aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t any known interactions between Ubrelvy and acetaminophen (Tylenol) or ibuprofen (Motrin). But you should only take Ubrelvy with an additional pain medication like these if your doctor recommends it. Keep in mind that Ubrelvy is approved to treat a migraine episode on its own without other drugs.The Healthline Pharmacist TeamAnswers represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Ubrelvy imagesVIEW GALLERY2", "content_hash": "14ce2a3f7f4ef61d086e46d4f0add9feb50acbcc2d547c6348735906e5f309d9", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:51.407949+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1379", "title": "World Legal Materials from Asia", "url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/asia", "final_url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/asia", "text": "Armenia Azerbaijan Bangladesh Bhutan Brunei Cambodia China Georgia Hong Kong India Indonesia Japan Kazakhstan Korea Kyrgyzstan Laos Macau Malaysia Mongolia Myanmar Nepal North Korea Pakistan Philippines Singapore Sri Lanka Taiwan Tajikistan Thailand Turkmenistan Uzbekistan Vietnam Regional Institutions For further information see Cornell Law Library's \"Foreign and International Law Sources on the Internet\" Armenia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | President | Ministries | Parliament | Legislation | Selected Laws | Banking Law | Embassy | Mission to UN Azerbaijan: Constitution | President | Ministry of Economic Development | Constitutional Court | Constitutional Court Decisions | Selected Laws | Natural Resources Legislation | Legal Links | More Legal Resources | Embassy | Mission to UN Bangladesh: Constitution | Government | Prime Minister | Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Parliament | Legislation Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Bhutan: Constitution | Government | Anti-Corruption Commission | Selected Laws | Acts | Legislation Links Brunei: Constitution Overview | Government | Monarch | Prime Minister | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Legislative Council | Selected Laws | Judiciary | Corruption Act (Synopsis) | Legislation Links | Government Links Cambodia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Council of Ministers | National Assembly | Laws | Legislation Links | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN China: Constitution | Government | Ministries | Institutions | National People's Congress | Supreme Court | Declaration of Human Rights | Statutes and Regulations | Mining Law | IP Law | Legislation Links | ChnLaw | China Today | ChinaOnline | Other Legal Materials | Embassy Georgia: Constitution | Parliament | Legislation | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Constitutional Court | Legislation Links | Embassy Hong Kong: Constitution | Constitutional Background | Government | Department of Justice | Legislative Council | Bills | Basic Law | Statutes, Ordinances and Regulations | Legislation Links | Judiciary | Offshore Business Law | Bar Association | More Legal Links India: Constitution | Constitutional Background | Government | President | Prime Minister | Cabinet Secretariat | Ministries | Ministry of Law & Justice | Parliament | Council of States | House of the People | Code | Supreme Court | High Court of Kerala | Courts & Case Law | Legislation Links | IP Law | Telecommunications Law | Government Links | Alternate Site | Other Legal Materials | Embassy | Mission to UN Indonesia: Constitution | Government | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | House of People's Representatives | People's Consultative Assembly | Legislation Links | IP Law | Mining Law | Environmental Law | Embassy | Mission to UN Japan: Constitution | Alternate copy | Alternate copy | Prime Minister | Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | House of Councillors | House of Representatives | Statutes | Code (Japanese) | Statutes & Regulations (Japanese) | Supreme Court | Courts & Case Law | Cases | Legislation Links | IP Law | Commercial Law | More Legal Materials | JapanLaw | Japan Law Guide (Stanford) | Other Law Resources | National Diet Library | Government Links | Alternate Site | Embassy | Mission to UN Kazakhstan: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | President | Parliament | Bills | Legislation Links | Banking Law | Government Links | Alternate Site | Other Legal Materials | Embassy | Mission to UN Korea (Republic): Constitution | Government | President | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Ministry of Justice | National Assembly | Constitutional Court | Constitutional Court Act | Supreme Court | Supreme Court Decisions | Legislation Links | Environmental Law | National Assembly Library | KoreaLaw | Korean Bar Association Kyrgyzstan: Constitution | Government | Parliament | Legislation | Legal Links | More Law Resources | Banking Law | Other Legal Materials | Embassy Laos: Constitution | Alternate copy | National Assembly | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Selected Laws | Legal Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Macau: Basic Law | Government | Legislative Assembly | Legislation | Press Law (Portuguese) | Media Registration Law (Portuguese) | Judiciary | Public Prosecutions Office | Legal Affairs Bureau | International Law Bureau | Legislation Links | Government Links | Alternate Site Malaysia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Prime Minister | Government Directory | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Parliament | Bills | Acts | Judiciary | Attorney General | Law Database | Legislation Links | Other Legal Materials | Bar Council | Government Links | Mission to UN Mongolia: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | President | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Parliament | Law Database | Constitutional Court | Courts & Case Law | Mongolia Law Library | Civil Code | Legislation Links | Legal Info | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Myanmar: Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Burma/Myanmar Law Library | Government Links | Embassy Nepal: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Prime Minister | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Parliament | Bills | Legislation Links | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN North Korea: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Legislation | North Korean Human Rights Act | Selected Laws Pakistan: Constitution | Alternate copy | Alternate copy | Government | President | Ministry of Justice | Senate | National Assembly | Lahore High Court | Judiciary Overview | Law & Justice Commission | Legislation Links | Shari'ah Act | Other Legal Links | Government Links | Alternate Site | Embassy | Mission to UN Philippines: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | President | Senate | House of Representatives | Laws/Rules & Regulations | Law Database | Supreme Court | Supreme Court Decisions (1901 - present) | Government Directory | IP Law | Mining Law | Selected Laws | Legislation Links | Other Law Links | More Legal Materials | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Singapore: Constitution | Government | President | Prime Minister | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Ministry of Law | Government Directory | Parliament | Statutes | Supreme Court | Attorney General | Selected Laws | Legislation Links | Singapore Legal Portal | Other Legal Links | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Sri Lanka: Constitution | Government | President | Prime Minister | Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Acts & Bills | Legal Draftsman's Department | Customs | Telecommunications Commission | Other Legal Materials | Government Websites | Embassy | Mission to UN Taiwan: Constitution | Alternate Copy | Judicial Yuan | President | Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | Executive Yuan | Legislative Yuan | National Assembly | Legislation Links | Government Links Tajikistan: Constitution | President | Assembly of Representatives | National Assembly | Legislation Links | Embassy Thailand: Constitution | Royal Thai Government | Monarchy | National Assembly | Senate | Selected Legislation | Judiciary | Attorney General | Thai Law Forum | Law Library | Legislation Links | More Legal Materials | Other Law Resources | Government Links | Embassy Turkmenistan: Constitution | Alternate copy | Government | Selected Laws | IP Law (Summary) | Other Legal Materials | Embassy | Mission to UN Uzbekistan: Constitution (PDF) | Alternate copy | Alternate copy | Government | Legislative Chamber | Senate | Ombudsman | Judiciary Overview | Legislation Links | Other Legal Materials | More Law Links | Embassy Vietnam: Constitution | Government | Ministries | Ministry of Foreign Affairs | National Assembly | Selected Laws | Legal Resources | Legislation Links | Other Legal Documents | More Legislation Materials | Government Links | Embassy | Mission to UN Regional Institutions: Asian Pacific Economic Cooperation | ASEAN | South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation", "content_hash": "76506869026bdffc56024217a322f4344bbad132434a9a3d60b047e36dd41639", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:52.666896+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1380", "title": "NDIC\n                                                Videos", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/videos", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/videos", "text": "NDIC Videos Watch official NDIC videos \u2014 depositor verification guides, short explainers, news features and more from the Corporation. Featured August, 2026 Understanding NDIC's Mandate Who protects your money when you keep it in a bank, and what does the NDIC do to make the banking system safer? Watch now All MDIC Shorts In the News Depositor Verification and Maximum Deposit Insurance Coverage (MDIC) 5:42 Nov 24, 2025 How to Verify Your Bank Deposits with NDIC Walk through the depositor verification process and check your coverage status. Aug 2026 Understanding NDIC's Mandate: Episode 2 An informative guide for anyone interested in understanding how depositor protection works in Nigeria. Aug 2026 Understanding NDIC's Mandate: Episode 3 Protecting Your Deposit continues... Sep 18, 2026 NDIC Focus Group -Episode 5 (Part One) Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) engaging with members of the informal economy to improve financial literacy and inclusion. Sep 20, 2026 NDIC Focus Group-Episode 6 (Part Two) NDIC Promotes Financial Literacy at Nyanya Park Sep 20, 2026 Importance of Financial Literacy NDIC Nigeria discusses the importance of financial literacy Sep 20, 2026 How are Financial Literacy and Financial Inclusion Connected? The crucial relationship between financial literacy and financial inclusion as advocated by the NDIC Sep 20, 2026 NDIC Focus Group-Episode 7 (Part Three) The importance of deposit insurance for traders in busy markets Sep 20, 2026 Common Misconceptions about Deposit Insurance Coverag NDIC Raises Awareness on Deposit Insurance Sep 20, 2026 NDIC's Consumer Protection Initiatives NDIC Explains Its Role in Protecting Depositors Sep 20, 2026 NDIC's Financial Literacy Campaigns (Kano International Trade-Fair) -Episode 8 NDIC Promotes Financial Literacy at Kano Trade Fair Sep 20, 2026 What Are the Major Challenges when A Bank Fails? NDIC Educates Public on Bank Failure Protection E Go Better SHORTS 1:08 Nov 22, 2025 E Go Better: Insure Your Deposit Quick tip on why insured deposits give you peace of mind. 0:58 Nov 08, 2025 E Go Better: Smart Saving Tips Three small habits that build long-term financial resilience. Oct 18, 2025 E Go Better: Protect Your PIN A short reminder on how to keep your card and online banking safe. 1:57 May 2014 E Go Better: Hausa 'E Go Better-The Microfinance Way' by the GIZ-SEDIN Programme is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. NDIC in the News 2:33 Mar 29, 2023 NDIC Re-enactment Bill Senate Passes NDIC Re-enactment Bill 2023 2:58 Feb 7, 2023 NDIC Reiterates Commitment To Financial Stability The Nigeria deposit insurance corporation has reiterated it's commitment towards strengthening the deposit insurance framework ensuring prompt and timely support of troubled insured financial institutions according to international best practices. 3:08 Nov 29, 2022 NDIC Reiterates Role In Boosting Depositors Confidence In Financial System The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation is advocating a more accurate and balanced reporting of the country\u2019s financial sector by the media. 3:13 May 5, 2022 NDIC, Lawmakers Synergise To Strengthen Financial System The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) says it has embarked on collaboration and cooperation with other deposit insurance agencies globally to address the challenges facing the financial industry. 2:56 Aug 10, 2022 NDIC, Other Agencies Partner To Tackle Banking Malpractices The Nigeria Deposit insurance Corporation has buttressed the need to enhance collaboration among relevant stakeholders so as to curb banking malpractices. 3:25 Jun 13, 2022 NDIC, Senate Strengthens Collaboration On Deposit Insurance The Managing Director and Chief Executive of the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, Mr. Bello Hassan says the banking sector is now immunized to withstand shocks that may impact the economy and the financial system. 3:02 Oct 21, 2021 NDIC Organises Capacity Building Workshop For Journalists The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, NDIC has organized a capacity building workshop for journalists to help improve on their delivery. No videos match your search. The NDIC Story in Motion See More", "content_hash": "52d2ef88acaf4e882aa266fbe1af75b92fab224b122b83aba4fe6ed4937a2f7a", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:52.968306+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1381", "title": "Vraylar for Depression and Other Disorders: Key Facts", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/vraylar", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/drugs/vraylar", "text": "Key takeaways Vraylar (cariprazine) is a prescription drug used to treat certain mental health conditions, such as depression and bipolar I disorder. Vraylar comes as a capsule that you swallow once daily. Depending on the condition you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re taking it to treat, your doctor may prescribe Vraylar alone or with another medication. Vraylar\u00e2\u0080\u0099s cost can depend on several factors, including the pharmacy you use, whether or not you have insurance, and whether you qualify for any savings programs. What is Vraylar?Vraylar (\u00e2\u0080\u009cVRAY-lar\u00e2\u0080\u009d) is a prescription drug used to treat certain mental health conditions. The active ingredient in Vraylar is cariprazine. It belongs to a group of drugs called atypical antipsychotics.It comes as an oral tablet that you swallow once per day.Vraylar is manufactured by Forest Laboratories Ireland Limited and is distributed by AbbVie, Inc.Vraylar genericVraylar is a brand-name medication. It is not currently available in a generic version.What is Vraylar used for?Vraylar is approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for use to treat the following conditions:depression (also called major depressive disorder or MDD) in adultsmanic or mixed episodes associated with bipolar I disorder in adults and children ages 10 years and olderbipolar depression (depressive episodes associated with bipolar I disorder) in adultsschizophrenia in adults and children ages 13 years and olderWhen used to treat depression, Vraylar is used as an add-on medicine for adults who are currently taking an antidepressant medication but still have unresolved depression symptoms. This is called adjunctive therapy.How does Vraylar work?Vraylar\u00e2\u0080\u0099s mechanism of action (how it works) isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t clear. The drug is thought to affect the activity of two brain chemicals, dopamine and serotonin. These brain chemicals are involved in regulating your mood, thoughts, and behaviors. By affecting dopamine and serotonin levels, Vraylar may help ease the symptoms of the conditions it treats.What is Vraylar\u00e2\u0080\u0099s dosage?Vraylar capsules come in six strengths:0.5 milligrams (mg)0.75 mg1.5 mg3 mg4.5 mg6 mgDoctors usually prescribe a low starting dose of Vraylar. Then, they may increase your dosage over time until they find the dosage that\u00e2\u0080\u0099s right for you on an ongoing basis (the maintenance dose).\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Dosage details for VraylarWhat are Vraylar\u00e2\u0080\u0099s side effects?Side effects of Vraylar can vary depending on the indication it is used for and other factors.In clinical trials of the drug, the most common adverse reactions (occurring in at least 5% of cases and at least twice the rate of a placebo treatment) of Vraylar for its FDA-approved indications were as follows:Adjunctive treatment of depressionThe most common Vraylar side effects included:akathisia (restlessness and an intense urge to move, mainly in your legs)fatigueconstipationnauseainsomniaincreased appetitedizzinessextrapyramidal symptoms, including involuntary or uncontrollable movementsBipolar maniaThe most common Vraylar side effects included:extrapyramidal symptomsrestlessnessdyspepsia (indigestion)vomitingsleepinessBipolar depressionThe most common side effects of Vraylar included:nausearestlessnessextrapyramidal symptomsSchizophreniaThe most common Vraylar side effects were extrapyramidal symptoms and restlessness.These lists don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t include all possible side effects of Vraylar.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Vraylar side effects and tips for managing themWhat does Vraylar cost?Whether you have health insurance or not, cost may be a factor when you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re considering Vraylar. What you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll pay for Vraylar may depend on several things, such as your treatment plan and the pharmacy you choose.Here are a few things to consider regarding Vraylar cost and savings:Comparing pharmacies: The price of Vraylar may vary depending on which pharmacy you use, so it can help to compare prices across pharmacies to find the lowest cost.Drug coupons: You may be able to find drug coupons on prescription discount websites that can reduce the cost of your medication. These coupons cannot be used with insurance copays or benefits, but the discounted price may be lower than what you would pay through insurance.Financial assistance: Some websites provide details about drug assistance programs, ways to make the most of your insurance coverage, and links to savings cards and other services. Two such websites are: Medicine Assistance ToolNeedyMedsAlso, AbbVie, the distributor of Vraylar, has a savings program you may be eligible for. See this webpage for details.\u00c2\u00bbMORE:Search for your medication on Optum Perks to see available coupons and download a free Optum Perks discount card.Optum Perks is owned by RVO Health. By clicking on this link, we may receive a commission. Learn more.Vraylar interactionsTaking a medication with certain vaccines, foods, and other things can affect how the medication works. These effects are called interactions.Before taking Vraylar, be sure to tell your doctor about all the medications you take, including prescription and over-the-counter types. Also describe any vitamins, herbs, or supplements you use. Your doctor or pharmacist can tell you about any interactions these items may cause with Vraylar.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Vraylar drug interactions, alcohol, and other considerationsWarnings and precautionsBoxed warningsVraylar has boxed warnings for the following risks:suicidal thoughts and behaviors in young adults (ages 24 years and younger) and childrendeath in older adults (ages 65 and older) with dementia-related psychosisA boxed warning is the most serious warning required by the FDA. It alerts doctors and patients to drug effects that may be dangerous.Discuss these risks with your doctor before starting treatment with Vraylar.Help is out thereIf you or someone you know is in crisis and considering suicide or self-harm, please seek support:Call or text the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline at 988 or chat at 988lifeline.org. Caring counselors are available to listen and provide free and confidential support 24/7.Text HOME to the Crisis Text Line at 741741 to connect with a volunteer crisis counselor for free and confidential support 24/7.Not in the United States? Find a helpline in your country with Befrienders Worldwide.Call 911 or your local emergency services number if you feel safe to do so.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re calling on behalf of someone else, stay with them until help arrives. You may remove weapons or substances that can cause harm if you can do so safely.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re not in the same household, stay on the phone with them until help arrives.Other warnings and precautionsVraylar may not be right for you if you have certain medical conditions or other factors that affect your health, including:diabetescholesterol problemsseizuresagesevere liver or kidney problemslow white blood cell levelsrisk factors for stroke or heart diseasehigh or low blood pressurealcohol consumptionprevious allergic reaction to Vraylar or any of its ingredientsThoroughly discuss your health history with your doctor before you start taking Vraylar.Pregnancy and breastfeedingIf you can become pregnant, are breastfeeding, or are using birth control, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to discuss with your doctor whether Vraylar is a safe choice for you.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:Vraylar, pregnancy, and breastfeedingFrequently asked questionsDoes stopping Vraylar cause withdrawal symptoms? Can you stop taking it \"cold turkey\"?No, stopping Vraylar shouldn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t cause withdrawal symptoms. This includes stopping treatment abruptly (\u00e2\u0080\u009ccold turkey\u00e2\u0080\u009d). The drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s effects take a while to wear off after your last dose.But stopping Vraylar treatment can cause the symptoms of your condition to return or worsen. Some people may need to receive care in the hospital if their symptoms become severe.For your safety, do not stop taking Vraylar on your own. Talk with your doctor before changing or stopping Vraylar (or any prescription medication).Does Vraylar interact with caffeine?No, Vraylar does not interact with caffeine.But caffeine does interact with lithium, a drug your doctor may prescribe along with Vraylar for bipolar I disorder. Caffeine can make lithium less effective than usual.Keep in mind that consuming a lot of caffeine when you have a mental health condition may cause or worsen certain symptoms. These can include anxiety, mania (high mood), and insomnia.If you have questions about consuming caffeine with Vraylar, talk with your doctor.Is Vraylar similar to alternative drugs, such as Rexulti and Seroquel?Yes. Vraylar, Rexulti, and Seroquel all are atypical antipsychotic medications and they have similar mechanisms of action.But each of these drugs has its own unique active ingredient and is used for different specific indications. For details, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Does Vraylar treat anxiety or borderline personality disorder?No, Vraylar is not used to treat anxiety disorders or borderline personality disorder. The FDA has not approved Vraylar for treating these conditions.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re looking for potential treatment options for anxiety or borderline personality disorder, talk with your doctor.Is Vraylar an SSRI?No, Vraylar is not a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI).SSRIs are antidepressants that are used to treat depression and anxiety disorders, among other uses. Vraylar is a kind of drug called an atypical antipsychotic.Vraylar does have some similar effects to an antidepressant and can be used to treat depression. But it does not work the same way that SSRIs do. For details, talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Is Vraylar a controlled substance?No, Vraylar is not a controlled substance.A controlled substance is a drug that has a high potential for being misused or causing dependence. Misuse refers to taking a drug in a way other than how your doctor prescribed it, such as taking too much of it. And being dependent on a drug means your body needs it to feel as you usually do.These risks do not apply to Vraylar.What should be done in case of overdose?Do not take more Vraylar than your doctor prescribes. Taking more than this may lead to serious side effects.Symptoms of overdoseSymptoms caused by an overdose can include:feeling very sleepyorthostatic hypotension (a drop in blood pressure upon standing or sitting up)What to do in case you take too much VraylarCall your doctor if you think you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve taken too much Vraylar. You can also call 800-222-1222 to reach America\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Poison Centers, or use its online resource. However, if you have severe symptoms, immediately call 911 or your local emergency number. Or go to the nearest emergency room.TakeawayVraylar (cariprazine) is a brand-name atypical antipsychotic medication primarily prescribed for adults to treat schizophrenia, manic or mixed episodes of bipolar I disorder, and bipolar depression, as well as major depressive disorder when used alongside antidepressants. Taken as a daily capsule, the drug is thought to work by modulating dopamine and serotonin levels in the brain to regulate mood and behavior. Common side effects of Vraylar include restlessness, nausea, and sleepiness. But it also has serious boxed warnings regarding an increased risk of death in older adults with dementia-related psychosis and a heightened risk of suicidal thoughts in children and young adults.This is a summary article for general educational purposes only. For more details about Vraylar, see the drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescribing information or talk with your doctor or pharmacist.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.Vraylar imagesVIEW GALLERY4", "content_hash": "4848ba6218cf64e7f600dc016df12f9170329a4b3fa1b75e5eb126edb90b42b7", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:17:55.201680+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1382", "title": "World Legal Materials from Europe", "url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/europe", "final_url": "https://law.cornell.edu/world/europe", "text": "Albania Andorra Austria Belarus Belgium Bosnia-Herzegovina Bulgaria Chechnya Croatia Cyprus Czech Republic Denmark Estonia Finland France Germany Greece Hungary Iceland Ireland Italy Latvia Liechtenstein Lithuania Luxembourg Macedonia Malta Moldova Netherlands Norway Poland Portugal Romania Russia Slovak Republic Slovenia Spain Sweden Switzerland Ukraine United Kingdom Serbia and Montenegro European Union Other Regional Institutions For further information see Cornell Law Library's \"Foreign and International Law Sources on the Internet\" Albania: Constitution | Other legal materials | President | Albanian Parliament | Banking Law | Labor Law | Law & Politics | Criminal Code | Criminal Procedure Code | Albanian legislation Andorra: Constitution | Government | General Council | Trademark Office Austria: Constitution | Federal Constitutional Law (PDF) | Constitutional Court (German) | Parliament (German) | Legal texts | Austria Govt. | IP Law (German) | Austrian Bar Association (German) | Arbitration Law | Austrian legislation Belarus: Constitution | Alternate copy | National Assembly | Collection of Laws (in English and Russian) | President | Ministries | Council of Minisiters | Constitutional Court | Supreme Economic Court | National Center of Legal Information | Parliament (Russian) | Belorussian legislation Belgium: Constitution | Alternate copy | Supreme Administrative Court | Cour de Cassation (French & Dutch) | Parliament | Federal Government | Legal Links | Legal Research Page (French) | Research Guide to Belgian Law | Arbitration Law | Belgian legislation Bosnia-Herzegovina: Constitution | Dayton Agreement | Republic of Srpska Bulgaria: Constitution | Alternate copy | Constitut